  ('793537462958880427', '“allez!”', 'Aleksandr I. Kuprin', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'Set against a circus or performance backdrop, the story captures courage, discipline, and the human cost behind spectacle. It reflects on endurance and the demands placed on performers. Translated from Russian by Douglas Ashby Originally published 1889', 'https://archive.org/services/img/aleksandr-i.-kuprin-allez-1889-final', 'https://archive.org/details/aleksandr-i.-kuprin-allez-1889-final', 'internet-archive:aleksandr-i.-kuprin-allez-1889-final'),
  ('784910095789168082', '"Bison Medicine"', 'Brandon Peele', 2025, 'History', 'If you enjoy this book, please make a donation to American Prairie , a great organization that partners with First Nations to acquire and protect the habitat of the bison. ... Now is not the time for politics or activism as usual. Now is not the time for raging online, or escaping to screens or foreign lands. You are needed here and now. Your gifts are needed and we have much work to do. We are a nation that does big things. We are the nation of the Constitution, NASA, and the Internet. We defeated the Confederacy and the Third Reich. We defeated hate before and we will defeat it again. But first we have to scope the problem. The nature of our problems are not political, technological, or material - we already have every resource, tool, and policy we need to be free and flourish. Rather, our problems are moral, cultural, spiritual, and psychological and we have to work the problem on these levels. Only then can we be free, flourish, remake society, and finally give hate no quarter on this soil. Bison Medicine jumpstarts this moral, cultural, spiritual, and psychological transformation. The book explores three key ideas: 1. We have a sacred 3-part national purpose to fulfill (A. All Created Equal, B. Life, Liberty, and the Pursuit of Happiness, and C. E Pluribus Unum ). 2. In 2016, we summoned the majestic bison, and consecrated it as our National Mammal. In this dark hour, it offers us guidance to fulfill our nation’s purpose. 3. By activating your unique personal purpose in your organization and community, you can unleash your gifts, lead a team, and fulfill our nation’s purpose right here and now. Right here, where you live and work. "A monumental work of art... a tribute to an enlightened experiment..." Jon Robison, PhD "A prophetic call for ...the bison''s individual and collective power..." Luis Marrero, PhD, CEO, Boston Institute for Meaningful Purpose "...brilliantly conceived, extensively researched, and passionately presented." Reggie Marra, Author, Healing America''s Narratives " a renewed sense of civic purpose.” - Dr. Joel Domingo, Research Director, City University of Seattle “The gift of Bison Medicine can be summed up in one word—restorative. So, if like many of us, you’ve felt concerned that America’s promise might be a bygone hope, be encouraged that even in a time such as this, there are still those who take up the call to offer good medicine. With Bison Medicine , Brandon Peele has offered a vision that any American can locate themselves in" - Pedro Silva, Director of Engagement, YOUnify', 'https://archive.org/services/img/bison-medicine-revised-10-feb', 'https://archive.org/details/bison-medicine-revised-10-feb', 'internet-archive:bison-medicine-revised-10-feb'),
