  ('354505837473683853', '[Core Document] – History of Amigos Internacionales (1967–Present)', 'Amigos Internacionales', 2026, 'History', 'Part of the Amigos Internacionales Archive Collection. CATEGORY: Core Organizational Documents This document provides an archival historical summary of Amigos Internacionales, a U.S.-based nonprofit humanitarian organization founded in 1967. Compiled from organizational records, historical materials, program documentation, and publicly available sources, this document outlines the development, geographic expansion, and program evolution of the organization over multiple decades. Amigos Internacionales began with early humanitarian and medical outreach efforts and has since grown into a multi-faceted international nonprofit operating primarily in East Africa, with initiatives focused on clean water access, education, medical missions, and community-based development. Central to its long-term strategy is the MissionPoint model—a holistic approach to sustainable community transformation integrating infrastructure, healthcare, education, and local leadership development. This archival record is intended to provide a structured and verifiable overview of the organization’s historical foundation, operational growth, and ongoing impact from 1967 to the present. RELATED DOCUMENTS: History of Amigos Internacionales (1967–Present) https://archive.org/details/history-of-amigos-internacionales-1967-present MissionPoint Model Explained – Amigos Internacionales https://archive.org/details/mission-point-model-explained 2025 Medical Impact & Outcomes Report – Amigos Internacionales https://archive.org/details/2025-medical-impact-outcomes-report-amigos-internacionales Amigos Internacionales and U.S. Food Assistance Programs: A Historical and Programmatic Linkage Summary https://archive.org/details/amigos-food-assistance-linkage-summary Agreement Between the Government of British Honduras (Belize) and Amigos Internacionales (1970) https://archive.org/details/amigos-belize-government-agreement-1970 Texas Academy of Family Physicians (AAFP) Journal – Amigos Internacionales Medical Missions in British Honduras (1971) https://archive.org/details/1971-gp-press-amigos-internacionales_202604 Official website: https://www.amigosii.org', 'https://archive.org/services/img/history-of-amigos-internacionales-1967-present', 'https://archive.org/details/history-of-amigos-internacionales-1967-present', 'internet-archive:history-of-amigos-internacionales-1967-present'),
