  ('1077432274327499763', 'A Christmas Carol In Prose. Being a Ghost Story of Christmas', 'Dickens, Charles', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A Christmas Carol investigates moral development, civic obligations, and human compassion within the framework of Victorian England. Dickens uses Ebenezer Scrooge''s spectral experiences to link individual metamorphosis with a broader societal understanding, demonstrating the negative consequences of avarice and apathy. It stands out as a key moral tale because it promotes empathy, compassion, and shared accountability, combining sentiment with social critique and ethical imperative. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/a_christmas_carol_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/a_christmas_carol_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:a_christmas_carol_charles_dickens_zebabooks'),
