  ('845182699160852114', 'A geometric horror novella about a world that bends at the edges', 'A. slice', 2026, '• Horror fiction • Psychological horror • Geometric horror • Liminal spaces • Reality distortion • Atmospheric fiction • Surreal fiction • Independent fiction • Novella • A. Slice', 'Carl’s world begins to slip out of alignment—first in a quiet underpass, then in his dreams, and finally inside his own home. Shadows bend where they shouldn’t, corridors stretch by fractions, and reality seems to correct itself when he looks directly at it. As the distortions grow more deliberate, Carl realises something is watching him from the edges of geometry itself. A slow‑burn, atmospheric horror about perception, misalignment, and the spaces that notice us back.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-shadows-bend-story', 'https://archive.org/details/the-shadows-bend-story', 'internet-archive:the-shadows-bend-story'),
