  ('12197666475664466', 'A history of the organization, development and services of the military and naval forces of Canada from the Peace of Paris in 1763, to the present time', 'Unknown', 2025, 'History', 'Vol. 1. The local forces of New France; The Militia of the Province of Quebec, 1763-1775. -- v. 2. The war of the American Revolution: The province of Quebec under the administration of Governor Sir Guy Carleton, 1775-1778. -- v. 3. The war of the American Revolution; The province of Quebec under the administration of Governor Frederic Haldimand, 1778-1784', 'https://archive.org/services/img/vol1t3historyoforganiz01quebuoft', 'https://archive.org/details/vol1t3historyoforganiz01quebuoft', 'internet-archive:vol1t3historyoforganiz01quebuoft'),
  ('908007585340663677', 'A History Of The Personal Computer', 'Roy A. Allan', 2001, 'History', 'This book is an exciting history of the personal computer revolution. Early personal computing, the "first" personal computer, invention of the microprocessor at Intel and the first microcomputer are detailed. It also traces the evolution of the personal computer from the hardware and software hacker, to its use as a consumer appliance on the Internet. This is the only book that provides such comprehensive coverage. It not only describes the hardware and software, but also the companies and people who made it happen. The paperback edition of the book (ISBN 0-9689108-0-7) can be purchased at amazon.com', 'https://archive.org/services/img/historyofPC', 'https://archive.org/details/historyofPC', 'internet-archive:historyofPC'),
