  ('118764052348921515', 'A Legend', 'Aleksandr I. Kuprin', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A reflective tale built around a moral or symbolic narrative, exploring themes of faith, human weakness, and redemption. Kuprin blends realism with a parable-like tone to question spiritual values. Translated from Russian by Leo Pasvolsky Originally published 1905', 'https://archive.org/services/img/aleksandr-i.-kuprin-a-legend-1905-final', 'https://archive.org/details/aleksandr-i.-kuprin-a-legend-1905-final', 'internet-archive:aleksandr-i.-kuprin-a-legend-1905-final'),
  ('593924055268598737', 'A Lesson In Sancocho Warmth Thanos Kalamidas', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'eBook', 'The Rolling Recipes are more than instructions; they are passports. Each dish carries the aroma of distant markets, the whispers of family kitchens and the indelible stories of culture, memory and the place that created it. Sancocho, Panama''s beloved national stew, is a hearty and aromatic chicken soup brimming with rustic flavors. Its defining ingredients are tender corn on the cob and chunks of starchy ñame root. All that with a Mediterranean soft touch and a small story. "Señora Alma clicked her tongue, a sound of both sympathy and mild disapproval. "You''re hollow," she declared, not unkindly. "You need a sancocho. Not the café version. A real one." The word meant nothing to me then. She saw the blank look and simply nodded. "Tomorrow. You will help me. You will learn."', 'https://archive.org/services/img/a-lesson-in-sancocho-warmth-thanos-kalamidas', 'https://archive.org/details/a-lesson-in-sancocho-warmth-thanos-kalamidas', 'internet-archive:a-lesson-in-sancocho-warmth-thanos-kalamidas'),
