  ('801692334205329598', 'A May Night', 'Nikolai Gogol', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A young Cossack, Levko, seeks to marry his beloved despite his father’s opposition. A supernatural encounter with a drowned maiden helps him uncover a hidden truth, ultimately securing his happiness. The story blends Ukrainian folklore with romance and gentle satire. Translated from Russian by Claud Field Published in 1831', 'https://archive.org/services/img/nikolai-gogol-a-may-night-1831', 'https://archive.org/details/nikolai-gogol-a-may-night-1831', 'internet-archive:nikolai-gogol-a-may-night-1831'),
