  ('55263542602274818', 'A Tale of a Tub', 'Swift, Jonathan', 2026, 'Literature', 'A Tale of a Tub is a biting satire that targets religious excess, intellectual vanity, and cultural pretension through sharp irony and deliberate disorder. Using the allegory of three brothers and an unreliable narrator, Swift mocks sectarian division, pedantry, and self-delusion, exposing humanity’s preference for comforting illusions over difficult truths. A work of relentless wit and moral severity, it remains one of the sharpest critiques of false authority in English satire. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/a_tale_of_a_tub_jonathan_swift_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/a_tale_of_a_tub_jonathan_swift_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:a_tale_of_a_tub_jonathan_swift_zebabooks'),
