  ('1050015527243714406', 'Against Smoothness', 'Birgitta Welzel', 2026, 'Literature', 'This collection of essays by Birgitta Welzel presents a pioneering competency model for creative writing with Large Language Models, framing the author as a "strategic curator" who overcomes the statistical "smoothness" of AI-generated text. Through fictional workshop conversations with figures such as Erich Auerbach, Umberto Eco, and Italo Calvino, the work establishes a theoretical bridge between technological application and the high aesthetic standards of the literary tradition. It defines the essential curatorial skills required to transform machine-generated raw material into literature characterized by aesthetic necessity and intellectual resistance.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/against-smoothness', 'https://archive.org/details/against-smoothness', 'internet-archive:against-smoothness'),
