  ('264446892111553213', 'Al Mustadrak Imam Hakim -Urdu Translation', 'Unknown', 2010, 'Literature', 'Al-Mustadrak ala aṣ-Ṣaḥeeḥayn ( Arabic : المستدرك على الصحيحين ‎) or Mustadrak Al Hakim ( Arabic : مستدرك الحاكم ‎) is a five volume hadith collection written by Hakim al-Nishapuri (Nishapur is located in Iran). He wrote it in the year 393 AH (1002–1003 CE), when he was 72 years old. It contains 9045 hadith. He claimed all hadith in it were authentic according to the conditions of either Sahih al-Bukhari or Sahih Muslim or both. The statement of authenticity was not accepted by a number of prominent later Sunni scholars. Al-Dhahabi , a 14th century Sunni Shafi''i Islamic scholar made an abridged version of the collection named Talkhis al-Mustadrak where he commented on its authenticity. It has become the habit of scholars today working in the field of hadîth, when compiling them and determining their authenticity, to say things like "It is authenticated by al-Hâkim and al-Dhahabî concurs". In doing so, they are referring to al-Dhahabi''s Talkhîs, his abridgement of the Mustadrak that is often published along with it in its margins. Dhahabi also wrote: The Mustadrak contains a good number of hadîth that conform to the conditions of authenticity of both (al-Bukhârî and Muslim) as well as a number of hadîth conforming to the conditions of either one of them. Perhaps the total number of such hadîth comprises half the book. There is roughly another quarter of the hadîth that have authentic chains of transmission, but that have something else about them or that have some defect. As for the rest, and that is about a fourth, they are rejected and spurious narrations that are unauthentic. Some of those are fabrications. I came to know of them when I prepared an abridgement of the Mustadrak and pointed them out.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/almustadrakimamhakimurdutranslationvolume6al-mustadrakalaas-saheehaynarabicormus', 'https://archive.org/details/almustadrakimamhakimurdutranslationvolume6al-mustadrakalaas-saheehaynarabicormus', 'internet-archive:almustadrakimamhakimurdutranslationvolume6al-mustadrakalaas-saheehaynarabicormus'),
  ('587016400512861256', 'Al Qaeda Now', 'Karen Joy Greenberg', 2005, 'Politics', 'Al Qaeda Now by Karen Joy Greenberg. A politics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8326127W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL8326127W-'),
  ('188861241553703764', 'Al Quds: The City of Jerusalem | Chronicles of Bani Israel | Promo', 'Mohammad Zahid Mateen', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A land shaped by revelation. A nation tested by trials. A history that changed the course of the world. This book offers a journey like no other. It traces the story of Banī Isrāʾīl and the blessed city of al-Quds from the time of Prophet Ibrāhīm عليه السلام to the defining upheavals of 1948. For the first time, the narratives of the Prophets, the rise and fall of empires, the Crusades, and the enduring struggle for Jerusalem are woven into a single, coherent account. It provides the reader with a clear and comprehensive understanding of a history that has shaped faith, civilisation, and the Ummah. Grounded in the Qurʾān, authentic aḥādīth, early Muslim scholarship, and rigorously verified historical sources, this work goes beyond narration. It extracts meaning. It brings forward enduring lessons on obedience and defiance, justice and oppression, faith and resilience, mercy and accountability. It connects past to present, enabling the reader to understand not only what happened, but why it happened, and why it continues to matter. Written with sincerity and deep reverence, this is not merely a book to be read. It is a call to reflection. It invites the reader to engage with history as a living guide, a mirror for one’s faith, a warning against error, and a source of strength in the pursuit of truth and justice. From the footsteps of the Prophets to the struggles of our time, this work equips the reader to understand, to connect, and to act. It calls you to move beyond passive reading and to allow history to inform your worldview, shape your convictions, and guide your response to the challenges of today. We ask Allah to accept this humble effort for His sake alone. We ask Him to unite us with our Prophet ﷺ at al-Kawthar and to protect us from being among those about whom the Prophet ﷺ said that Allah may support this religion through a wicked person. JazākumAllāhu Khayran to Shaykh Dr Furhān Zubairī, Shaykh Dr ʿUmar Sulaymān, Shaykh Ṭāriq Appleby, Shaykh Wisnu Tanggap Prabowo, Shaykh Shuʿayb Wānī, and Shaykh Sajjād Mīr for their guidance, review, and invaluable counsel.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/al-quds-promo', 'https://archive.org/details/al-quds-promo', 'internet-archive:al-quds-promo'),
  ('761921026261291149', 'Al Sira Al Nabawiyya Vol 1', 'Ibn Kathir', 2019, 'Biography', 'Al-Sira al Nabawiyya by Imam IBN KATHIR is a full examination, in chronological order of the background, life and the mission of the Prophet Muhammad (saw). Drawn from the earliest and most reliable Arabic sources, it offers, in this close English translation, the Fullest available account of the historical circumstances and personalities most important in the foundation of Islam. IBN KATHIR''s work offers a fine example of the Islamic scholarship; the quotations and anecdotes that constitute its core are evaluated in terms of trustworthiness of the sources. Variant wordings that are related through differing lines of transmission are noted, and Ibn Kathir gives both his own assessments and those of the earliest Islamic authorities concerning the likely authenticity of these records. The comments and conversations, derived from ancient texts, that are quoted in this work constitute the basis of our knowledge of Islam during the life time Muhammad (saw)', 'https://archive.org/services/img/AlSiraAlNabawiyyaVol1', 'https://archive.org/details/AlSiraAlNabawiyyaVol1', 'internet-archive:AlSiraAlNabawiyyaVol1'),
  ('908311991074112032', 'Al-Qaeda', 'Jason Burke', 2003, 'Politics', 'Al-Qaeda by Jason Burke. A politics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6048782W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL6048782W-'),
