  ('767992852708997264', 'Alice Lonnon Perkins Hill of Palomar Mountain', 'Peter Brueggeman', 2026, 'History', 'Alice Lonnon Perkins, a retired theatrical actress whose stage name was Alice Lonnon, came to Palomar Mountain after she married Harry Elwood Hill in 1917. They built a house on high land above Lower Doane Valley on the east. Alice Hill was well known locally, hosting friends and family near and far. Palomar''s Robert Asher was a good friend and wrote considerably about her. The Hills divorced and she continued living on Palomar Mountain for many years, finally moving off mountain in 1951.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/hill_20251010', 'https://archive.org/details/hill_20251010', 'internet-archive:hill_20251010'),
