  ('580370372859325983', 'Amplified Evil, How Hitler And Codreanu Deployed Ancient Elite Mechanisms Through Modern Technology', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This comparative case study examines Adolf Hitler in Nazi Germany (1933-1945) and Corneliu Zelea Codreanu''s Legion of the Archangel Michael in Romania (1927-1938), analyzing how both deployed ancient elite power mechanisms amplified through twentieth-century technology. The study demonstrates that Hitler''s success and Codreanu''s failure hinged on elite coordination strategies rather than ideological differences, with Hitler successfully manipulating conservative elites while Codreanu threatened them and was assassinated. Through comparison with Alexander the Great, Julius Caesar, and Napoleon Bonaparte, the analysis reveals systematic historical patterns of continental conquest and challenges the "Hitler was crazy" narrative as an elite construct obscuring persistent power mechanisms. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/amplified-evil-how-hitler-and-codreanu-deployed-ancient-elite-mechanisms-through-modern-technology', 'https://archive.org/details/amplified-evil-how-hitler-and-codreanu-deployed-ancient-elite-mechanisms-through-modern-technology', 'internet-archive:amplified-evil-how-hitler-and-codreanu-deployed-ancient-elite-mechanisms-through-modern-technology'),
