  ('1125389513724595546', 'Ancient Cities: The Archaeology of Urban Life In The Ancient Near East And Egypt, Greece And Rome', 'Unknown', 2011, 'Classic Literature', 'Editorial Reviews About the Author Charles Gates is senior lecturer of archaeology and art history at Bilkent University in Ankara, Turkey. His research focuses on Minoan, Mycenaean and Greek art and archaeology. Since 1993 he has participated in the excavations at Kinet Höyük (Turkey), a Bronze and Iron Age port city in the north-east Mediterrean. Publisher : Routledge; 2nd edition (March 17, 2011) Language: : English Paperback : 504 pages ISBN-10 : 0415498643 ISBN-13 : 978-0415498647 Item Weight : 1.83 pounds Dimensions : 6.85 x 1.14 x 9.69 inches', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ancient-cities-the-archaeology-of-urban-life-in-the-ancient-near-east-and-egypt-', 'https://archive.org/details/ancient-cities-the-archaeology-of-urban-life-in-the-ancient-near-east-and-egypt-', 'internet-archive:ancient-cities-the-archaeology-of-urban-life-in-the-ancient-near-east-and-egypt-'),
  ('635423683384571061', 'Ancient Greek Philosophy Revisited (From the Presocratics to Plato’s Academy) in Dialogue with Neutrosophy and Plithogeny (Logical Extensions of Classical Dialectics)', 'Florentin Smarandache', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'This book reexamines early Greek philosophy through the conceptual framework of neutrosophy and plithogenic theory. Covering thinkers from the Presocratics to the early Platonic Academy, it investigates how ancient philosophers addressed problems involving indeterminacy, contradiction, mixture, and plurality. The study analyzes the doctrines of figures such as Anaximander, Pythagoras, Heraclitus, Parmenides, Zeno, Empedocles, Anaxagoras, Democritus, Protagoras, Socrates, Archytas, Eudoxus, Theaetetus, Speusippus, and Xenocrates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ancient-greek-philosophy-revisited', 'https://archive.org/details/ancient-greek-philosophy-revisited', 'internet-archive:ancient-greek-philosophy-revisited'),
