  ('530120375243626484', 'Angus Robertson Memories', 'Richard Wakefield', 2026, 'History', 'Description: A first-hand account of Sydney’s iconic Angus & Robertson bookstore at 89 Castlereagh Street from 1960 to 1972, by staff member Richard Wakefield. This memoir recalls daily operations, unique roles like the remainders and buy-in boys, the bustling counters, legendary annual book sales, and memorable colleagues including Hedley Jefferies. It offers rare insights into the people, culture, and literary life of A&R’s final years at Castlereagh before the move to Pitt Street and the 1975 fire. An essential record of mid-20th-century Australian bookselling history.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/angus-robertson-memories', 'https://archive.org/details/angus-robertson-memories', 'internet-archive:angus-robertson-memories'),
