  ('15789447103090588', 'As I Have Loved You Michael Lujan', 'Michael Lujan', 2026, 'History', 'As I Have Loved You is a historical narrative about the most radical claim Jesus made about his followers: that the world would recognize them by love. Tracing the commandment through early Christianity and beyond, the book explores how faith is shaped—sometimes refined, sometimes distorted—by war, power, fear, and exile. From moments of spiritual beauty to episodes of terrifying betrayal, it asks a steady question: What happens when love stops being the badge of discipleship? Blending accessible scholarship with immersive storytelling, As I Have Loved You offers history with a heartbeat—careful with facts, rich with human detail, and written for readers who want more than a textbook without drifting into historical fiction.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/as-i-have-loved-you-michael-lujan', 'https://archive.org/details/as-i-have-loved-you-michael-lujan', 'internet-archive:as-i-have-loved-you-michael-lujan'),
