  ('745502265890864513', 'Awkward', 'Chmakova, Svetlana, 1979- author, illustrator', 2015, 'Middle schools', 'After shunning Jaime, the school nerd, on her first day at a new middle school, Penelope Torres tries to blend in with her new friends in the art club, until the art club goes to war with the science club, of which Jaime is a member', 'https://archive.org/services/img/awkward0000chma', 'https://archive.org/details/awkward0000chma', 'internet-archive:awkward0000chma'),
  ('1078411477854041177', 'Awoken Love Of Poetry', 'Hamid Ali', 2026, 'Literature', 'This poetry collection is a journey through grief, guilt, memory, loneliness, and self-realization in the modern world. The poems move between deeply personal emotions and symbolic reflections on society. The opening pieces center on the loss of a mother, portraying her as a source of forgiveness, purity, and unconditional love. The speaker expresses regret, spiritual emptiness, and a longing for redemption, presenting motherhood as a sacred shelter now absent. Symbolism plays a strong role throughout the collection. In The White Tree, the jungle and transforming tree represent inner struggle, confrontation with despair, and spiritual awakening. Ordinary objects in The Old Curtain and The Old Socks are personified, giving voice to neglected things to mirror human neglect, endurance, and silent loyalty. These poems suggest that even the unnoticed carries meaning and memory. Themes of betrayal and self-reflection appear in Jealous Friend, where friendship becomes a metaphor for trust broken and lessons learned. In Sleeping Strangers and A Barking Dog, dream and darkness blur reality, revealing fears, subconscious anxieties, and social isolation. The tone shifts between surreal imagery and stark warnings. Modern societal critique emerges in Reels Cycle, which questions digital addiction and the loss of productivity and authentic human connection. The poem reflects frustration with distraction, wasted potential, and self-destructive habits. Meanwhile, Pain I Bore and Yes and Up explore ambition, mental strain, societal pressure, and the chaotic pursuit of success in a competitive world. Overall, the collection blends innocence with existential questioning. It explores the tension between purity and corruption, tradition and modernity, attachment and detachment. Through simple yet symbolic language, the poems capture a restless soul searching for meaning, forgiveness, discipline, and light in a fragmented contemporary world.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/awoken-love-of-poetry', 'https://archive.org/details/awoken-love-of-poetry', 'internet-archive:awoken-love-of-poetry'),
  ('657231248093213622', 'AWOL', 'Kathy Roth-Douquet, Frank Schaeffer, Roth-Douquet, Kathy, Schaeffer, Frank', 2006, 'Politics', 'AWOL by Kathy Roth-Douquet, Frank Schaeffer, Roth-Douquet, Kathy, Schaeffer, Frank. A politics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5852642W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL5852642W-'),
