  ('660789744921398437', 'Before The Great Flood – A Comparative Eschatological Study', 'Advocate Muhammad Yasir', 2025, 'Literature', 'This research-based study explores the mysteries surrounding the pre-flood world and its connection to the end times. Drawing upon Islamic, Christian, and Jewish sources including the Qur''an, Hadith, Bible, and Book of Enoch, this comparative eschatological study examines figures such as the Nephilim, Gog and Magog (Yajuj and Majuj), fallen angels, and ancient civilizations. Key themes include: • The identity and role of Azazel and his parallels with the Dajjal • Evidence of ancient giants, long-living prophets, and lost technologies • The survival of hybrid beings and their relevance to end-time prophecies • How eschatology connects with historical narratives and sacred texts This book presents a bold theory supported by scripture, historical references, and theological insights. It aims to spark deeper inquiry and reflection about humanity''s ancient past and its prophetic future.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/before-the-great-flood-a-comparative-eschatological-study', 'https://archive.org/details/before-the-great-flood-a-comparative-eschatological-study', 'internet-archive:before-the-great-flood-a-comparative-eschatological-study'),
