  ('156673869334443902', 'Bibliotheca Thomistica', 'SolitaryMan133', 2026, 'History', 'Having noticed that the work of the Doctor Angelicus in the website of the University of Navarra was at the mercy of an outdated system, I decided to compile everything into one coherent work so that those who seek the logical coherence, meekness, and the supernatural capacity of the 13th- century monk of Roccasecca could now have access to it. In this volume, I have compiled all the works that were absent from the first volume. This volume contains: The Thomae Lexikon (Ludwig Schütz): A massive, 1,000+ page dictionary defining Thomas''s specific usage of Latin and Greek philosophical terminology. The Fontes Vitae (Contemporary Biographies): The primary historical accounts of St. Thomas’s life, including the Ystoria by William of Tocco , the Vita by Bernard Gui , and the official Acts of Canonization . The Catalogus Thomisticum: A critical index of all genuine and attributed works, providing the structural backbone for Thomistic research. Bibliographia Thomistica: A comprehensive 20th-century bibliography of global scholarship concerning the life and thought of the Angelic Doctor. Auctores Alii & Officium: Supplemental works by contemporaries and the liturgical texts for the Office of Corpus Christi. "Digitized using XeLaTeX and the FreeSerif typeface to ensure full Unicode support for Ancient Greek and Latin cross-references."', 'https://archive.org/services/img/bibliotheca-thomistica-final-archive', 'https://archive.org/details/bibliotheca-thomistica-final-archive', 'internet-archive:bibliotheca-thomistica-final-archive'),
