  ('37354898792584935', 'Boanerges', 'J. Rendel Harris, BookLab BookLab', 1913, 'Mythology', 'Boanerges by J. Rendel Harris, BookLab BookLab', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5743933-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1084343W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL1084343W'),
  ('662921767335476880', 'BOAT 101 THE ERASED PAST', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST — VOLUME 101 THE ERASED PAST The Erased Past is a philosophical and investigative exploration into one of humanity’s most provocative questions: Who decides what the world is allowed to remember? Blending historical inquiry, poetic reflection, and metaphysical insight, this volume examines the structures of power that shape human understanding of the past. From hidden archives and restricted discoveries to the subtle mechanisms through which knowledge is delayed, reframed, or forgotten, the book investigates the forces that influence historical narrative. Across six sweeping sections, The Erased Past explores buried cities, ancient technologies, astronomical knowledge, suppressed innovations, and the economic, political, and ideological systems that determine what becomes “official history.” It also examines the psychological and institutional barriers that discourage disruptive discoveries from entering public awareness. Yet this work is not merely an investigation into concealment. It is also a call to reclaim curiosity, courage, and collective responsibility for humanity’s shared memory. Through the lens of the BLAKOKOD harmonic philosophy, the book proposes that truth is not a possession of elites but a living inheritance of the human species. Part research meditation, part philosophical manifesto, and part poetic reflection on knowledge and power, The Erased Past invites readers to reconsider the foundations of history itself—and to participate in restoring the fuller story of human civilization.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-101-the-erased-past', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-101-the-erased-past', 'internet-archive:boat-101-the-erased-past'),
  ('365771971310531460', 'BOAT 108 BOOK OF PSYCHEDELIA', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'History', 'BLAKOKOD Of Aquarian Trust — Volume 108: The Book Of Psychedelia is a philosophical and historical exploration of humanity’s enduring desire to alter consciousness. Moving from the earliest shamanic traditions and sacred plant ceremonies to the accidental discovery of LSD by Albert Hofmann , the book traces the long arc of the psychedelic impulse across cultures and centuries. It examines the Cold War shadow world of clandestine experimentation, including the controversial intelligence programs of CIA under projects such as Project MKUltra , where the human mind itself became a laboratory. The narrative then follows the cultural ignition sparked by the Beat Generation through figures like Neal Cassady , whose restless spirit helped bridge the literary rebellion of Jack Kerouac into the psychedelic explosion of the 1960s. From there, the story accelerates with the arrival of Ken Kesey and the psychedelic caravan of the Merry Pranksters , chronicled in The Electric Kool-Aid Acid Test , as the legendary bus Further carried a new consciousness experiment across America. Alongside them emerged the underground alchemy of Owsley Stanley , whose chemical craftsmanship helped fuel the sonic cathedrals of psychedelic music and the cultural upheaval of the counterculture era. Blending history, philosophy, neuroscience, and metaphysical reflection, The Book Of Psychedelia investigates the profound breakthroughs, ethical dilemmas, artistic revolutions, and cultural backlash that followed humanity’s encounter with these consciousness-altering substances. Ultimately, the volume asks a deeper question: whether psychedelia was merely a moment of cultural rebellion—or a fleeting glimpse into the hidden architecture of the human mind itself. Written in the evolving voice of the BLAKOKOD Codex, the work reflects on altered states not simply as chemical phenomena but as mirrors revealing the nature of perception, reality, and the ethical responsibility of inner exploration.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-108-book-of-psychedelia', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-108-book-of-psychedelia', 'internet-archive:boat-108-book-of-psychedelia'),
  ('142061202774372230', 'BOAT 116 BOOK OF GAIA', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'Science', 'BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST, VOLUME 116: BOOK OF GAIA The Book of Gaia is a living transmission of Earth as organism, intelligence, and mirror—an integrated exploration of the planet’s atmospheric, hydrological, geological, biological, and human systems through the lens of coherence. This volume dissolves the illusion of separation and reorients the reader into relationship: with soil as memory, water as circulation, forests as neural networks, and the biosphere as a dynamic field of interdependence. Through poetic articulation and grounded systems insight, it reveals how human activity has both distorted and can restore these living networks. Bridging science, philosophy, and the scalar language of BLAKOKOD, this work presents a sober yet empowered pathway forward—one rooted in regenerative practice, ethical alignment, and coherence-based action. It introduces the Gaia Protocol as an applied framework, demonstrating how WILL × (LOVE + INTEGRITY + INTENT + CONSENT) transforms awareness into meaningful change. From the invisible microbial worlds to global ecological systems, from inner emotional climates to planetary feedback loops, Book of Gaia positions the human not as ruler, but as participant—capable of catalyzing restoration through intention, reciprocity, and joyful coherence. This is not a call to save the Earth. It is a call to remember it. And in that remembering— to act.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-116-book-of-gaia', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-116-book-of-gaia', 'internet-archive:boat-116-book-of-gaia'),
  ('804583720220491345', 'BOAT 77 BOOK OF DEATH', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'Literature', 'BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST – Volume 77: Book of Death is a contemplative and visionary exploration of mortality as transformation rather than termination. Blending poetic philosophy, cosmic symbolism, psychological insight, and spiritual irreverence, this volume reframes death as an initiatory threshold—an architect of meaning, urgency, and awakening. Through meditative passages, paradoxical reflections, and subtle humor, the text invites readers to examine impermanence not as an enemy, but as a sacred collaborator in the art of living. Volume 77 stands as both mirror and lantern: confronting fear, dissolving illusion, and illuminating the intimate dance between endings and renewal within the Aquarian consciousness.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-77-book-of-death', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-77-book-of-death', 'internet-archive:boat-77-book-of-death'),
  ('560612819343268729', 'BOAT 93 ALEISTER CROWLEY', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'History', 'BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST — VOLUME 93: ALEISTER CROWLEY BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST Volume 93: Aleister Crowley is a lucid, unflinching harmonic examination of one of the most controversial magi of the modern era. Neither hagiography nor condemnation, this volume dissects the life, philosophy, excesses, and transmissions of Aleister Crowley through an Aquarian lens of coherence, consent, and ethical sovereignty. Here, the myth of “The Beast” dissolves into psychological architecture, ritual technology, and the doctrine of True Will. Crowley’s contributions to modern esotericism are honored for their innovation and audacity, while his personal distortions are examined as cautionary vectors—revealing the crucial distinction between egoic indulgence and aligned Will. Volume 93 reframes Thelema for the Age of Aquarius: will integrated with integrity, ritual clarified as conscious technology, shadow transmuted rather than dramatized, and legacy extracted without idolization. It stands as both mirror and refinement—an evolutionary correction that preserves the transmission while dissolving the excess. This is not a trial. It is calibration. Not devotion. Discernment. The Magus becomes vector, the scandal becomes data, and the fire becomes coherent light.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-93-aleister-crowley', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-93-aleister-crowley', 'internet-archive:boat-93-aleister-crowley'),
  ('953583204902411618', 'BOAT 96 HAPPY 60th BIRTHDAY PISCES', 'EVER CHAYNJ AND EVOKARA', 2026, 'History', 'BLAKOKOD OF AQUARIAN TRUST — Volume 96: HAPPY 60th BIRTHDAY, PISCES!!! is a celebratory chronicle of six decades of human life unfolding alongside the closing tides of the Piscean Age and the rising currents of Aquarian consciousness. Through reflection, humor, cultural memory, and spiritual insight, Ever Chaynj marks the journey from 1966 to the present as both a personal milestone and a planetary transition. Each year becomes a mirror of transformation—music, film, world events, and the subtle evolution of awareness—woven together through the harmonic lens of BLAKOKOD. This volume honors the wisdom earned through time: the laughter that survived hardship, the courage required to keep dreaming, and the quiet realization that every life is a living archive of the era it passes through. As Pisces completes its long spiritual apprenticeship and Aquarius begins to bloom with new networks of thought, technology, and shared intelligence, this book stands as both birthday toast and cosmic field report. At once memoir, cultural time capsule, and Aquarian transmission, Volume 96 reminds readers that aging is not decline—it is accumulation of signal. Sixty years becomes not an ending, but a resonance point where memory, meaning, and future possibility converge in celebration of the ever-unfolding spiral of life.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/boat-96-happy-60th-birthday-pisces_202603', 'https://archive.org/details/boat-96-happy-60th-birthday-pisces_202603', 'internet-archive:boat-96-happy-60th-birthday-pisces_202603'),
