  ('758741131430567273', 'Byzantine Monastic Foundation Documents: A Complete Translation of the Surviving Founders’ Typika and Testaments', 'Thomas, John Philip, Hero, Angela Constantinides', 2000, 'History', 'Among the sources for the history of Byzantine monasticism, none are more important than the typika, or foundation documents. Collected and translated in these volumes, the typkia may be used, for the first time, as a comprehensive study of religious life and institutions in the Greek East and as a comparison between Greek and Latin monasticism. Together, the typika illuminate almost every aspect of Byzantine monastic life and its development from the eighth to the fifteenth century. The work of these five volumes brought together a team of fourteen translators for sixty-one foundation documents. The nature of the typika, discussed by John Thomas in the introduction, was one of flexible and personal documents, which differed considerably in form, length, and content. Not all of them were foundation documents in the strict sense, since they could be issued at any time in the history of an institution. Some were wills; others were reform decrees and rules; yet others were primarily liturgical in character.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/thomas-hero-byzantine-monastic-foundation-documents', 'https://archive.org/details/thomas-hero-byzantine-monastic-foundation-documents', 'internet-archive:thomas-hero-byzantine-monastic-foundation-documents'),
  ('575941274198965165', 'C. Iulii Caesaris Commentarii de bello gallico', 'Gaius Julius Caesar, Marieluise Deißmann', 1570, 'History', 'C. Iulii Caesaris Commentarii de bello gallico by Gaius Julius Caesar, Marieluise Deißmann. A history book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL10306940W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL10306940W-'),
  ('875830588797402028', 'C. Iulii Caesaris Commentarii de bello gallico', 'Gaius Julius Caesar, Marieluise Deißmann', 1570, 'History', 'C. Iulii Caesaris Commentarii de bello gallico by Gaius Julius Caesar, Marieluise Deißmann', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6483181-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL10306940W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL10306940W'),
  ('419877994047769078', 'C. McKinney Provisional Patent for Fractal-Based Method and System for Modeling Complex Systems with Ethical Safeguards Across Multiple Domains', 'Clayton Alexander McKinney', 2025, 'Science', 'This is the original provisional patent filing by Clayton A. McKinney, submitted March 19, 2025, for a "Fractal-Based Method and System for Modeling Complex Systems with Ethical Safeguards Across Multiple Domains." The submission includes: - Provisional patent application documents - Cover letters - Technical drawings - Fee receipts - Certification and correspondence This work describes a novel approach to modeling, simulating, and analyzing complex systems using fractal mathematics, with explicit mechanisms for embedding ethical constraints and oversight. Patent Pending. U.S. Provisional Application filed March 19, 2025. This archive serves as a public, time-stamped disclosure of the invention and supporting materials, establishing prior art as of the upload date. **Rights Notice:** This work is proprietary and protected by U.S. provisional patent (filed March 19, 2025). All rights reserved. No rights or license are granted for use, reproduction, distribution, or commercialization of any part of this work without the explicit, prior written permission of the author. For licensing, collaboration, or permissions, contact: fractalprojectresearch@outlook.com Unauthorized use, reproduction, or distribution is strictly prohibited and may result in legal action.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/c.-mc-kinney-provisional-patent', 'https://archive.org/details/c.-mc-kinney-provisional-patent', 'internet-archive:c.-mc-kinney-provisional-patent'),
  ('301152129943869816', 'C# Notes for Professionals', 'Stack Overflow', 2018, 'Science', 'The C# Notes for Professionals book is compiled from Stack Overflow Documentation , the content is written by the beautiful people at Stack Overflow. Text content is released under Creative Commons BY-SA. See credits at the end of this book whom contributed to the various chapters. Images may be copyright of their respective owners unless otherwise specified. Book created for educational purposes and is not affiliated with C# group(s), company(s) nor Stack Overflow. All trademarks belong to their respective company owners.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/2018CSharpNotesForProfessionals', 'https://archive.org/details/2018CSharpNotesForProfessionals', 'internet-archive:2018CSharpNotesForProfessionals'),
