  ('701088216536004800', 'Civil Action No. 26-434', 'Judge Cynthia M. Rufe', 2026, 'History', '▪ On February 16th, 2026, Federal Judge Cynthia Rufe ordered the Trump administration to restore slavery-related exhibits at the national park site on the foundation of former President George Washington’s home in Philadelphia. ▪ Rufe invoked George Orwell’s dystopian novel '' 1984 ,'' saying the administration had attacked the concept of truth itself as it sought to erase details of America’s legacy of slavery. ▪ Rufe said the removal of the exhibits in January papered over Washington’s ownership of slaves and the special measures he took to avoid those enslaved persons gaining their liberty while he lived in Philadelphia from 1790 to 1797.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/civil-action-no.-26-434-02-16-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/civil-action-no.-26-434-02-16-2026', 'internet-archive:civil-action-no.-26-434-02-16-2026'),
