  ('789673270732646215', 'Conjuring Boxes Thanos Kalamidas', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'Mystery', 'The box was warm. A low, pulsing heat. Like a fever. Sara hadn’t meant to touch it again. She’d spent three gruelling weeks playing a game of mental tug-of-war, telling herself she was done. But there it sat. 3:47 AM. The "Dead Zone." The cube glowed on her nightstand, a dying ember in the dark, whispering to her without making a sound. Her fingers reached out, acting on a reflex her brain hadn''t authorised yet. Heat. It was always the heat. She’d found the damn thing six months ago. It had been hiding, tucked behind Hugo’s Les Misérables on the shelf Max had abandoned, along with his promises and his life with her. A small black cube. No bigger than a matchbox. Smooth as polished obsidian. Cold as a grave until you touched it. The first time she’d picked it up, it had hissed. It burned so badly she’d dropped it, the skin on her palm bubbling into an angry, white blister.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/conjuring-boxes-thanos-kalamidas', 'https://archive.org/details/conjuring-boxes-thanos-kalamidas', 'internet-archive:conjuring-boxes-thanos-kalamidas'),
  ('539898597005265476', 'CONNECTED Lucio Moschella 2026 Version 102 EN', 'LUCIO DAMIAN MOSCHELLA', 2026, 'History', 'CONNECTED: From the Commodore''s Blue Screen to Artificial Intelligence. A personal journey through the evolution of technology — from early home computers to the age of AI. Written by an IT professional who lived the transformation firsthand, this book traces three decades of technological change through personal experience, industry shifts, and the human stories behind the machines. Free digital edition, 2026.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/connected-lucio-moschella-2026-version-101-en', 'https://archive.org/details/connected-lucio-moschella-2026-version-101-en', 'internet-archive:connected-lucio-moschella-2026-version-101-en'),
