  ('857834918299905133', 'Constantine''s Strategic Appropriation, The Enginering Of Christian Empire', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This case study examines Constantine the Great''s strategic appropriation of Christianity (306-337 CE) to solve the Roman Empire''s legitimacy crisis following the Third Century collapse. It demonstrates how Constantine captured an existing belief system with robust institutional infrastructure—rather than constructing new legitimacy frameworks or restoring discredited ones—and redirected Christian bishops, theology, and church organization to legitimate imperial authority. The analysis traces this appropriation''s consequences from immediate stabilization through Christianity''s transformation into a civilization-shaping force over the subsequent two millennia.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/constantines-strategic-appropriation-the-enginering-of-christian-empire', 'https://archive.org/details/constantines-strategic-appropriation-the-enginering-of-christian-empire', 'internet-archive:constantines-strategic-appropriation-the-enginering-of-christian-empire'),
