  ('1103688292548230759', 'Counterintelligence Support of U.S. Immigration: Historical Development and Institutional Logic', 'Andrey Spiridonov', 2026, 'History', 'This book examines the historical evolution and institutional logic of counterintelligence support to United States immigration governance. It analyzes immigration systems as strategic security infrastructures shaped by constitutional law, statutory authority, and administrative practice. The study traces the integration of preventive security logic into immigration control from the early republic through the Cold War and into the contemporary era, emphasizing the balance between national security imperatives and legal constraint.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/counterintelligence-support-of-u.-s.-immigration-historical-development-and-institutional-logic', 'https://archive.org/details/counterintelligence-support-of-u.-s.-immigration-historical-development-and-institutional-logic', 'internet-archive:counterintelligence-support-of-u.-s.-immigration-historical-development-and-institutional-logic'),
