  ('784704151574646290', 'Da Vinci And His World Famous Painting And Dan Browns Fictional Code Everything You Thought You Knew Is Wrong', 'Dr. Avraham Mattityahu', 2025, 'Historical Fiction', 'Da Vinci and His World-Famous Painting — and Dan Brown’s Fictional Code: Everything You Thought You Knew Is Wrong by Avraham Mattityahu This powerful, eye-opening book dismantles centuries of artistic and cultural misunderstanding surrounding Leonardo da Vinci’s The Last Supper and the sensational myths popularized by Dan Brown’s The Da Vinci Code . With clarity and reverence, the author exposes how Renaissance art and modern fiction distorted one of the most sacred events in human history — the final Passover meal of Yeshua (Jesus). Through careful historical reconstruction, readers discover: What the real Passover setting looked like — from food and posture to lighting and atmosphere. How da Vinci’s painting replaced Jewish reality with European imagination . The true meaning of the Last Supper as the fulfillment of Passover, not a new ritual. Why Dan Brown’s claims about secret bloodlines, hidden codes, and church conspiracies are historically baseless . How Yeshua, the Lamb of Yehovah, transformed Passover into the New Covenant of redemption . Combining biblical scholarship, historical accuracy, and accessible teaching, this work restores the Jewish roots of Christian faith and reclaims the heart of the Gospel message: “The greatest mystery was never hidden in art. It hung on a cross.” An essential read for believers, historians, and truth seekers alike, this book replaces myth with meaning — and shows how rediscovering the authentic Passover transforms our understanding of Communion, covenant, and salvation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/da-vinci-and-his-world-famous-painting-and-dan-browns-fictional-code-everything-', 'https://archive.org/details/da-vinci-and-his-world-famous-painting-and-dan-browns-fictional-code-everything-', 'internet-archive:da-vinci-and-his-world-famous-painting-and-dan-browns-fictional-code-everything-'),
