  ('136567214474086766', 'Debt: The First 5000 Years', 'David Graeber', 2011, 'History', 'Debt: The First 5,000 Years is a book by anthropologist David Graeber, published in 2011. It explores the historical relationship of debt with social institutions such as barter, marriage, friendship, slavery, law, religion, war and government; in short, much of the fabric of human life in society. It draws on the history and anthropology of a number of civilizations, large and small, from the first known records of debt from Sumer, in 3500 BC until the present.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/DebtTheFirst5000Years', 'https://archive.org/details/DebtTheFirst5000Years', 'internet-archive:DebtTheFirst5000Years'),
