  ('764828686947134765', 'Decentralized Law: The Power of Blockchain to Transform the Broken Legal System', 'Wesley Thysse', 2025, 'History', 'Decentralized Law is a groundbreaking analysis of how blockchain technology can transform our legal systems. Written by Wesley Thysse, this comprehensive work explores 2,500 years of legal history, examining natural law, civil law, international law, and private law to understand how our current system evolved and where it is failing. The book examines the property rights associated with crypto assets, and analyzes the legality of popular blockchain applications and their missing legal frameworks. Thysse introduces a new approach to law-making that prioritizes liberty and consent over centralized authority. He presents revolutionary legal concepts including the Decentralized Bill of Liberties, Declaration of State Rights and Duties, and Freedom of the Nodes, alongside practical frameworks like Smart Contract Blocks, Consensus Jurisdictions, Decentralized Legal Systems, and Decentralized Autonomous Associations. This visionary work offers both theoretical foundations and practical solutions for a more balanced, decentralized legal future.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/decentralized-law', 'https://archive.org/details/decentralized-law', 'internet-archive:decentralized-law'),
