  ('802743772381244003', 'Desta Bierbauer: Collected Writings', 'Desta Bierbauer', 2026, 'Science', 'Desta Bierbauer: Collected Writings is a unified archive of original writing produced and maintained by Desta Bierbauer. This work is ongoing and lifelong in scope, originating in sustained conceptual engagement beginning in 1997 and entering public circulation in 2011 through serialized email distribution. The writings engage questions drawn from rhetoric, systems thinking, and science, including conceptual work informed by theoretical physics, without adhering to disciplinary boundaries. The archive gathers texts that were previously dispersed across private correspondence, informal publication, and serial transmission, and presents them as a coherent body of work under a single authorship. Its purpose is not to announce conclusions but to preserve continuity: rhetorical, conceptual, and formal. Authorship is single and canonical. The writings collected here are authored by Desta Bierbauer and are presented as the authoritative record of that work, organized retrospectively and maintained prospectively as new material is added. No claim of completion or finality is made. The collection exists for readers interested in long-form thinking developed over time, including work that moves between rhetoric, systems, science, and theory without conforming to disciplinary boundaries. It is intended as a point of orientation rather than instruction, allowing readers to encounter the material at varying depths and potentially in non-linear order. The archive functions as a root: a stable reference point for material that continues to evolve, expand, and interrelate. Citation & Archival Note Author: Desta Bierbauer Title: Desta Bierbauer: Collected Writings Status: Ongoing work Preparatory work: Began 1997 Public circulation: Began 2011 Archival note: The PDFs associated with this item constitute the primary texts of record. The materials together represent a unified body of work by Desta Bierbauer , authored and circulated over time as a single, continuous project.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/collected-writings', 'https://archive.org/details/collected-writings', 'internet-archive:collected-writings'),
