  ('1140012655141542208', 'Deterministic Tensorial Generative Framework Applied To The P Versus NP Problem', 'Tyrone Farmer', 2026, 'Science', 'This document presents an application of the Deterministic Tensorial Generative Framework (DTGF) to the P versus NP problem in computational complexity theory. The framework models decision problems as elements of a deterministic tensorial state space equipped with structure-preserving flows, invariance conditions, and formal provability predicates. Within this framework, complexity classes are analyzed through deterministic transformations that preserve satisfiability, halting behavior, and polynomial-time structure. The work examines NP-complete problems under DTGF invariance assumptions and demonstrates that, within the framework’s axioms, a separation between P and NP cannot be maintained without violating determinism or semantic preservation. As a result, the framework yields an internal collapse of NP into P. The result is explicitly framework-relative and does not claim to resolve the classical P versus NP problem in the standard Turing machine model. Instead, it provides a formal exploration of how invariant-preserving deterministic generative systems constrain computational complexity distinctions. This work is intended for readers interested in theoretical computer science, complexity theory, and alternative formal frameworks for analyzing computation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/deterministic-tensorial-generative-framework-applied-to-the-p-versus-np-problem', 'https://archive.org/details/deterministic-tensorial-generative-framework-applied-to-the-p-versus-np-problem', 'internet-archive:deterministic-tensorial-generative-framework-applied-to-the-p-versus-np-problem'),
