  ('489990478957643856', 'DTIF: A Universal Architecture for Autonomous Science and Sovereign Discovery Economies', 'Er. Nabal Kishore Pande', 2026, 'Science', 'This paper introduces the Digital Trust & Interoperability Framework (DTIF), a universal architecture designed to support trustworthy autonomous scientific ecosystems. The framework integrates three core components: • The Self-Driving Laboratory (SDL) Maturity Model for classifying levels of laboratory autonomy • The Digital Trust Score (DTS) for evaluating the reliability and auditability of autonomous research agents • The FRYX Interoperability Protocol for enabling coordinated multi-agent experimentation across heterogeneous laboratory systems Together these components establish a foundation for large-scale autonomous scientific discovery and the emergence of a global discovery economy based on AI-driven experimentation and robotic laboratories. Author: Er. Nabal Kishore Pande Independent Researcher, India Official DOI version available on Figshare: https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.31742800', 'https://archive.org/services/img/fryx-dtif-autonomous-science-framework-pande-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/fryx-dtif-autonomous-science-framework-pande-2026', 'internet-archive:fryx-dtif-autonomous-science-framework-pande-2026'),
