  ('13080935144194610', 'Early Floods In Los Angeles County, J. F. Reagan 1917', 'Reagan, J. F.', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'Early Floods in Los Angeles County (1917) By J. F. Reagan, County Flood Control Engineer Published in 1917, Early Floods in Los Angeles County is a primary-source compilation prepared by Los Angeles County Flood Control Engineer J. F. Reagan documenting major flood events from 1811 through the early 20th century. The volume includes indexed accounts of the floods of 1811, 1815, 1822, 1825, 1832, 1842, 1851--52, 1858--59, 1859--60, and 1861--62, together with later 19th-century events. Drawing from interviews, correspondence, court records, well logs, rainfall notes, and contemporary newspapers (including the Los Angeles News and Los Angeles Star ), Reagan records testimony from identified residents, landowners, engineers, and public officials across the Los Angeles, San Gabriel, Santa Ana, and related river systems. Locations documented include Los Angeles, San Fernando, El Monte, Downey, Rivera, Compton, Artesia, Long Beach, Tropico, and surrounding agricultural districts. The work is organized both geographically and thematically, with sections addressing river diversions (Los Angeles, San Gabriel, Santa Ana, New River, Verdugo Wash, and others), channel shifts, driftwood accumulation, rainfall, bank protection, groundwater conditions, artesian wells, and observations such as wood found in wells and the closing of the mouth of the Los Angeles River at Long Beach. An extensive index lists contributors, addresses, and page references, making the volume both a historical narrative and a structured reference document. Prepared during the formative period of organized flood control planning in Los Angeles County, the report preserves detailed observations of river behavior, overbank flooding, groundwater interaction, and channel migration prior to comprehensive levee construction and channelization. It remains a significant historical reference for researchers examining watershed change, historical river alignments, and early flood documentation in the Los Angeles Basin.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/early-floods-in-los-angeles-county-j.-f.-reagan-1917', 'https://archive.org/details/early-floods-in-los-angeles-county-j.-f.-reagan-1917', 'internet-archive:early-floods-in-los-angeles-county-j.-f.-reagan-1917'),
