  ('805858904488044615', 'Eng தமிழரின் வானியல் அறிவு', 'கி. காளைராசன், Dr. K.. Kalairajan,', 2026, 'Literature', 'This article explores the fascinating intersection of Sangam literature, ancient astronomy, and temple architecture. It specifically highlights how the astronomical descriptions in the Sangam-era poem ''Nedunalvadai'' by poet Nakkeerar correlate with the unique stone carvings of the 27 stars (constellations) found at the Avudaiyar Koil (Thirupperunthurai) in Pudukkottai. The piece delves into how ancient Tamils recorded celestial movements on clay-coated pillars, a tradition that was later immortalized in stone. I believe this subject will be of great interest to your readers who follow Indian heritage, literature, and art history.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/eng_20260325', 'https://archive.org/details/eng_20260325', 'internet-archive:eng_20260325'),
