  ('582622964275739383', 'Family Narratives and Notes from Cassie Widener-Shields', 'Jeffrey Hunt', 2026, 'History', 'This entry reflects on family history prompted by a post about Lewis Nolan Smith. It records two direct-line ancestors—William Lowery Shields and his son James William Shields—who were both killed by falling trees while working in the woods near Yoncalla, Douglas County, Oregon. The note documents the circumstances of their deaths and situates them within the broader context of early logging work and occupational hazards in the region. Written by Cassie Widener-Shields.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/james-william-shields', 'https://archive.org/details/james-william-shields', 'internet-archive:james-william-shields'),
