  ('705599862491597796', 'Finland, From Swedish Colony To Social Democracy Elite Power And The Price Of Revolution ( 1150s 2025)', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines elite power mechanisms in Finland across 850+ years (1150s-2025), analyzing how Swedish colonization created a Swedish-speaking elite that persisted through Russian rule, independence, civil war, and social democratic development. It demonstrates how the 1918 Civil War''s White Terror (37,000 dead, 1.1% of population) violently reconsolidated elite power, followed by minimal land reforms and eventual social democratic compromise that reduced wealth concentration from 40-50% to 15-20% (top 1%) while preserving capitalist ownership structures. The study reveals how language became a class marker throughout Finnish history, with Swedish-speakers dominating elite positions despite representing only 12-15% of the population, and how social democracy achieved real improvements in workers'' lives while operating within fundamental limits that preserved concentrated wealth ownership. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/finland-from-swedish-colony-to-social-democracy-elite-power-and-the-price-of-revolution-1150s-2025', 'https://archive.org/details/finland-from-swedish-colony-to-social-democracy-elite-power-and-the-price-of-revolution-1150s-2025', 'internet-archive:finland-from-swedish-colony-to-social-democracy-elite-power-and-the-price-of-revolution-1150s-2025'),
