  ('266969063755894114', 'First School Building in Camas Washington Built in 1886', 'Jeffrey Hunt', 2026, 'History', 'A photo of the first school building in Camas, constructed in 1886, shown after later additions. This image appeared in the Camas-Washougal Post-Record dated May 27, 1970 in the Crown Zellerbach Centennial edition. The caption describes the photo as taken about 1903 after additions were made, including a porch, a rear wing, and a cupola. Source and credit: Internet Archive, Virginia Warren collection, uploaded by Camas Public Library. License: CC BY–NC–SA 4.0. (Sharing with credit for non-commercial use.)', 'https://archive.org/services/img/camas-first-school-building-built-1886-ia00', 'https://archive.org/details/camas-first-school-building-built-1886-ia00', 'internet-archive:camas-first-school-building-built-1886-ia00'),
