  ('75411653718363287', 'Flash Gordon By Alex Raymond REMASTER', 'Alex Raymond (scanned images improved by Fabian1966)', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'PACKAGE ======== Flash_Gordon_by_Alex_Raymond_REMASTER CONTENT ======== Improved version of the 26 Flash Gordon comic stories by Alex Raymond. Flash_Gordon_by_Alex_Raymond_REMASTER_cbz.zip Flash_Gordon_by_Alex_Raymond_REMASTER_jpeg.zip Flash_Gordon_by_Alex_Raymond_REMASTER_pdf.zip The 3 archives contain the same about 700 comic pages as jpg images in different package formats. The images were taken from old scanned jpg images and were massively improved by AI image enhancement. DESCRIPTION ============ I am a fan of the old classic Flash Gordon comics by Alex Raymond, so I downloaded the collection of 26 stories also available here on archive.org. The collection was created by scanning the original comics many years ago. Recently I had some really impressive results with the new AI image enhancement tools for photos and comics. So I took the open source AI enhancer tool "upscayl" and ran it over all the scanned pictures in the downloaded archives Settings for upscayl were: model is digital artwork, upscaling factor is two, output format is jpg. After this I recompressed the resulting big jpg pictures as much as possible without loss of image quality, but the images are still quite large. My created "jpeg" archive and also the "cbz" archive directly contains these pictures. NOTE1: CBZ means comic book zip NOTE2: the CBZ files are simple ZIP archives, just change file name ending cbz to zip. Also the PDF files were created from these jpg files without further compression and thus are quite big, up to 100 Megabytes per PDF. But these big PDF files are no problem for a modern PC and color printer. There are a lot of tools to make the PDF files smaller if you need this. Fabian February 2025 (archive.org user fabian1966)', 'https://archive.org/services/img/flash-gordon-by-alex-raymond', 'https://archive.org/details/flash-gordon-by-alex-raymond', 'internet-archive:flash-gordon-by-alex-raymond'),
