  ('932833517063078777', 'Found', 'M.B. Tohamov', 2026, 'Science', 'In the aftermath of a global cognitive event that humanity quietly agreed to forget, Walid—a psychiatrist in Germany—receives a routine assignment: evaluate a man named Rieger. Rieger claims to remember what the world erased. What begins as a forensic psychiatric assessment becomes an ethical trap. Diagnosis blurs into belief. Silence becomes institutional. Medication replaces meaning. And the question Walid cannot answer is no longer whether Rieger is ill—but whether sanity itself survived the Event. As Walid’s personal life fractures and the machinery of bureaucracy closes in, Found explores the thin membrane between truth and survival, responsibility and abdication. A novel about psychiatry, power, collapse, and the cost of remaining reasonable in an unreasonable world.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/found_20260228', 'https://archive.org/details/found_20260228', 'internet-archive:found_20260228'),
