  ('551765268773764894', 'From Port To Parish Full Copy', 'Dr. Shannon Bennett Santiesteban, LL.M.', 2026, 'History', 'From Port to Parish: A Creole Family''s Journey Through Reconstruction Louisiana is a work of microhistory, a sustained examination of one family across multiple generations, situated within the broader historical forces that shaped and constrained their lives. Its subject is Anatole Louis Borée and his descendants: his widow, Josephine, likely born Lavilotte or Laviolette; his daughter Marie, an educator in Reconstruction-era New Orleans; his daughter Adelaide, who would carry the family name into the Cane River region through her marriage into the Perret family; and Loretta Perret Blanchard, whose presence in the Seventh Ward of New Orleans represents the culmination of a multigenerational journey from port to parish, from political precarity to rooted community life.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/from-port-to-parish-full-copy', 'https://archive.org/details/from-port-to-parish-full-copy', 'internet-archive:from-port-to-parish-full-copy'),
