  ('399005824333614989', 'FULL MOONS, GROUNDING AND DISCIPLINE:What our ancestors knew and we forgot', 'Amlima Mawuvi', 2026, 'Science', 'This paper presents an ancestral Afrikan analysis of lunar cycles, focusing on the Full Moon as a moment of revelation rather than intervention. Rooted in Eʋe and broader Afrikan cosmological logic, it critiques modern performative spirituality and reasserts grounding, discipline, and cyclical restraint as core principles of authentic spiritual authority. The work is intended for researchers, cultural practitioners, and readers interested in decolonized approaches to spirituality, cosmology, and Afrikan knowledge restoration.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/full-moons-grounding-and-discipline-ancestral-afrikan-perspective-amlima-mawuvi', 'https://archive.org/details/full-moons-grounding-and-discipline-ancestral-afrikan-perspective-amlima-mawuvi', 'internet-archive:full-moons-grounding-and-discipline-ancestral-afrikan-perspective-amlima-mawuvi'),
