  ('489041652862651618', 'Gay History: NY Organized Crime and Drag', 'Brian A. Smith, D.C.', 2026, 'History', 'A look at the ties between the world of organized crime and the drag culture through the actions of Anna (Petillo) Genovese, wife of the crime-family boss Vito Genovese, and the clubs she was involved in: Club Caravan at 578 West Broadway in 1939, Club 82 at 82 E. 4th St. in 1950, and the 181 Club in East Manhattan. Also dincluded is a collection of sources on the "drag queen killers," Little Davey Petillo & Charles Gagliodotto, who used drag to get close to their victims in New York City of the 1920s and 1930s. Whether there is afamilial tie between Anna and Little Davey is not known.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/mob-and-drag', 'https://archive.org/details/mob-and-drag', 'internet-archive:mob-and-drag'),
