  ('229347496660161887', 'Genealogy Module V 1.2', 'James Lashley', 2026, 'History', 'Convergent Inference Framework (CIF) v3.9 — Genealogy Module v1.2 Author: James Lashley (Independent Researcher) Date: April 2026 License: CC BY 4.0 --- Overview This document is the Genealogy Module for CIF v3.9. It provides domain-specific guidance for genealogical research deployments under the Convergent Inference Framework. This module requires CIF v3.9 Core Framework. --- What''s Inside Phase 0b Guidance — Mandatory Hypothesis Categories for Genealogical Deployments: - Direct Origin - Alternative Geographic Origin - Record Discontinuity - Multiple Independent Origins - Structural Indeterminacy Addendum Protocol for research leads emerging after Phase 0b closes Source Lineage Verification Guidance — Genealogical Derivative Chain Types: - Parish Register to Genealogical Compilation - Primary Record to Online Tree - Academic Paper to Secondary Citation - DNA Test Result to Interpretation Publication - Researcher Synthesis to AI Synthesis Module Gates: - Rule 6 — Patrilineal Continuity Risk Declaration - Migration Gap Risk Declaration - Phase VII Patrilineal Continuity Qualification Phase V Cross-Reference Note — Assessment Suppression and Record Discontinuity Minimum Verification for Evidence-driven Classification in Genealogy Single-Lineage Source Concentration Threshold (60%) --- Key Features - Record Discontinuity Hypothesis Obligation (prevents assuming plausible connections are confirmed) - Addendum Protocol for post-registration research leads - Derivative chain collapse requirements before Evidence-driven classification - Integration with Category 6 Assessment Suppression (Phase V, Core Framework) --- Required Companions - CIF v3.9 Core Framework - MAIA v2.2 Protocol (for post-run audit) --- Suggested Citation Lashley, James. "Convergent Inference Framework (CIF) v3.9 — Genealogy Module v1.2." Internet Archive, April 2026. [URL] --- Contact James Lashley, Independent Researcher Correspondence via Substack: https://substack.com/@jameslashley1?utm_source=share&utm_medium=android&r=h4c8c', 'https://archive.org/services/img/genealogy-module-v-1.2', 'https://archive.org/details/genealogy-module-v-1.2', 'internet-archive:genealogy-module-v-1.2'),
  ('219795286971136547', 'Generac 2024 Annual Report & Proxy Statement', 'Generac Holdings Inc.', 2025, 'History', 'The 2024 annual report & Form 10-K, Proxy Statement and Chairman''s message to stockholders for Generac Holdings Inc. (Ticker: GNRC). Generac is an American manufacturer of backup power generators and other power products for residential, industrial and light commerical markets. Founded in 1959, the company is based in Waukesha, Wisconsin. The corporate name is a combination of ''generating'' and ''AC''.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/generac-holdings-inc.-gnrc-proxy-statement-2025-06-12', 'https://archive.org/details/generac-holdings-inc.-gnrc-proxy-statement-2025-06-12', 'internet-archive:generac-holdings-inc.-gnrc-proxy-statement-2025-06-12'),
