  ('261384474197705866', 'Gibbs: A Once-Lost Family History from Colonial Pennsylvania through Southern Illinois to DeKalb', 'Derek M. Gibbs', 2026, 'History', 'This book tells the story of the Gibbs and the related Cook, King, Mattingly, and Williams families—not as names on a chart, but as lives once lived. From the hills of Pennsylvania and Kentucky to Indiana farmsteads, Illinois homesteads, coal towns, and northern factory cities, these families followed the promise of land, work, and a better future for their children. They were farmers and laborers, mothers and soldiers, shaped by war, migration, faith, loss, and resilience. Much of their story was nearly lost. Through records, photographs, and rediscovered evidence, these lives are brought back into view—so they are no longer just ancestors, but people again. Written for descendants and future generations, this book is an act of remembrance: a way of honoring where we come from, and why those journeys still matter. ISBN: 979-8-90119-059-3', 'https://archive.org/services/img/GibbsBookDeKalb', 'https://archive.org/details/GibbsBookDeKalb', 'internet-archive:GibbsBookDeKalb'),
