  ('786276923082239963', 'GOSPEL & MISSION TO MARS', 'PETER ELGIN', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'In Gospel.The Black Prince submarine.Comes back to the Pacific Ocean after its trip to Gilda Prime.And find a global news feed with a story of a crashed spaceship on Mount Ararat, fabled.Resting place of Noah''s Ark. When Doctor Goodfellow.Chambers investigate.They find that there''s breeding units and incubators. Can starts a research program at least university with the help of Vice Chancellor Martin Emerson. And persuades Sarah Dunlop and Harry Sullivan to be the parents of the 1st artificial human. In the sequel to this exciting story the baby is born in a central London clinic. Elgin takes a voyage across the ocean In the BLACK PRINCE SUBMARINE and starts his M ISSION TO MARS . The first colony on Mars Co-produced by the Galactic Federation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/mission-to-mars-a', 'https://archive.org/details/mission-to-mars-a', 'internet-archive:mission-to-mars-a'),
  ('199358508220230784', 'Goth Adivasi Stories from Gujarat', 'Kanji Patel', 2017, 'Literature', 'Goth: Adivasi Stories from Gujarat by Kanji Patel (ed.) and by Sonal Baxi (trans .) Published by Bhasha Research and Publication Centre (India) © 2017 which has since made its vast catalogue of books, articles and journals freely available(Open Access) Contributors Arvind Patel, Dahyabhai Vadhu, Jeetendra Vasava, Mansing Chaudhari, Nazroo Rathwa, Urmila Gamit, Vanita Valvi Illustrators Chetan Parshuram Gangavane, Eknath Parshuram Gangavane, Desing Rathwa, Lalji Rathwa, Mahendra Gamit, Nazroo Rathwa Layout and Design Rajat Gajjar, Yash Desai and Sahana Iyer Cover Illustration Chetan Parshuram Gangavane and Eknath Parshuram Gangavane Bhasha and its publication unit, Purva Prakash , have together documented the rich literature prevalent in these languages, their epics, narratives, theatre, music traditions and arts. Bhasha and Purva Prakash have published literary and children’s magazines, books, educational material in print and digital format in 32 Adivasi languages as well as in the major languages as Gujarati, Hindi, Marathi and English. These publications present the Adivasi imagination, knowledge systems, culture and society and have brought visibility to and understanding regarding a significant but long neglected stream of Indian literature and society.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/GothAdivasiStoriesfromGujarat', 'https://archive.org/details/GothAdivasiStoriesfromGujarat', 'internet-archive:GothAdivasiStoriesfromGujarat'),
