  ('693339752029518377', 'GUIDE BOOK FOR DESCRIPTIVE PAPER LIS PROFESSIONALS BY SAKET SHARMA', 'Saket Sharma', 2025, 'Science', 'The "Guide Book for Descriptive Paper – LIS Professionals" by Saket Sharma is a comprehensive resource crafted especially for aspirants preparing for various Library and Information Science (LIS) competitive examinations that include descriptive/subjective-type questions . This book is designed to bridge the gap between theoretical understanding and practical expression, enabling candidates to present well-structured, content-rich answers in exams conducted by UGC-NET, KVS, NVS, DSSSB, RSMSSB, State PSCs, University Recruitments, and other Government organizations . 📚 Key Features ✅ Exam-Oriented Approach : Covers all major topics expected in descriptive sections of LIS exams. ✅ Well-Organized Content : Divided into thematic sections like Library Types, Services, ICT, Management, Bibliometrics, Research Methodology, and National Policies. ✅ Model Answers : Includes model descriptive answers with proper formatting, introductions, and conclusions. ✅ Updated Terminology : Incorporates recent trends, terminology, standards, and government initiatives relevant to LIS. ✅ Useful for Interviews : Aids in interview preparation and academic writing , enhancing the candidate’s ability to articulate ideas clearly. 🔍 Topics Covered Include : Information Sources &amp; Services Library Classification &amp; Cataloguing Digital Libraries &amp; Library Automation Library Management &amp; Marketing Research Methodology &amp; Technical Writing Public &amp; Academic Library Systems Professional Ethics &amp; LIS Education in India Government Bodies &amp; Library Networks (e.g., INFLIBNET, DELNET, RRRLF) Current Affairs in LIS &amp; ICT Tools 👤 About the Author Saket Sharma is a seasoned Library Professional, Mentor, and Tech-savvy Educator who has supported hundreds of students and professionals in their LIS journey. With hands-on experience and deep academic insight, he brings practical strategies and clarity for mastering descriptive papers in library science. 🎯 Ideal For : MLIS/BLIS students Library Assistant and Librarian aspirants UGC-NET (Paper II – LIS) candidates Professionals appearing for written tests with descriptive questions Anyone aiming to sharpen their academic writing skills in LIS', 'https://archive.org/services/img/guide-book-for-descriptive-paper-lis-professionals-by-saket-sharma', 'https://archive.org/details/guide-book-for-descriptive-paper-lis-professionals-by-saket-sharma', 'internet-archive:guide-book-for-descriptive-paper-lis-professionals-by-saket-sharma'),
