  ('889072702741233128', 'History of Campsites and Crestline on Palomar Mountain', 'Peter Brueggeman', 2026, 'History', 'History of the Birch Hill / Crestline development on Palomar Mountain, which was known as Campsites. Includes history of the clubhouse and lodge whose earlier names were Edgewood Tavern and Skyline Lodge. People associated with the area include Reid Wallace, Spencer Scott Purkey, Everett Clyde Linthicum, Milton Fenelon Bailey, Lucius Carlisle ''Carl'' Mendenhall, Ralph Tillinghast, Frank and Lydia Shupe, Thomas Sheridan Boland, Thomas Hill Boland, Art and Mildred Koenig, Oliver Brown, Betty and Bob Lowe.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/campsites_202312', 'https://archive.org/details/campsites_202312', 'internet-archive:campsites_202312'),
