  ('690948560402839777', 'How I Pack My Lunch', 'Jennifer Boothroyd, Intuitive, Intuitive Intuitive', 2014, 'Cooking', 'How I Pack My Lunch by Jennifer Boothroyd, Intuitive, Intuitive Intuitive. A cooking book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20337140W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL20337140W-'),
  ('538717429576159889', 'How I Pack My Lunch', 'Jennifer Boothroyd, Intuitive, Intuitive Intuitive', 2014, 'Cooking', 'How I Pack My Lunch by Jennifer Boothroyd, Intuitive, Intuitive Intuitive', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9001241-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20337140W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL20337140W'),
  ('882352530662782604', 'How Military Outcomes Determine What People Believe', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This theoretical paper examines the material and institutional origins of religious belief, arguing that the specific content of what people believe is determined primarily by military outcomes and institutional infrastructure rather than individual spiritual discernment. Drawing on three case studies — the Persian plateau''s transition through Zoroastrianism, Manichaeism, and Islam across four centuries; the English Reformation as administrative reorganization; and secular nationalism as a non-theological application of the same mechanism — the paper demonstrates how controlling schools, courts, ceremonies, and other institutions converts military victory into durable belief across generations. The analysis extends to secular belief systems including French republicanism and Soviet Marxism-Leninism, arguing the mechanism is about legitimating power rather than religion specifically. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/how-military-outcomes-determine-what-people-believe', 'https://archive.org/details/how-military-outcomes-determine-what-people-believe', 'internet-archive:how-military-outcomes-determine-what-people-believe'),
  ('1121317476372668147', 'How Music Works', 'David Byrne', 2012, 'Music', 'How Music Works by David Byrne. A music book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17068219W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL17068219W-'),
  ('42623192236657097', 'How Music Works', 'David Byrne', 2012, 'Music', 'How Music Works by David Byrne', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8867987-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL17068219W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL17068219W'),
  ('721752414781062570', 'How Not to Kill Your Husband', 'Sandra Cabot', 2012, 'Self Help', 'How Not to Kill Your Husband by Sandra Cabot. A self help book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL35690865W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL35690865W-'),
  ('299952802525768352', 'How Not to Kill Your Husband', 'Sandra Cabot', 2012, 'Self Help', 'How Not to Kill Your Husband by Sandra Cabot', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/olid/OL35690865W-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL35690865W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL35690865W'),
  ('713770902530721059', 'How Population Change Will Transform Our World', 'Sarah Harper', 2016, 'Science', 'How Population Change Will Transform Our World by Sarah Harper. A science book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20155211W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL20155211W-'),
  ('1111094518645267757', 'How Ruling Elites Use Belief To Prevent The People They Rule From Recognizing Each Other', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This theoretical paper examines how ruling elites simultaneously produce vertical identification (alignment with one''s own ruling class) and horizontal alienation (hostility toward structurally equivalent people in other civilizations) through the same institutional mechanisms of belief transmission. Using parallel case studies — an Iranian woman and an American woman each performing institutionally defined femininity, and factory workers in Iran and the United States each having their anger redirected away from class grievance and toward civilizational threat — the paper argues that the specific content of belief systems differs across civilizations while the mechanism of manufacture and the elite interest it serves are identical. Drawing on Marx, Gramsci, and comparative feminist scholarship, it analyzes historical moments when cross-civilizational solidarity briefly emerged and the institutional responses that suppressed it. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/how-ruling-elites-use-belief-to-prevent-the-people-they-rule-from-recognizing-each-other', 'https://archive.org/details/how-ruling-elites-use-belief-to-prevent-the-people-they-rule-from-recognizing-each-other', 'internet-archive:how-ruling-elites-use-belief-to-prevent-the-people-they-rule-from-recognizing-each-other'),
  ('130425357273156060', 'How space rockets began', 'Le Grand', 1960, 'Science', 'How space rockets began by Le Grand. A science book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL15737490W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL15737490W-'),
  ('694905112991596858', 'How Technology Works', 'Unknown', 2019, 'Science', 'Have you ever asked yourself how the inventions, gadgets, and devices that surround us actually work? Discover the hidden workings of everyday technology with this graphic guide. How Technology Works demystifies the machinery that keeps the modern world going, from simple objects such as zip fasteners and can openers to the latest, most sophisticated devices of the information age, including smartwatches, personal digital assistants, and driverless cars. It includes inventions that have changed the course of history, like the internal combustion engine, as well as technologies that might hold the key to our future survival, including solar cells and new kinds of farming to feed a growing population. Throughout the book, step-by-step explanations are supported by simple and original graphics that take devices apart and show you how they work. The opening chapter explains principles that underpin lots of devices, from basic mechanics to electricity to digital technology. From there, devices are grouped by application--such as the home, transportation, and computing--making them easy to find and placing similar devices side by side. How Technology Works is perfect for anyone who didn''t have training in STEM subjects at school or is simply curious about how the modern world works. Power technology -- Transportation technology -- Materials and construction technology -- Technology in the home -- Sound and vision technology -- Computer technology -- Communications technology -- Farming and food technology -- Medical technology.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/how-technology-works', 'https://archive.org/details/how-technology-works', 'internet-archive:how-technology-works'),
  ('873346022379814905', 'How The Alchemists Meditated Hauck', 'Dennis William Hauck', 2025, 'History', 'In this full-color edition, a leading researcher in the field reveals the actual meditations used by alchemists and provides considerable evidence that psycho-spiritual alchemy was practiced many centuries before the Renaissance—contrary to what some modern academics believe. A primary tool in the work of the alchemists was a unique kind of meditation based on the light of Mind. They gradually learned how to work with this light to discover the “First Matter”—of objects, their own mental states, and their very souls—and transmute them into something new and more perfect. Thousands of years ago, alchemists realized the light of the One Mind of the universe is reflected in their own minds and bodies, and they began to develop a physico-spiritual technology based on the universal principles of transformation. Most of us share the same deep yearning of the alchemists to connect to the energies behind creation and change—that is the true source of alchemy. The mystery of the cosmos is something we all sense at some time in our lives. Or, in the words of Albert Einstein: "The most beautiful thing we can experience is the mysterious. It is the source of all art and science.” Includes Table of Contents, extensive Bibliography of Spiritual Alchemy, and dozens of Internet Resources for further research.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/how-the-alchemists-meditated-hauck', 'https://archive.org/details/how-the-alchemists-meditated-hauck', 'internet-archive:how-the-alchemists-meditated-hauck'),
