  ('839349858911510415', 'Imminent; Inside The Pentagon''s Hunt For UFO''s', 'Luis Elizondo', 2024, 'History', 'This new heavily promoted best-seller is a mixed bag of partial disclosures stirred in with outright lies to disinform those new to this topic. Here is what world class exopolitics scholar Dr. Michael Salla had to say about the pluses and minuses of this new book in a recent review: “So people are being told UFOs have crashed that these UFOs are piloted by non-human beings. So right there you get people being told that the UFO phenomenon is associated with extraterrestrial life. Now that''s something that up until recently was being suppressed very heavily in the mainstream news media as well as the Pentagon. But now someone has turned on the, or turned off the suppression switch. And so now mainstream media can talk about people with evidence or who have maybe some kind of firsthand account of having interacted with these non-human intelligences associated with the UFOs. And the other thing that Luis Alizondo mentions is that this program that he is associated with that they learned that there has been a crashed retrieval reverse engineering program going on for decades. So what that means is that these craft have been recovered by the military, handed over to top aerospace companies and these top aerospace companies have been studying these craft for decades now. “So I think there are pluses and minuses when we look at Luis Alizondo''s testimony. The plus is that the general public is learning that UFOs are real, that the recovery of crashed UFOs have happened, that Roswell really did happen and that even earlier incidents in 1933 in Italy happened. And that these craft are being piloted by non-human intelligence. So far that''s really good, that''s opening the door. “But there are some negatives. I mean, he''s saying that, he''s telling people that these reverse engineering efforts have been unsuccessful, that there is no Secret Space Program, that what we''re seeing up there are these UFOs piloted by non-human intelligence. And there''s nothing in the United States inventory or the inventories of Russia or China that can replicate the behavior of the performance of these craft. So… I''ve written a seven volume series on Secret Space Programs and there''s just abundant evidence that Secret Space Programs are real. They have been successfully developed by top aerospace companies that were involved in these. Now, why Alizondo doesn''t know this? Well, I think I go back to that dictum that I remember hearing Richard Hoagland talk about over 20 years ago, he was saying the lie is different at every level. So the general public would be told one lie. Middle level bureaucrats in the Pentagon would be told another lie. And even senior level officials in the Pentagon or in Congress would be told another lie. “And so on it goes that the lies exist at these different levels. But when you get to the deepest innermost level, it''s like, yes, these craft have been successfully reverse engineered and that they are in operation today and that what we see in the skies, people are seeing, a majority of those are actually reverse engineered craft, not extraterrestrial craft. “And here''s the other negative from Luis Alizondo''s testimony and his book is that UFOs are a national security threat. Well, he approaches this as someone working for the Pentagon and of course, Pentagon officials look for national security threats. In fact, I mean, if you read his book halfway through reading his book, Imminent. And I mean, it''s very clear that he stresses that this is a national security threat, what these UFOs are doing and why isn''t anyone else in the senior leadership of the Pentagon paying attention on giving this serious thought and of course, because he failed, in his view, failed to impress upon the Pentagon officials, the seriousness of the UFO threat, he decided to quit and go public. And that''s, and that happened back in 2017 and led to a story in the New York Times that kind of launched this new phase that we''re in. “So I think at best Luis Alizondo is really helping educate people that have not been aware of the UFO issue in their professional lives, make them aware that this is a real issue. But I think he is also steering people down the wrong track and that''s where you get the idea of a limited hangout [half-truths] that Alizondo is part of an orchestrated limited hangout that some people have been contending. And I can''t dispute that. I think that this is at best a limited hangout that Alizondo truly believes what he believes, but he was told a bunch of lies when he was working in the Pentagon and investigating the UFO phenomenon that he was out of the loop of this kind of UFO phenomenon, which he talks about in his book anyway, and he admits to that.” More than that, why was the book so poorly researched in the first place? There are hundreds of books on this topic available that are not fear mongering upstarts. Table of contents : Half Title Title Page Copyright Trigger Warning Dedication Author’s Note Contents Foreword by Christopher Mellon Introduction CHAPTER 1: Damned If I Do, Damned If I Don’t CHAPTER 2: Colares CHAPTER 3: A Reluctant Warrior CHAPTER 4: The Secrets Within CHAPTER 5: Writing on the Wall CHAPTER 6: Orbs CHAPTER 7: The Tic Tac CHAPTER 8: Angels or Demons CHAPTER 9: Into the Void CHAPTER 10: The Secret in Their Brains CHAPTER 11: Biological Remains CHAPTER 12: The Observables CHAPTER 13: Where the Evidence Lies CHAPTER 14: Searching for Breakthroughs CHAPTER 15: USS Roosevelt CHAPTER 16: The “Aha” Moment CHAPTER 17: What Now? CHAPTER 18: The 800-Pound Gorilla CHAPTER 19: . . . And the Horse You Rode In On CHAPTER 20: The Three Heads of Cerberus CHAPTER 21: Out of the Airlock CHAPTER 22: All the Small Things CHAPTER 23: The War Plan CHAPTER 24: The Next Level of Disclosure CHAPTER 25: New Horizons Acknowledgments Appendix Index Photos', 'https://archive.org/services/img/imminent-inside-the-pentagons-hunt-for-ufos-2024-luis-elizondo', 'https://archive.org/details/imminent-inside-the-pentagons-hunt-for-ufos-2024-luis-elizondo', 'internet-archive:imminent-inside-the-pentagons-hunt-for-ufos-2024-luis-elizondo'),
