  ('441397203577216105', 'Iran 2026 The Pivot Of World History Assaulted By The Barbarians Of The West I', 'Muhammad Shamsaddin Megalommatis', 2026, 'History', 'Time to win the Empire or lose the State Secular Governance is invariably the Quintessence of all Iranian and Islamic Empires Contents I. Iran: the Pivot of World History II. Falsehood Diffused, Heinous Acts Performed, and Intentional Destruction of Mankind Undertaken by the Western Colonials III. Iran & Aniran or Center & Periphery or Truth & Lie: a 2600-year Long History A. Achaemenid Zoroastrianism vs. Mithraism: Caesaropapism vs. Papo-Caesarism or Monotheism vs. Polytheism B. Alexander the Great as Macedonian King, Egyptian Pharaoh, and Iranian Emperor: a Monotheist against Mithraism C. The Division of Iran among the Arsacid Parthians and the Diadochi D. The ''Imperium Romanum'' and the Greco-Roman Civilization: a Barbarous Pseudo-Empire and a Divisive, Worthless Legacy E. The Orientalization of the Roman Empire -and of the West in general F. Manichaeism and Mani, the Greatest Man of All Times G. Kartir, the Eradication of Manichaeism in Iran, and its Prevalence in the Roman Empire H. Why the Roman Elite imposed the Composite -Memphitic Egyptian & Mithraic Iranian- Dogma of ''Christianity'' instead of Manichaeism I. Islam and the Mythologization of the so-called ''Arab Conquests'' J. The Falsehood of the Western Orientalists about Islam, Christianity, and the Use of Force in the Diffusion/Imposition of a Religion K. The Falsehood of the Western Orientalists about the Arrival of Islam in Iran IV. The Irrevocable, Overwhelming and Infinite Iranization of Islam in Asia and Europe, and the Attempt of Unification of Christianity and Islam A. Bayt al Hikmah: the incorporation of all scientific, academic and intellectual schools and traditions into a unified, universal, original, and exemplar house of sciences B. The inevitable return of Iran: the useless and fake Islamic Caliphate ultimately supplanted by the Iranianates (wrongly named ''Persianates'') C. The Iranization of all Turanians, Slavs included, heading to the South (the So-called Indian Subcontinent) and the West (the Bogus-continent of Europe) D. The Unification of the Iranian and the Eastern Roman Worlds, and the First Barbarous Onslaught against them: the Anti-Christian Crusades IV. The Enduring, 5-century Long Western Assault on Iran V. Iran as Lighthouse to Nations at the End of Times', 'https://archive.org/services/img/iran-2026-the-pivot-of-world-history-assaulted-by-the-barbarians-of-the-west-i', 'https://archive.org/details/iran-2026-the-pivot-of-world-history-assaulted-by-the-barbarians-of-the-west-i', 'internet-archive:iran-2026-the-pivot-of-world-history-assaulted-by-the-barbarians-of-the-west-i'),
  ('502007063744988119', 'Iran, the illusion of power', 'Graham, Robert, Robert Graham', 1978, 'Economics', 'Iran, the illusion of power by Graham, Robert, Robert Graham. A economics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL120282W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL120282W-'),
  ('574467739317156518', 'Iraq, From British Mandate To Chronic Instability ( 1880 2025) Imperial Engineering And Century Long Consequences', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Calude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This comprehensive 4-part case study examines British mandate engineering in Iraq from Ottoman provinces (1880) through 2025, analyzing how imperial state formation created structural conditions for century-long instability. It documents how British officials drew boundaries to control oil and strategic routes, empowered a Sunni Arab minority to rule over the Shia Arab majority and Kurdish minority, structured oil concessions to enrich foreign companies, and built extractive institutions designed for control rather than governance—choices that generated sectarian civil war, military coups, authoritarian dictatorship, failed uprisings, American invasion, ISIS, and chronic state dysfunction persisting in 2025. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/iraq-from-british-mandate-to-chronic-instability-1880-2025-imperial-engineering-', 'https://archive.org/details/iraq-from-british-mandate-to-chronic-instability-1880-2025-imperial-engineering-', 'internet-archive:iraq-from-british-mandate-to-chronic-instability-1880-2025-imperial-engineering-'),
