  ('917163142758911086', 'Iron Flame Rebecca Yarros', 'Rebecca Yarros', 2025, 'Romance', 'The first year is when some of us lose our lives. The second year is when the rest of us lose our humanity.” —Xaden Riorson Everyone expected Violet Sorrengail to die during her first year at Basgiath War College—Violet included. But Threshing was only the first impossible test meant to weed out the weak-willed, the unworthy, and the unlucky. Now the real training begins, and Violet’s already wondering how she’ll get through. It’s not just that it’s grueling and maliciously brutal, or even that it’s designed to stretch the riders’ capacity for pain beyond endurance. It’s the new vice commandant, who’s made it his personal mission to teach Violet exactly how powerless she is–unless she betrays the man she loves. Although Violet’s body might be weaker and frailer than everyone else’s, she still has her wits—and a will of iron. And leadership is forgetting the most important lesson Basgiath has taught her: Dragon riders make their own rules. But a determination to survive won’t be enough this year. Because Violet knows the real secret hidden for centuries at Basgiath War College—and nothing, not even dragon fire, may be enough to save them in the end.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/iron-flame-rebecca-yarros_202507', 'https://archive.org/details/iron-flame-rebecca-yarros_202507', 'internet-archive:iron-flame-rebecca-yarros_202507'),
  ('976100872370412995', 'Iron man', 'Tony Iommi, TONY IOMMI, Tommy Iommi', 2011, 'Music', 'Iron man by Tony Iommi, TONY IOMMI, Tommy Iommi. A music book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16475399W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL16475399W-'),
  ('500744672780354275', 'Iron man', 'Tony Iommi, TONY IOMMI, Tommy Iommi', 2011, 'Music', 'Iron man by Tony Iommi, TONY IOMMI, Tommy Iommi', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10662505-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16475399W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL16475399W'),
  ('285321585661291236', 'Iron Smelters in India: From Tradition to Industry', 'Savio Pereira', 2026, 'History', 'This presentation is based on the Class 8 NCERT History textbook chapter that explores India’s iron smelting tradition. It traces the journey from ancient craftsmanship to colonial decline, highlighting communities like the Agarias and the impact of British forest laws, taxes, and imports. It also covers the rise of Tata Steel in 1907, marking India’s industrial transformation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/iron-smelters', 'https://archive.org/details/iron-smelters', 'internet-archive:iron-smelters'),
  ('977117856022049829', 'Iron Transformation And Phosphorus Reten', 'Kase Branham', 2026, 'Science', 'Amazonian Dark Earth (ADE, terra preta) maintains fertility for centuries to millennia in ferralsol that exhausts within years. We propose that this persistence arises from a multi-factorial reactor in which ash raises pH, driving iron reduction and transformation on a persistent biochar scaffold, which both immobilizes iron and maintains phosphorus in desorbable form. We test this model through comprehensive reanalysis of the Schmidt et al. (2023) geochemical dataset (3,689 samples, 67 variables) and the de Freitas et al. (2023) 16S amplicon dataset (44 samples, 21,470 ASVs). Three previously unrecognized geochemical patterns emerge. First, ADE’s electrical conductivity correlates with magnetic susceptibility (ρ=+0.892) but not organic carbon (ρ=+0.093, n.s.)—a mineralogical rather than carbon-based signature. Second, iron displays a divergent fate: unchanged in total (1.02×), depleted in exchangeable form (0.25×), enriched in magnetic form (3.1×)—consistent with in-situ transformation to ferrimagnetic phases, while manganese and zinc accumulate as bioavailable nutrients. Third, pH is the dominant driver: mediation analysis shows magnetic susceptibility mediates 90% of pH’s effect on conductivity. ADE retains 37% of total P in available form versus 1% in background—a 37× difference in retention efficiency that represents a kinetic triumph, changing the soil’s relationship with phosphorus from irreversible fixation to reversible retention. Independent microbial evidence converges on the same mechanism. The obligate iron reducer Anaeromyxobacter is significantly depleted in ADE (ρ=–0.655, p=1.5×10–5), consistent with exhaustion of bioavailable Fe(III) substrate, while the P-solubilizer Paenibacillus is enriched 2.6× in bulk ADE. Phylum-level community shifts independently identify pH as the primary driver. Published Mössbauer spectroscopy and XRD have identified maghemite in ADE soil at an independent site; dual-frequency susceptibility identifies magnetite and superparamagnetic maghemite in ADE clay fractions at a second site. Five alternative hypotheses for magnetic enrichment are systematically tested and eliminated. No single component—biochar, lime, or compost alone—replicates terra preta’s properties, because no single intervention provides all three reactor components simultaneously', 'https://archive.org/services/img/iron-transformation-and-phosphorus-reten', 'https://archive.org/details/iron-transformation-and-phosphorus-reten', 'internet-archive:iron-transformation-and-phosphorus-reten'),
