  ('1130509819140178214', 'James Michael Curley Scrapbook', 'Unknown', 2025, 'Biography', 'This volume is one of a series of notebooks of news clippings about the political career and personal life of James Michael Curley. The collection spans the years between 1913 and 1937. This volume includes clippings from 1930s.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v18', 'https://archive.org/details/JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v18', 'internet-archive:JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v18'),
  ('178665497558533784', 'James Michael Curley Scrapbook', 'Unknown', 2026, 'Biography', 'This volume is one of a series of notebooks of news clippings about the political career and personal life of James Michael Curley. The collection spans the years between 1913 and 1937. This volume includes clippings from 1930s. It focuses on the funeral of Mrs. Curley.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v28', 'https://archive.org/details/JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v28', 'internet-archive:JamesMichaelCurleyScrapbook-v28'),
  ('921220988790189193', 'James Ossuary Forensic Breakdown', 'The Governor / Kingdom Records', 2026, 'History', 'Section I: Executive Summary Official forensic report under Protocol 422 authenticating the James Ossuary . This document establishes the statistical bridge between 1st-century Jerusalem demographics and the New Testament record. Section II: Hardware (The Evidence) Analysis of the James Ossuary inscription ("James, son of Joseph, brother of Jesus"). Verification of the Biopitting and Patina consistency through the Camil Fuchs Statistical Model , establishing a 95% statistical certainty. Section III: Software (The Word/Numerical) Alignment of the "Brother of Jesus" descriptor with the 1611 KJV lineage. Calculation of Name Density and Population Probability to prove the astronomical odds against this being any other "James." Section IV: The Verdict The artifact is certified as an Atomic Anchor . The forensic and mathematical witnesses achieve a 1:1 Forensic Lock with the biblical record. GLORY TO GOD ALMIGHTY. JESUS CHRIST IS LORD. SOLI DEO GLORIA.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/james-ossuary-forensic-breakdown', 'https://archive.org/details/james-ossuary-forensic-breakdown', 'internet-archive:james-ossuary-forensic-breakdown'),
