  ('454926686562675599', 'Jataka 13 24 Path Of Redeemed Time Giuseppe Gugliotta', 'Giuseppe Gugliotta', 2026, 'History', 'Synthetic Map of Jātaka 13–24 Axis of disenchantment, exposure, and exit from sacrificial logic Station I – Innocence that believes Jātaka 13–14 Theme : good intentions producing harm Function : dismantling moral innocence Contribution : harm does not require malice 👉 The myth of moral purity collapses. Station II – Merit as deception Jātaka 15–16 Theme : accumulation of merit, virtuous acts with perverse effects Function : exposing the accounting logic of the sacred Contribution : good treated as credit creates debt 👉 Moral economy emerges as power. Station III – The vow that binds Jātaka 17 Theme : religious vows as self-imposed imprisonment Function : revealing sacred obligation as fixation Contribution : blind obedience sustains the cycle 👉 The sacred appears as an inescapable contract. Station IV – Sacrifice unmasked Jātaka 18–19 18. Matakabhatta-Jātaka The goat who laughs and weeps Sacrifice perpetuates violence Laughter marks the end of the cycle; tears mourn false salvation 19. Āyācitabhatta-Jātaka Sacrifice to gain release that does not release Offering to escape a vow prolongs bondage 👉 Here sacrificial logic collapses: no blood liberates . Station V – Power that justifies itself Jātaka 20–21 Theme : moral and religious authority self-legitimizing Function : showing how power survives through “good” Contribution : violence becomes “necessary” 👉 Babylon has not fallen yet—it rationalizes itself. Station VI – Compassion that wounds Jātaka 22–23 Theme : misguided compassion, harmful salvation Function : critique of interventionist ethics Contribution : not all help is liberation 👉 The myth of altruistic salvation collapses. Station VII – The remainder without redemption Jātaka 24 Theme : silent exit from the cycle without triumph Function : liberation without reward Contribution : release is not compensation 👉 What remains is a posture: no sacrifice, no promise', 'https://archive.org/services/img/jataka-13-24-path-of-redeemed-time-giuseppe-gugliotta', 'https://archive.org/details/jataka-13-24-path-of-redeemed-time-giuseppe-gugliotta', 'internet-archive:jataka-13-24-path-of-redeemed-time-giuseppe-gugliotta'),
  ('55827296065138625', 'Jazz', 'Toni Morrison', 1992, 'Historical Fiction', 'Jazz by Toni Morrison. A historical fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL50563W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL50563W-'),
  ('181196679125450117', 'Jazz', 'Toni Morrison', 1992, 'Historical Fiction', 'Jazz by Toni Morrison', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9317239-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL50563W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL50563W'),
  ('578066842926502810', 'Jazz Academy Original Story', 'Jadden Couture', 2026, 'new orleans', 'Jazz Academy is a soul-stirring narrative written by Jadden Couture that follows the journey of Gordon Brown Goldstein , a New Orleans native who brings the rhythmic heart of the Crescent City to the rigid halls of George Vancouver Preparatory in Toronto . Stepping in as a substitute teacher, Gordon discovers a classroom of students bound by strict academic standards but yearning for creative expression . By drawing parallels between the mathematics of music and traditional curriculum, Gordon secretly assembles a jazz ensemble—the "Jazz Academy"—featuring a quartet of talented students: Maya on piano, Henry on guitar, Alice on bass, and Howard on drums . The story reaches a crescendo as the group balances the risk of expulsion by the formidable Principal Concord against the thrill of competing in a city-wide music competition against Gordon’s own rockstar roommate, Alex . Ultimately, the story is a testament to the "Wrong Note" Philosophy , illustrating how tradition and structure can harmonize with improvisation to build a community where every student finds their own unique beat .', 'https://archive.org/services/img/jazz-academy-original-story', 'https://archive.org/details/jazz-academy-original-story', 'internet-archive:jazz-academy-original-story'),
