  ('464465906188896372', 'Joan Of Arc, Sacred Figurehead And Elite Power Consolidation In The Hundred Years'' War ( 1428 1431)', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines Joan of Arc''s role in the Hundred Years'' War (1428-1431), analyzing how French elites appropriated her divine mandate narrative to legitimate Charles VII''s contested monarchy, mobilize military forces, and consolidate royal authority. It demonstrates how belief systems function as force multipliers for elite power, showing that what appeared as miraculous intervention was systematic deployment of pre-existing Catholic theology about prophecy and virgin saints to solve political legitimacy crisis through a charismatic figurehead who was ultimately disposable once her utility expired. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/joan-of-arc-sacred-figurehead-and-elite-power-consolidation-in-the-hundred-years-war-1428-1431', 'https://archive.org/details/joan-of-arc-sacred-figurehead-and-elite-power-consolidation-in-the-hundred-years-war-1428-1431', 'internet-archive:joan-of-arc-sacred-figurehead-and-elite-power-consolidation-in-the-hundred-years-war-1428-1431'),
