  ('657555353816476012', 'Kalabhairav Temple, Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh Compressed', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'History', 'This free ebook provides detailed information about the famous Kalabhairav Temple located in Ujjain, Madhya Pradesh, India. The temple is dedicated to Lord Kalabhairava, the fierce manifestation of Lord Shiva, who is regarded as the guardian deity of the sacred city of Ujjain. One of the most unusual traditions of this temple is the offering of liquor to the deity, which mysteriously disappears during the ritual. The temple has deep connections with ancient Tantric worship traditions and is closely associated with the famous Mahakaleshwar Jyotirlinga. This ebook includes information about: • Location and how to reach the temple • Legends and mythological stories associated with Kalabhairava • Temple architecture and deities • Daily rituals and special poojas • Major festivals celebrated at the temple • Spiritual significance of Kalabhairava worship • Nearby temples and tourist attractions in Ujjain • Facilities for pilgrims and useful travel information This book is intended for devotees, pilgrims, researchers, and readers interested in Indian temples and spiritual traditions. The ebook is shared freely for educational and spiritual purposes.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/kalabhairav-temple-ujjain-madhya-pradesh-compressed', 'https://archive.org/details/kalabhairav-temple-ujjain-madhya-pradesh-compressed', 'internet-archive:kalabhairav-temple-ujjain-madhya-pradesh-compressed'),
  ('188584000829824837', 'Kalki Puran', 'Maharishi Ved Vyas Shri Kalki Bal Vatika', 2020, 'Literature', 'कल्कि पुराण', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wg789', 'https://archive.org/details/wg789', 'internet-archive:wg789'),
  ('437021790477904299', 'Kallia Tsmaranika 2026', 'Kalliat Thazhathu Veedu Kshethra Samuchaya Trust,', 2026, 'History', 'Annual Souvenir of Kalliat Thazhathu Veedu Tharawad with articles on local history, memoirs, write-upsand photose', 'https://archive.org/services/img/Kalliat_Souvenir-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/Kalliat_Souvenir-2026', 'internet-archive:Kalliat_Souvenir-2026'),
  ('448053277080291140', 'Kalsi Mechanical Works and S. Nauhria Singh Kalsi – Industrial History of Ludhiana (1912–Present)', 'Kalsi Mechanical Works / Kalsi Family Archive, Kalsi Family Archive', 2026, 'History', 'Kalsi Mechanical Works was a pioneering industrial enterprise founded in 1912 in Nandpur, Ludhiana (Punjab, India) by S. Nauhria Singh Kalsi , a self-made inventor and industrialist who became one of the early founders of the hosiery and knitting machine manufacturing industry in India. This archive preserves rare historical documents, photographs, and reports relating to the founder, his inventions, and the growth of indigenous machine manufacturing in pre- and post-independence India. S. Nauhria Singh Kalsi began with minimal formal education and limited resources but went on to establish one of India’s earliest indigenous knitting machine manufacturing industries. Founded in 1912, Kalsi Mechanical Works became renowned for manufacturing hosiery and knitting machines domestically at a time when India depended heavily on imported machinery. He developed machine parts and later complete knitting machines using self-built tools and experimentation, eventually securing a patent in 1923 for his innovations. His work significantly contributed to the development of Ludhiana as a major hosiery manufacturing hub in India. Industrial Contributions: Founded Kalsi Mechanical Works in 1912 in Nandpur, Ludhiana Among early Indian manufacturers of hosiery and knitting machines. Built indigenous alternatives to imported British machinery. Helped support the growth of India’s domestic textile machinery industry. Recognized by industrial leaders and government officials of the time. The enterprise gained recognition across India and internationally, receiving visits and appreciation from political leaders, industrial experts, and global observers. Awards & Recognition: Kalsi Mechanical Works received multiple recognitions including: All India Industrial Exhibition (1935) – Certificate of Merit with Gold Medal. Indian Empire Exhibition (Lahore) – Silver Medal for hosiery machines. Government and industry appreciation for indigenous machine innovation. The factory was also visited by dignitaries including the Viceroy of India in 1935. Contents of This Archive: This digital archive contains: Historical report and documentation of Kalsi Mechanical Works. Rare photographs of factory, machinery, and visits by dignitaries. Life sketch of founder S. Nauhria Singh Kalsi. Industrial achievements and recognitions. Documentation of early Indian mechanical innovation. These materials are preserved for historical, educational, and research purposes.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/kalsimechanicalworks', 'https://archive.org/details/kalsimechanicalworks', 'internet-archive:kalsimechanicalworks'),
  ('764878898507234146', 'Kalyana Kirana Apr 2007', 'Ashok Domlur www.esahithya.com', 2026, 'Literature', 'ಕಲ್ಯಾಣ ಕಿರಣವು ಬಸವಣ್ಣನವರು ಮತ್ತು ಶರಣ ಪರಂಪರೆಯ ಉಪದೇಶಗಳಿಗೆ ಸರ್ಮಪಿತವಾದ ಕನ್ನಡ ಮಾಸಪತ್ರಿಕೆಯಾಗಿದೆ . Kalyana Kirana is a monthly kannada magazine dedicated to the teachings of Basavanna and the sharana tradition Kalyana Kirana Monthly Magazine, ಕಲ್ಯಾಣ ಕಿರಣ ಮಾಸ ಪತ್ರಿಕೆ', 'https://archive.org/services/img/kalyana-kirana-apr-2007', 'https://archive.org/details/kalyana-kirana-apr-2007', 'internet-archive:kalyana-kirana-apr-2007'),
