  ('1025440290882853329', 'KIM-1 and Commodore PET: User Manuals, Software and Books', 'Various', 2025, 'History', 'Comprehensive collection of vintage computer documentation for the KIM-1 and Commodore PET systems. Includes user manuals, programming guides, software documentation, technical references, and books covering these pioneering personal computers from the 1970s. The KIM-1 (Keyboard Input Monitor) was a single-board computer kit that introduced many users to microprocessors, while the Commodore PET (Personal Electronic Transactor) was one of the first mass-market personal computers. This archive preserves essential documentation for enthusiasts, historians, and collectors of early computing technology. Note: Each item has their own copyright owner. We do not own the rights to this material, nor does any online archive.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/kim-1-and-commodore-pet-user-manuals-software-and-books', 'https://archive.org/details/kim-1-and-commodore-pet-user-manuals-software-and-books', 'internet-archive:kim-1-and-commodore-pet-user-manuals-software-and-books'),
