  ('374636184025608842', 'Klara and the Sun', 'Kazuo Ishiguro', 2019, 'Technology', 'Klara and the Sun by Kazuo Ishiguro. A technology book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20883297W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL20883297W-'),
  ('960062804619320048', 'Klasik Türk Edebiyatında Abıhayat Hikâyesi ( Kökeni, Sembolizmi, Tahlili) Murat ASLAN', 'Murat ASLAN', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'The classical Turkish literary tradition is based on using literary metaphors to achieve original meanings (bikr-i mazmun) within a limited thematic framework and through the use of specific words. One of the metaphors accepted by this tradition is the Water of Life (Abıhayat). The Water of Life metaphor is based on Alexander''s quest for the Water of Life. This quest is recounted in Persian and Turkish Iskendername (Alexander the Great) poems. However, the foundations of the story are not in Turkish, Persian, and Arabic cultures, that is, Islamic culture; they extend to Jewish, Greek, and Sumerian cultures. Therefore, this study first focuses on the origin and development of the Water of Life story. The Water of Life story, which originated in Islamic culture and possesses four fundamental elements (Water of Life, Alexander, Khidr, Land of Darkness), was given a symbolic character by Persian and Turkish poets. The meanings symbolized by the four elements of the story reveal the way Islamic culture interprets humanity and life. This becomes even more apparent when compared to how the fountain of life, or the water of life, is depicted in Western culture. Therefore, the second aim of this study is to determine the symbolic value of the story of the water of life. From the perspective of Persian and Turkish literature, the story of the water of life and its elements are more than just symbols. Poets have widely used this story as an element of comparison and metaphor, transforming it into an allegorical figure of speech. Therefore, almost every Turkish poet has produced examples of poems using the metaphor of the elixir of life. Based on this, an attempt has been made to determine the meaning and imaginative universe of the Water of Life story in classical Turkish literature. The sample of the study consists of Iskendername poems and 125 divans selected from every period of classical Turkish literature. Content analysis, divan analysis, and commentary methods were used in the study.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/klasik-turk-edebiyatinda-abihayat-hikayesi-kokeni-sembolizmi-tahlili-murat-aslan', 'https://archive.org/details/klasik-turk-edebiyatinda-abihayat-hikayesi-kokeni-sembolizmi-tahlili-murat-aslan', 'internet-archive:klasik-turk-edebiyatinda-abihayat-hikayesi-kokeni-sembolizmi-tahlili-murat-aslan'),
