  ('371989565468652577', 'Lattice Enhanced Screening Parameterization (v 3, Final)', 'Fernando Gonzalez', 2026, 'Science', 'This document presents a closed, unit-consistent phenomenological model for lattice-enhanced screening effects in low-energy nuclear reactions within condensed matter systems. The formulation defines all variables explicitly, ensures dimensional consistency, establishes well-posed reaction-rate integrals, and closes the energy accounting without implicit sources. The model parameterizes screening via lattice coherence and loading observables, modifies barrier penetration probabilities through an effective energy shift, and provides a reproducible numerical test procedure with clear falsification criteria. The framework is observer-independent by construction and is intended for experimental and numerical evaluation under standard non-relativistic assumptions. This version (v3, Final) supersedes earlier exploratory notes by the author and represents the first fully closed, MVP-clean formulation suitable for archival reference and independent replication.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/lattice-enhanced-screening-parameterization-v-3-final', 'https://archive.org/details/lattice-enhanced-screening-parameterization-v-3-final', 'internet-archive:lattice-enhanced-screening-parameterization-v-3-final'),
