  ('905417645061047733', 'Lead Like The Babaylans', 'FUSASIS', 2026, 'History', '“Lead Like the Babaylans” is an educational and reflective presentation that explores the role of Babaylans —precolonial Filipino spiritual leaders who served as healers, mediators, and community guides. Drawing from early historical accounts by Spanish chroniclers, the material critically examines how colonial perspectives shaped and often misrepresented indigenous beliefs, gender roles, and systems of knowledge. Through a decolonial lens, the presentation reinterprets these narratives, highlighting the sophistication of Babaylan traditions, including holistic healing, ecological spirituality, and gender inclusivity. It also emphasizes the resilience of these practices despite colonial suppression. Beyond history, the work connects Babaylan values to modern leadership, encouraging individuals to embody principles of service, justice, healing, and cultural pride. Designed for academic and advocacy purposes, this resource promotes awareness of Filipino identity, indigenous wisdom, and gender equality in both historical and contemporary contexts.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/lead-like-the-babaylans', 'https://archive.org/details/lead-like-the-babaylans', 'internet-archive:lead-like-the-babaylans'),
