  ('1086878725414151768', 'Manuscript Vitran Peeq Theory Anshik', 'Anshik Pathak', 2026, 'Science', 'What if the "empty space" around us isn''t empty at all, but a dense, continuous web of energy? In this hypothesis, author Anshik Pathak introduces The Vitran-Peeq Postulate, a new theoretical framework that shifts our understanding from "particles" to a "Fundamental Source." The paper explores the existence of the Vitran Field—a universal primordial substrate—and Peeq-nodes, which are localized oscillations that serve as the precursors to all matter. Key Highlights of the Theory: The Origin of Solidity: Introduces the "Kinetic Persistence Principle," explaining how high-frequency field oscillations create the macroscopic sensation of solid objects. Anshik’s Constant (A_p): Defines a new fundamental coupling stiffness that bridges the gap between quantum oscillations and material bulk modulus. A New Look at Dark Matter: Proposes that galactic rotation anomalies are not caused by invisible particles, but by "Tension Gradients" within the Vitran Web itself. The Speed of Light: Reinterprets c as the maximum elastic response speed of the universal substrate. This work provides a logical "Root-Source" for the laws of physics, sitting beneath the Standard Model to explain what matter is truly made of at the most fundamental scale.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/manuscript-vitran-peeq-theory-anshik', 'https://archive.org/details/manuscript-vitran-peeq-theory-anshik', 'internet-archive:manuscript-vitran-peeq-theory-anshik'),
