  ('302842865175424581', 'Mata Amritanandamayi Devi, Kollam, Kerala', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'Biography', 'A richly illustrated PDF dedicated to Sri Mata Amritanandamayi Devi (Amma), the revered spiritual leader and humanitarian known worldwide as the "Hugging Saint." This document presents her early life in Parayakadavu (Kollam, Kerala), spiritual realization, core teachings on unconditional love, compassion and selfless service, and her global mission through Embracing the World. Includes detailed information about Amritapuri ashram with practical travel directions, high-quality photographs of Amma and the ashram, selected YouTube video links, and key publications from the Math. An inspiring resource for devotees, spiritual seekers, and those interested in modern saints and humanitarian work. Language: English.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/mata-amritanandamayi-devi-kollam-kerala', 'https://archive.org/details/mata-amritanandamayi-devi-kollam-kerala', 'internet-archive:mata-amritanandamayi-devi-kollam-kerala'),
  ('28390901479736', 'Material Conditions Determine Belief Systems, Why Military Victory Decides What Populations Believe', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This theoretical essay articulates a fundamental principle that belief systems follow military and political victory rather than the reverse, demonstrating how conquering elites must impose their legitimating belief systems through systematic indoctrination apparatus (education, media, law, ritual) to maintain scaled governance beyond coercion. Through detailed examination of Germany''s post-WWII division (West: liberal democracy; East: Soviet Marxism splitting exactly along occupation lines), Japan''s State Shinto collapse upon military defeat despite seeming deeply "Japanese," and Protestant-Catholic distribution mapping political victories rather than theological persuasion, the analysis proves that what populations believe reflects which elite won the last war and imposed their ideology, not organic cultural development or free marketplace of ideas. The framework synthesizes historical materialism (material base determines ideological superstructure) with elite consciousness theory (elites knowingly deploy belief systems as power tools), resolving the apparent paradox that belief is both tool of elite power AND constraint on elite action since conquering elites must maintain ideological consistency to preserve legitimacy. This theoretical essay is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which examines how elite power operates through belief infrastructure across maximum historical variation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/material-conditions-determine-belief-systems-why-military-victory-decides-what-populations-believe', 'https://archive.org/details/material-conditions-determine-belief-systems-why-military-victory-decides-what-populations-believe', 'internet-archive:material-conditions-determine-belief-systems-why-military-victory-decides-what-populations-believe'),
