  ('532500169255622022', 'Merankron, the 9 law manifesto', 'Ntirikwaamaa', 2026, 'History', 'Merankron is a manifesto outlining the philosophical and cultural foundations of Neo-Akanism , an experimental artistic and intellectual movement aimed at re-engaging Akan heritage through contemporary design, visual culture, and theory. The document proposes a framework for cultural renewal rooted in Akan cosmology, language, social structures, and material traditions while confronting the distortions created by colonial anthropology and the Western gaze. The manifesto presents a set of principles intended to guide a modern Akan renaissance across disciplines including graphic design, architecture, fashion, writing systems, and everyday objects. Rather than treating Akan culture as a static heritage to be preserved in museums, Merankron argues for an active process of reinterpretation one that integrates ancestral knowledge with modern technologies, urban realities, and global cultural exchange.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/merankron', 'https://archive.org/details/merankron', 'internet-archive:merankron'),
