  ('17329018082173498', 'Middlemarch, A Study of Provincial Life', 'Eliot, George', 2026, 'Literature', 'Middlemarch, A Study of Provincial Life is a complicated work about the lives of numerous characters in a tiny English town, with marriage, ambition, reform, and disillusionment as central themes. Dorothea Brooke and Tertius Lydgate are two characters in George Eliot''s novels that explore the conflict between idealism and social realism. The novel''s realism stems from its emphasis on moral choices, societal influence, and slow development, which depict society as an interconnected web in which human aspirations shape public outcomes. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/middlemarch_george_eliot_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/middlemarch_george_eliot_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:middlemarch_george_eliot_zebabooks'),
