  ('295443986779796524', 'MINS Cemetery 8.5 X 11 V 5 Final', 'Kelly, Dennis, Haynes, Elaine', 2026, 'History', 'A historical and civic account of the Mare Island Naval Cemetery in Vallejo, California, the oldest naval cemetery on the Pacific Coast. This volume documents its establishment in 1856, the veterans and families interred there, the decades of neglect following the closure of Mare Island Naval Shipyard, and the grassroots campaign that led to its restoration and transfer to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs in 2023. Drawing on archival research, archaeology, military history, public policy, and first-hand participation by the authors, the book examines the BRAC process, historic preservation challenges, veterans’ advocacy, and the role of community action in securing national-shrine status for the cemetery. Includes photographs, maps, headstone documentation, historical analysis, and appendices.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/mins-cemetery-8.5-x-11-v-5-final', 'https://archive.org/details/mins-cemetery-8.5-x-11-v-5-final', 'internet-archive:mins-cemetery-8.5-x-11-v-5-final'),
