  ('181139540154090660', 'Most Popular Marquee (2026)', 'Funtastic Studios', 2026, 'Literature', 'Synopsis: A student of Malcolm Lockjaw Junior High, there’s no doubt that young Marquee Newman is an aspiring student like many of her peers. However, her biggest secret isn’t anything as extraordinary as having an obsession with writing down the names of everyone in her life every day, wondering who she knows best. When the school’s cheeky queen bee, Harmony Morricone, enlists her to get aristocrats for her birthday bash in exchange to make her popular, she’ll do her best to be seen as (kinda) most popular. Written and illustrated by Ivan. Produced and released by Funtastic Studios. Initial release on March 13th, 2026. Fun(tastic) Facts: The concept for Most Popular Marquee was inspired from a YouTube retrospective of the Disney XD sitcom Pair of Kings from YouTuber Keyan Carlie, released in June 2025. The day following the video, a rough pitch was made, under the working title of “Looking For” for a 2030 release, which acted the basis for the novel you are now reading. After I was approached for pitchfest consideration in late summer 2025 at a local event I attended, I revisited the idea as my pitch. However, as I became unsatisfied with the original version and the high fee involved with submitting, it was re-realized as a full-on illustrated novel release. Due to the amount of work I had already done, I decided to fast track for a spring 2026 release. Several scenes were based on personal experiences I had around the development time, such as the molded pie scene, the discussion of deer slippers that randomly appeared at my house, and accidentally getting dropped off to the wrong bus destination that was boarding off my local city. In the first draft from late 2025, Marquee’s mother, Vermin, and Renate (then named Reane Gray) did not have physical appearances, and were only mentioned by name. This was later changed Additionally, a scene cut from the final version was showing Marquee’s desk, except that it was a "censored for copyright reasons” image of my actual desk at the time. It didn’t look as good there, and it was replaced by the scene where it shows her documents of her main method with shows. Speaking of which, said scene includes homages to various famous failed cartoon pilots, but the one that isn’t is named Naeroikathgor, which is a nod to an early username of famous Nintendo YouTuber Nathanial Bandy. The reason for it’s inclusion is that I was watching a ton of NB videos around the time, and after hearing the name in his “25 Super-Duper Nathaniel Bandy Facts” video from 2016, I thought it would be an assuming addition that people wouldn’t get. The school’s name was inspired by a mix between the protagonist of Malcolm in the Middle and the antagonist of One Battle After Another , which I had recently seen at the time of production. It was briefly considered to be named Magnolia , based on another film by Paul Thomas Anderson. In the original KCU Pitchfest pitch, Harmony’s early name was Marnia, while the scene meant to sell the pitch was a shorter version of the opening. Marquee was meant to tap her shoes during it. The scene where Marquee discusses getting grocery store samples was directly lifted from my time trying out samples at Amazon Fresh, which was near me. By coincidence, Amazon Fresh would later announce to be closing on March 13, the day of Most Popular Marquee ’s release. The initial version was around the same length as Cocofolk and the Mushroom Hourglass , which was released the previous autumn. Revisions would end up making roughly double the duration, as I felt the second half didn’t develop enough of Marquee’s objectives to please Harmony. Up until the last cut, the scenes of introducing Vermin and Harmony''s trying to make the bus stop were close-ups, which was changed mere days before release. The main characters have last names based on famous film composers. Marquee and her mother have their last names taken from the Newman family, while Harmony’s has her from Italian film composer Ennio Morricone, and Renate’s is based on Punch-Drunk Love composer Jon Brion. Additionally, Renate’s first name is a nod to Norwegian actress Renate Reinsve, who I had then been recently introduced to through her collaborations with acclaimed foreign director Joachim Trier. As a bonus, it was not until right before release I forgot to change from Renate''s original name during the part where Marquee lists the various people she has seen throughout her month. If you want to be evil, then Marquee Newman has the same initials as Michael Newman, the main character of the infamous Adam Sandler picture Click , released exactly 20 years prior. This was a major oversight and accident that was unintentional, as I only watched Click in December 2025. Vermin’s name was taken after reading trivia about Diary of a Wimpy Kid , with how Manny Heffley was considered to be named Vermin. The idea was reused for Most Popular Marquee . If you like "Most Popular Marquee", consider spreading it around to your friends and family during the spring season. It may be a good short read for them. Remember, it''s simply just fun. Follow me via Instagram (@_funtastic.tendo_ for main, @_funtastic.paradise_ for artwork, @_funtastic.studios_ for work), Twitter (@tendofun), and Blue Sky (funtastic.bsky.social) if you want to. © 2026 Funtastic Studios. All rights reserved.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/most-popular-marquee', 'https://archive.org/details/most-popular-marquee', 'internet-archive:most-popular-marquee'),
