  ('623569564063137754', 'MYSTERY OF THE LETTER 3 March 2026', 'James C. Burke', 2026, 'Mystery', 'Set in 1919-20, Myrna Levesque, along with her cousin Liz Buchanan, take on another of Chief Inspector Hennessy’s “special inquiries” (or busywork). Earlier in the year, Arthur Mallet, a local businessman, disappears without a trace after receiving a warning message from a friend of a friend unwittingly delivered by railroad employee Emma Waddell. Several months after his disappearance, amateur and professional criminals make three spectacularly unsuccessful attempts to abduct Emma. Inspector Hennessy and Sheriff Smallwood devise a devious plan to spirit her out of the county. It works well. Afterwards Myrna and Liz must prepare of report documenting the progress of the collaborative investigation between the sheriff and the railroad into the connection between Mr. Mallet’s disappearance and the attempts to abduct Miss Waddell. It had reached a dead end. Working with their friends deputies Chester Wilkes and Tom Phales, Myrna and Liz uncover a multilayered decades-long conspiracy to defraud the shareholders of a textile company. Along the way, government man Charles M. Creswell helps Myrna, and her boys foil a train robbery, and Liz escapes from bootleggers. This is the second novel in a series. See The Adventures and Antics of the Levesque Sisters https://archive.org/details/adventures-and-antics-of-the-levesque-sisters-28-january-2026', 'https://archive.org/services/img/mystery-of-the-letter-3-march-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/mystery-of-the-letter-3-march-2026', 'internet-archive:mystery-of-the-letter-3-march-2026'),
