  ('1076199250269933216', 'Neko and Nekomata - The Mysterious Cats of Japan', 'Cat Man (Booklet''s)', 2026, 'History', 'Neko and Nekomata explores the fascinating world of Japan’s mysterious cats — from the first temple guardians of ancient Buddhist monasteries to the legendary two-tailed nekomata, the beckoning Maneki-Neko, and countless folk tales in which cats protect, deceive, transform, or even speak. This booklet traces the long cultural journey of the Japanese cat: once rare and sacred, later feared as a demon creature, and eventually cherished as a beloved household companion and symbol of good fortune. Presented with atmospheric, realistic illustrations and a carefully adapted retelling of classic stories, it offers a unique glimpse into Japanese folklore, mythology, and the deep bond between people and cats. A must-read for cat lovers, folklore enthusiasts, and anyone intrigued by the magical traditions of Japan.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/neko-and-nekomata', 'https://archive.org/details/neko-and-nekomata', 'internet-archive:neko-and-nekomata'),
  ('356680173053674158', 'Nel mare ci sono i coccodrilli', 'Fabio Geda', 2010, 'Crime', 'Nel mare ci sono i coccodrilli by Fabio Geda. A crime book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16414420W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL16414420W-'),
