  ('765999207792837308', 'Neutrosophic Sociological Analysis of Educational Formation, Governance, and Management in India', 'Dr. Suman Das, Dr. Rajib Mallik, Dr. Ajoy Kanti Das, Dr. Paras Uchat, Prof. Florentin Smarandache, Mr. Bibek Mahato, Mr. Jay Raj Kumar, Mr. Vaishnev A.', 2026, 'Science', 'Neutrosophic Sociological Analysis of Educational Formation, Governance, and Management in India provides a pioneering examination of the Indian educational landscape through the lens of neutrosophic theory. Moving beyond the traditional binary frameworks—such as success versus failure or inclusion versus exclusion—this work employs a triad of Truth (T), Indeterminacy (I), and Falsity (F) to capture the nuanced, fluid, and often contradictory realities of a society as diverse as India. The book explores education as a site of negotiated meanings and contested power relations, shaped by historical legacies, social hierarchies, and contemporary global pressures. Key themes include the intersection of caste-based stratification, economic liberalization, gendered norms, and the digital divide. By integrating classical sociological theories with neutrosophic logic, the authors analyze the simultaneous presence of progressive reforms (Truth), implementation ambiguities (Indeterminacy), and persistent structural exclusions (Falsity) in policy and governance. Ultimately, the book offers a robust, interdisciplinary framework intended to bridge the gap between theoretical abstraction and empirical reality, encouraging policymakers and researchers to embrace uncertainty as an inherent and productive feature of social life.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/neutrosophic-sociological-analysis-india', 'https://archive.org/details/neutrosophic-sociological-analysis-india', 'internet-archive:neutrosophic-sociological-analysis-india'),
