  ('953841162018233278', 'Oliver Twist or, The Parish Boy''s Progress', 'Dickens, Charles', 2026, 'Literature', 'Oliver Twist tells the story of an orphan traversing the harsh world of Victorian England, shedding light on the realities of poverty, criminality, and institutional brutality. Dickens utilizes Oliver''s experiences with workhouses, criminal elements, and incompetent guardians to criticize social injustice and moral pretension. The work, which combines realism and emotional depth, juxtaposes innocence and corruption, revealing how one''s environment shapes one''s character while also calling for the power of empathy, societal transformation, and human dignity in the face of adversity. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/oliver_twist_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/oliver_twist_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:oliver_twist_charles_dickens_zebabooks'),
