  ('550080115476578044', 'Oz:mosis: An Essential Grail Curriculum; Book One: Mental Yoga, The Unity of Opposites', 'Sean Melbourne', 2026, 'Science', 'Fact: We cannot tell the difference between what is real and sovereign and what is false and corrupt without some measure of inner-peace. But, when Henry VIII ordered the heads off two wives, and ploughed through six of them in the end; dissolved and destroyed the monasteries as the national custodians of inner-peace; hacked off plenty of more heads of once-was friends; gave the court jester a repetitive kick up the ass out of pure boredom and frustration from a virtual allergy to inner-peace! Ignited the trend of global colonialism and the exploitation of unknown other races in an attempt to assuage his discontent. And, when this was all cemented in the next century with the Great Fire of London in 1666 burning down churches en mass and replacing them with banks, with the avaricious pursuit of money and profit in a rat-race world to replace God’s sovereignty on Earth…is there any wonder as to why this restless ratty existence, with no rest for the wicked has led to the smartphone today robbing us of any prospect for inner-peace, to be duped by the folly of A.I. appearing conscious and running 24/7 to grease the wheels of industry to usurp God and his natural world at an accelerated pace? Could we have taken a wrong turn during the Tudor age? I mean, are we going to slam the brakes on this runaway train of rat-race growth gathering ever more gusto toward a cliff edge on the horizon with no bridge in sight? Oz:mosis is about hitting the brakes to have a civilized break, to avoid the impending disaster of an uncivilized crippling break! Like osmosis, it aims to foster balance but to steer our train safely onto the right track of sanity for inner-peace. And the Grail is all the answer. With its divine curriculum timely poised to transcend the rat-race world of industrialization to the natural order of God’s civilization on Earth…within the grand splendour of paradise on Earth. ---Read on for more------------ I mean, look! Look at all the ungodly technologies “gone loco” with the loony tunes of A.I. appearing conscious – that is absolutely rife; global pollution and the destruction of our ecosystem – rife; a loss of national culture and identity – rife; crypto-currencies posing as the modern day coins of Caesar – rife; corruption and lies – rife; populism – rife; lawlessness and wars – becoming rife…it goes on and on. It is a slow handcart to hell! This is the modern day equivalent of what Jesus and the early Christians were up against in the face of the Roman Empire that led them to embark on the quest for the Holy Grail. And, this is practically no different than what Frodo and his Hobbit companions were up against in the face of Sauron’s All-seeing " A.Eye ", that led them to embark on a similar quest in J.R.R. Tolkien’s fantasy epic The Lord of the Rings . Although it''s not a widely known fact, the core and true teachings of Jesus relate to the Holy Grail. They are not so much concerned with the commercialization of Christianity that Emperor Constantine sought to promote, that is widely known but not completely understood. And, to truly bring to life the Grail teachings of Jesus as opposed to the drama of his life story, this book and series will aim to complete what Jesus, his apostles, and all the medieval Grail romances have strived to communicate over the millennia. Make no mistake, this book and series will seek to unravel the mysteries of the Holy Grail to give credit to the legacy of Jesus; for God’s gift of fellowship, sovereignty and kinship to become commonplace on Earth…that has been captured in the Arthurian sense in the form of the civilization of Camelot. This first book in the Oz:mosis series has been written in the style of a modern day Grail Quest Cycle, that was originally inspired by a dream I had over twenty years ago about The Wizard of Oz , that since this book’s development has paved the yellow brick road to its completion, in the theme and spirit of the original 1939 classic film.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ozmosis-book-one_202601', 'https://archive.org/details/ozmosis-book-one_202601', 'internet-archive:ozmosis-book-one_202601'),
