  ('563076235242647376', 'Palestine: A Short History, From the Roots of Zionism to Today', 'Muhammed Ilhami (Author), A. K. Kelani (Translator)', 2025, 'History', 'This essential study takes readers on a journey through Palestine’s modern and contemporary history—from the origins of Zionist ambitions to the pivotal events of late 2023. It explores Theodor Herzl’s unprecedented success, the West’s pivotal role in fostering Zionism, and the Arab world’s ongoing struggle to counter its rise. 🛡️ How did resistance movements emerge and evolve? 📜 Why did secular forces dominate at times, and how did Islamic movements reclaim leadership? ⚔️ How did Gaza endure five wars before launching a shocking large-scale offensive? With deep intellectual and political insights, this book illuminates the forces shaping the Palestinian struggle and its evolving trajectory. 🔹 A must-read for history enthusiasts, researchers, and general readers alike 🔹 Engaging, thoroughly researched, and thought-provoking 🔹 Gain a fresh perspective on one of the world’s most significant geopolitical struggles A hard copy can be purchased from: Palestine: A Short History | History Revival', 'https://archive.org/services/img/palestine_ilhami', 'https://archive.org/details/palestine_ilhami', 'internet-archive:palestine_ilhami'),
