  ('926464309393032288', 'Perkins Coie v. Trump''s DOJ', 'Judge Beryl A. Howell', 2025, 'History', 'Civil Action No. 25-716 "No American President has ever before issued executive orders like the one at issue in this lawsuit targeting a prominent law firm with adverse actions to be executed by all Executive branch agencies but, in purpose and effect, this action draws from a playbook as old as Shakespeare , who penned the phrase: The first thing we do, let’s kill all the lawyers.” ▪ U.S. District Judge Beryl A. Howell''s 102-page ruling permanently blocking an unconstitutional executive order (signed by Trump ) punishing a law firm for representing clients or causes that he dislikes . ▪ Issued on May 2nd, 2025.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/1-perkins-coie-v.-trumps-doj-05-02-2025', 'https://archive.org/details/1-perkins-coie-v.-trumps-doj-05-02-2025', 'internet-archive:1-perkins-coie-v.-trumps-doj-05-02-2025'),
