  ('1081420688982780739', 'Remember Our Castle English', 'Rijamekee Tjikuzu Veii', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'Remember our castle is a historical literary novel set in and around the abandoned castle of Gruyères. Told through the quiet, observant voice of a young girl named Sarah, the story follows a small community of displaced souls who find refuge among crumbling stone walls, candlelight, and faith. As Sarah writes daily letters to Jesus from a tower overlooking the town, strangers become family: Veronica and her daughter Elsa, the brave Candice, the mysterious Hans, and the old storyteller Matherson. Together, they form a fragile sanctuary rooted in kindness, imagination, and hope. The novel explores themes of poverty and wealth, innocence and evil, faith and doubt, storytelling, homelessness, and grace. Though darkness threatens, the story ultimately moves toward redemption, love, and restoration. This work is intentionally released into the public domain so it may be freely read, shared, recorded, and preserved.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/remember-our-castle-english', 'https://archive.org/details/remember-our-castle-english', 'internet-archive:remember-our-castle-english'),
  ('880758110118539370', 'Remembering well', 'Delys Sargeant, Anne Unkenstein', 2002, 'Self Help', 'Remembering well by Delys Sargeant, Anne Unkenstein. A self help book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL23812065W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL23812065W-'),
