  ('1008845549488554132', 'review Open Source', 'Abdeljalil Mostefaoui', 2026, 'Science', 'Open Source – Comprehensive Revision is a complete and structured study guide designed for students learning Information Technology and Open Source Software . It covers both theoretical foundations and practical applications , making it ideal for high school, university, and vocational learners. The book begins with a clear introduction to Information Technology (IT) , including hardware, software, networks, robotics, Arduino, RFID, IoT sensors, and business systems such as ERP and EDI . It then provides an in-depth exploration of the Open Source ecosystem , including Linux distributions, development tools, office software, multimedia tools, collaboration platforms, and version control systems. A major strength of this document is its exam-oriented approach . It includes: Comprehensive chapter summaries The Golden Summary for fast revision Over 60 multiple-choice questions with detailed explanations Two full practice exams A final comprehensive exam with scoring rubric Real-world scenarios such as smart farms and university projects The guide also features a powerful “Proprietary vs Open Source” comparison table (page 6), helping learners understand real software alternatives such as Photoshop vs GIMP, Microsoft Office vs LibreOffice, Zoom vs Jitsi, Windows vs Linux , and many more. This document is ideal for: IT students Open source learners Exam preparation Teachers and instructors Anyone wanting a solid foundation in modern digital technologies', 'https://archive.org/services/img/open-source_202601', 'https://archive.org/details/open-source_202601', 'internet-archive:open-source_202601'),
