  ('274147445953132006', 'Ridges On The Coin', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This theoretical paper argues for an engineering approach to institutional design that accepts hierarchy as permanent and focuses on building structural constraints against elite exploitation. Drawing on John Locke''s involvement in the Great Recoinage of 1696—where milled edges on coins made clipping structurally impossible—the paper analyzes how constitutional liberal democracy represents humanity''s most sophisticated attempt to "put ridges" on governance institutions through separation of powers, federalism, regular elections, and rights protections. It concludes by arguing that the current UN system structurally resembles the failed Articles of Confederation and explores what a ridged global constitutional framework might require. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ridges-on-the-coin', 'https://archive.org/details/ridges-on-the-coin', 'internet-archive:ridges-on-the-coin'),
  ('199204051186677314', 'Riding the Bullet', 'Stephen King', 2000, 'Horror', 'Riding the Bullet by Stephen King. A horror book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL149155W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL149155W-'),
