  ('370504847779330412', 'Silent Scream: Nosferatu, The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari, Metropolis, and Edison''s Frankenstein--Four Novels', 'C. Augustine', 2025, 'Classic Literature', 'Silent Scream is a haunting tribute to the golden age of silent horror cinema. Drawing inspiration from Nosferatu (1922), The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari (1920), and Metropolis (1927), this book reimagines the shadows, vampires, mad scientists, and twisted dreamscapes of German Expressionist film as vivid gothic fiction. Written as both homage and adaptation, Silent Scream captures the eerie atmosphere of the silent era while exploring its lasting influence on horror, science fiction, and cult cinema. Perfect for readers of gothic horror literature, classic horror adaptations, and fans of underground film culture. Preserved here on Archive.org as part of cinema and horror history, this edition is available for free reading and download worldwide.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/silent-scream-four-novels', 'https://archive.org/details/silent-scream-four-novels', 'internet-archive:silent-scream-four-novels'),
  ('725466067634714269', 'Silent Spring', 'Rachel Carson', 1962, 'Science', 'Silent Spring by Rachel Carson. A science book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1884862W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL1884862W-'),
