  ('249688740634151022', 'Smith-ereens & BC Highway Guardian Zine March 2026', 'Keegan A', 2026, 'History', 'Smith-ereens & The BC Highway Guardian is a new fanzine and historical journal about the influential English ''Indie'' Rock Band The Smiths and the history of highways in the Province of British Columbia This magazine seeks to explore the history of both the Smiths and Highways in British Columbia in a combined historical publication that can attract a varied audience of readers and bring together Smiths fans in British Columbia and around the world. In our work we hope to serve as a ''hub'' for fans of the Smiths who live in British Columbia whilst furthering knowledge keeping of information about the story of roads in the province. A lens will be shined on highway projects, music theory, song commentary, honouring people, the recording and emphasis of obscure topics and serve to record the history of both subjects in a manner to satisfy the curious. Publishing is six times a year (every two months). Eventually, we hope to take commentary or submissions from our readers. Things are still being figured out.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/march.2026.smith-ereens.record.bc.highway.guardian', 'https://archive.org/details/march.2026.smith-ereens.record.bc.highway.guardian', 'internet-archive:march.2026.smith-ereens.record.bc.highway.guardian'),
