  ('699276197657237114', 'Spy camp', 'Gibbs, Stuart, 1969-', 2013, 'Spy stories', '321 pages ; 22 cm', 'https://archive.org/services/img/spycamp0000gibb', 'https://archive.org/details/spycamp0000gibb', 'internet-archive:spycamp0000gibb'),
  ('419632918367960351', 'Spy school', 'Gibbs, Stuart, 1969-', 2012, 'Spy stories', '290 pages ; 22 cm', 'https://archive.org/services/img/spyschool0000gibb', 'https://archive.org/details/spyschool0000gibb', 'internet-archive:spyschool0000gibb'),
  ('388616715810262922', 'Spy Stories Inside The Secret World Of ISI And RAW', 'Unknown', 2025, 'History', 'These are politically tinged tropes, and in the pages that follow spies from both secret services appear altogether different, as they describe how they became (and some still are) invisible protagonists, knee-deep in chaos, a few of them becoming militant, some losing traction, others having religious and political epiphanies, some going rogue, a few becoming crazy. Many of the events they participated in are well-known outrages, but they have redrawn them in the book in intimate, and revelatory ways, shedding new light, providing fingertip context, and drawing, sometimes, contrary, and shocking, conclusions.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/spy-stories-inside-the-secret-world-of-isi-and-raw', 'https://archive.org/details/spy-stories-inside-the-secret-world-of-isi-and-raw', 'internet-archive:spy-stories-inside-the-secret-world-of-isi-and-raw'),
  ('587688023996629926', 'Sri Durgaparameshwari Temple, Mandarthi, Brahmavara Taluk, Udupi District, Karnataka', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'History', 'This is a detailed, self-compiled guide to Sri Durgaparameshwari Temple in Mandarthi, Brahmavara Taluk, Udupi District, Karnataka – a renowned Shakti worship center. The PDF covers the temple''s legendary history (including the curse of the Naga princesses and manifestation of Goddess Durga), architecture in Vijayanagara style, main deity Sri Durgaparameshwari with sub-deities, daily poojas/rituals with charges, special sevas (e.g., Ranga Pooja, Kenda Seva, Yakshagana Harake), major festivals (Navratri, Annual Jathra, Kumbha Sankramana), facilities (accommodation, annadana, guest house), donation information, nearby temples/tourist spots, budget hotels, social/cultural activities, educational institutes, road maps, photos, and YouTube video links. An essential resource for devotees, pilgrims, researchers, and tourists interested in Coastal Karnataka temples and Yakshagana traditions. Jai Sri Durgaparameshwari!', 'https://archive.org/services/img/sri-durgaparameshwari-temple-mandarthi-brahmavara-taluk-udupi-district-karnataka', 'https://archive.org/details/sri-durgaparameshwari-temple-mandarthi-brahmavara-taluk-udupi-district-karnataka', 'internet-archive:sri-durgaparameshwari-temple-mandarthi-brahmavara-taluk-udupi-district-karnataka'),
  ('535566675544117351', 'Sri Mahishamardini Temple, Neelavara, Udupi, Karnataka', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'History', 'This is a detailed informational PDF on Sri Mahishamardini Temple (also known as Neelavara Temple or Kunjar Amma Temple) located in Neelavara village, Udupi district, Karnataka, India. The ancient Shakti Peetha is dedicated to Goddess Mahishamardini (Durga in her demon-slaying form) on the banks of the sacred Seetha River. Contents include: Temple location, how to reach, contact details Historical background (Alupa, Hoysala, Vijayanagara connections) Legends (Shankachuda daughters, Galava Maharshi, Mahishasura vadha) Deity description, sub-deities &amp; architecture Daily rituals, special poojas &amp; Abhishekas Navaratri celebrations, alankaras &amp; annual Rathotsava/Jathre Annadana, accommodation (Neelarthi Yatri Nivasa), facilities Nearby attractions &amp; temples Perfect resource for devotees, pilgrims, researchers, or anyone interested in coastal Karnataka''s temple heritage. Scanned/uploaded for preservation and wider sharing among bhaktas. Jai Mata Di!', 'https://archive.org/services/img/sri-mahishamardini-temple-neelavara-udupi-karnataka', 'https://archive.org/details/sri-mahishamardini-temple-neelavara-udupi-karnataka', 'internet-archive:sri-mahishamardini-temple-neelavara-udupi-karnataka'),
  ('1140656231418916417', 'Sri Marikamba Temple, Sagara, Karnataka', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'History', 'This PDF document provides comprehensive information on Sri Marikamba Temple (also known as Doddamma Temple) located in Sagara (Sagar), Shivamogga district, Karnataka, India. It includes details on the temple''s location, history and legends (including Keladi Nayaka origins and Adi Shankaracharya connection), greatness of Goddess Marikamba Devi (fierce form of Parvati/Durga, protector against epidemics), architecture, main deity and sub-deities, daily rituals/poojas, special sevas and possible charges, major festivals like Navaratri and the triennial Marikamba Jathra (with chariot procession), facilities for devotees, nearby temples (e.g., Ikkeri, Keladi, Sigandur), tourist attractions (Jog Falls, Honnemaradu), and practical tips. Ideal for pilgrims, tourists, researchers, or devotees interested in Shakti worship in Karnataka. Scanned/uploaded for public sharing and preservation of cultural heritage. (File size approx. as per Mega link). Jai Marikamba!"', 'https://archive.org/services/img/sri-marikamba-temple-sagara-karnataka', 'https://archive.org/details/sri-marikamba-temple-sagara-karnataka', 'internet-archive:sri-marikamba-temple-sagara-karnataka'),
  ('483410518718602776', 'Sri Vinayaka Shankaranarayana Durgamba Devasthana, Nandavara, Bantwal', 'Dr. M. Thirumaleshwar', 2026, 'History', 'This is a comprehensive informational document/PDF on Sri Vinayaka Shankaranarayana Durgamba Devasthana (also known as Nandavara Temple or Nandavara Sri Kshetra), located in Nandavara village, Bantwal Taluk, Dakshina Kannada District, Karnataka, India. The temple is situated on the scenic banks of the Netravati River and is dedicated to Lord Vinayaka (Ganesha), the harmonious Shankaranarayana form (Shiva-Vishnu unity), and Goddess Durgamba. The file includes: location & address details, how to reach, phone contacts (where available), historical legends tied to ancient Nandapura/Nanda Dynasty, temple architecture, main & sub-deities, daily rituals & poojas, special sevas, major festivals (e.g., Ganesh Chaturthi, Navaratri), devotee facilities, nearby temples & attractions, budget stay options in Bantwal/Mangalore area, and other useful notes for pilgrims and visitors. Ideal resource for devotees, researchers of Tulu Nadu temple culture, tourists planning Mangalore/Bantwal visits, or anyone interested in coastal Karnataka''s spiritual heritage. Uploaded for public archival and free sharing.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/sri-vinayaka-shankaranarayana-durgamba-devasthana-nandavara-bantwal', 'https://archive.org/details/sri-vinayaka-shankaranarayana-durgamba-devasthana-nandavara-bantwal', 'internet-archive:sri-vinayaka-shankaranarayana-durgamba-devasthana-nandavara-bantwal'),
