  ('210126572994731834', 'Studies In Proverbs The Tongue', 'Reed S. Rusniak', 2026, 'Literature', 'The Book of Proverbs gives more sustained attention to the use of words than to perhaps any other subject in its pages, with well over one hundred and fifty proverbs touching on the way human beings speak to one another. This study examines that rich body of teaching under a simple but memorable framework drawn from the acronym FACTS, standing for Few, Apt, Calm, True, and Sweet. Each element illuminates a distinct dimension of wise and godly speech, and together they provide a practical, biblically grounded guide for governing the tongue in ways that honor God and serve our neighbors.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/studies-in-proverbs-the-tongue', 'https://archive.org/details/studies-in-proverbs-the-tongue', 'internet-archive:studies-in-proverbs-the-tongue'),
  ('433412483239370678', 'Studies In Proverbs: "The Righteous And The Wicked"', 'Reed S. Rusniak', 2026, 'Literature', 'Few contrasts in the Book of Proverbs receive more consistent attention than the one between the righteous and the wicked. This study examines that contrast across four dimensions: who each group is, the character they show, the actions they take, and the results they face. Using the literary technique of Hebrew parallelism, where inspired poets of Scripture highlight one truth against another, the study shows that the difference between the righteous and the wicked isn''t just about actions but about two fundamentally different heart attitudes toward God. The righteous fear the Lord and pursue what is right and just. The wicked lack this fear and mostly live to satisfy themselves. The consequences of each path, for the individual, the community, and eternity, could not be more different.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/studies-in-proverbs-the-righteous-and-the-wicked', 'https://archive.org/details/studies-in-proverbs-the-righteous-and-the-wicked', 'internet-archive:studies-in-proverbs-the-righteous-and-the-wicked'),
