  ('1071894737937014472', 'Swatantra Bharat 75 Aurovivek Amrutvel', 'Dr. Narendra Joshi', 2026, 'Science', 'The Genius of India from her luminous seed of Vedic age till date has consistently manifested through her profound Philosophy , Science, Art, Polity, Literature, Education, Technology , Judiciary, Management, Wellness, Economy, and Sociology and revealed Life as the grand vision of Spiritual unity of all that exists. She knew that the development of physical, vital, and mental aspects of life do not get their full meaning, complete significance, and decisive effect until they are rightly placed and harmoniously related to the central truth of spiritual reality. The vision of Spiritual destiny and Godward journey of each soul, and ceaseless efforts to have a practical model of unity in diversity has been the incredibly unique genius of Indian Culture. Keeping this in view various lectures and courses are designed to provide the learners with a broad overview of spiritual foundations of Indian culture along with the decisive turn it can give to the global crisis today. The acute needs and the key problems to be addressed Stupendous progress in Science, Technology, Economics and Management over the last couple of centuries has brought humanity together but it is also observed that the individuals are painfully getting isolated, families are being divided and societies are crumbling. All these point to an evolutionary crisis as human beings are not yet ready for a radical change of consciousness. It is very unfortunate that Indians are imitating the West and making futile efforts to know about themselves through the Western mind-set. The root of all Our Problems is neglecting of Self . It is essential that we explore about Self and think about our national identity. Without this identity there is no meaning of independence, nor can independence become the instrument of progress and happiness . In the words of Sri Aurobindo, ‘Either India will be rationalized and industrialized and she will be no longer India or else she will be leader in a new world phase aid by her example and cultural infiltration the new tendencies of the west and spiritualize the human race.’ ‘India must stand in the forefront of the world and solve the political, social, economical, moral problems which Europe has failed to solve, yet the pursuit of which and feverish passage from experiment to experiment it calls her progress.’ The Genius of India series and Project: Aim This project aims to develop and implement new integral and evolutionary education and training material for various domains viz. Education, Sustainability, Management, Administration and Polity, Art and Culture, Health, Development and so on, in order to train Indians and even outsiders so that they can be instruments of the next evolutionary path of the great motherland of ours. The project “India on the March” is unique in its vision, application, aim and methodology . Rooted in the past, taking all inspiration from it, the project looks at the future, to the next stage of evolution of India, and thereby finally to the evolution of mankind. By these learnings, publications, applications it aims to contribute in a humble way to the service of this great nation. The project also aims to bring out a periodical and later several volumes of research based on the above experiences as well as scholarly work. The aim is to see development of human society in the light of the evolution of consciousness since the beginning of Indian Civilizations, role of India in this and now how the redefining of the same can solve the current problems in our society. The approach to the solution: Each nation is a Shakti or power of the evolving spirit in humanity and lives by the principle which it embodies. India is the Bharata Shakti, the living energy of a great spiritual conception, and fidelity to it is the very principle of her existence. For, by its virtue alone, she has been one of the immortal nations; this alone has been the secret of her amazing persistence and perpetual force of survival and revival. (CWSA 20: 57) We will attempt to uncover the unfolding or manifestation of this living energy, the Bharata Shakti, through its various forms and names, including philosophy, religion and spirituality, sociology, science and arts. This is our humble attempt to understand the genius of India as key to crisis of the humanity through the illumining words of Swami Vivekananda and Sri Aurobindo and other seers and sages of India. The book has four parts as follows: Introduction to project Swatantra Bharat 75 ‘The genius of India as a key to the crisis of humanity’ 0 to 11 Dedication and gratitude, Purpose, Vision, Mission, Message of this project, An introductory note, Foreword by Dr Gauri Mahulikar Part 1 Part 1 : More than hundred experts expressing their views on the theme: Expert lectures 175 series: Swatantra Bharat 75 12 to 177 List of all 175 sessions: dates, speakers, subjects, YouTube links of each session are put separately in a table at the beginning of Part 2 (Page 13 to 27) Each page has details as above plus link and QR code for session and a brief introduction. Part2 Part 2: Understanding the vision of Swatantra Bharat 75 ‘The genius of India as a key to the crisis of humanity’, through luminous words of Swami Vivekananda, Sri Aurobindo, and others 178 to 318 Summary points and articles based on some of the major works of Swami Vivekananda, Sri Aurobindo, and others including Pt Deendayal Upadhyay, Nolini Kanta Gupta. Part 3 Part 3: Some samples of courses developed for different institutes and universities to take this Project theme to the next generation, especially youths. 319 to 395 Glimpses of few Courses developed on Renaissance in India and Foundations of Indian Culture, Literature, Arts, Polity, Religion and Spirituality, Rationalistic Defence of Culture, Counselling, IKS, The Vedas, etc. In different modes and pedagogies. Part 4 Part 4: An attempt of Deciphering the theme and vision, of the project and the lectures by diverse field experts, through AI Tools to create books, stories, illustrations, and panels for children 396 to 466 Samples of few storybooks, write ups, animated comic books, and illustrative panels developed using different AI tools. End pages 467 to 470 The Sun seen from Vivekananda Rock memorial, You tube channel details and QR code, Channel snapshot. Foreword excerpts Rooted in the luminous legacies of the civilizational continuum of Bharat, this project reaffirms India’s eternal vision, a vision of spiritual unity amidst diversity, of harmony between thought and action, and of an unbroken dialogue between the timeless and the timely. The “Genius of India” is not a mere heritage of the past; it is a living, evolving force that continues to guide every sphere of life, philosophy, management, science, education, polity, and art. The thematic structure of “Swatantra Bharat 75: The Genius of India as a Key to the Crisis of Humanity” connects Sanātana Dharma and Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS) to modern challenges, showing how ancient Indian thought provides holistic frameworks for societal renewal. The thematic flow moves from spiritual foundations and philosophical perspectives (Swami Vivekananda, Sri Aurobindo) to practical applications in governance, education, and global consciousness. In essence, the book’s thematic structure can be divided into three layers: A) Philosophical Vision – Exploring India’s timeless wisdom and its relevance to humanity’s existential crises. B) Applied Knowledge – Showing how Indian systems of thought can address issues in science, management, and polity, and C) Youth and Nation-building – Inspiring the new generation to embody India’s spiritual and intellectual heritage in action. For scholars, this book offers more than a historical survey. Its interdisciplinary approach and deep research highlight how Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS) address the fundamental causes of modern crises, neglect of self, aimless imitation, loss of spiritual direction, and blind imitation of the West. Evoking Sri Aurobindo’s insight, the authors remind us that without a clear national identity, independence loses meaning and becomes a hollow promise. Rationalised and industrialised, India must not merely become a facsimile of the West; rather, it is called to lead a new phase of global consciousness, to spiritualise human progress, and to offer the “next evolutionary path” for the world. This vision is supported by a rich lecture series and research collected from leading voices in philosophy, science, management, art, education, and civil society. For the youth, this book is a powerful beacon of hope and self-belief. It seeks to awaken in young minds the spirit of Swami Vivekananda, faith in oneself, faith in the nation, and faith in the divine mission of humanity. It offers practical direction through training programs, creative initiatives, expert lectures, and inspirational narratives. Above all, it reminds every young Indian that the future of the nation and the world depend on their awakened potential and fearless service. Let this book be read not merely for information but for transformation. May it ignite a renewed sense of purpose and pride in every reader, may it help us rediscover the indomitable Soul of India, undaunted, compassionate, and eternally creative, so that our independence continues not only in form but in spirit. This work urges readers, scholars, seekers, and youth alike, not just to acquire knowledge but to engage in a transformative journey. It encapsulates the quintessential spirit of India, inviting all to embody its unity, courage, and vision. As we renew our commitment to independence in our spiritual essence, may the “Soul of India” emerge resilient and creative, poised to uplift not only the nation but all of humanity. May this Amrit Mahotsava truly become a celebration of India’s eternal genius, guiding humanity towards harmony, wisdom, and light.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/swatantra-bharat-75-aurovivek-amrutvel', 'https://archive.org/details/swatantra-bharat-75-aurovivek-amrutvel', 'internet-archive:swatantra-bharat-75-aurovivek-amrutvel'),
