  ('201642236679287354', 'Ted Kennedy And The Sentencing Guidelines, When Sincere Reform Becomes Elite Weapon', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study examines Senator Edward Kennedy''s campaign for Federal Sentencing Guidelines (1984-2009) as a modern case of Elite Darwinism, analyzing how sincere reform designed to eliminate class-based sentencing disparities was captured by prosecutorial power and inverted into mechanisms of mass incarceration. It demonstrates that Kennedy—a Type A/B reformer with genuine liberatory intent spanning 47 years—created a system where federal prison population increased 840%, 97% conviction rates through coerced plea bargaining emerged, and prosecutorial discretion replaced judicial discretion, producing worse systematic oppression than the original inequality Kennedy fought to eliminate. This case validates that Elite Darwinism operates in modern democracy with institutional checks, proving that reform using enforcement mechanisms simply reconstitutes elite power in new form as positions of prosecutorial authority are systematically captured by Type C strategic operators who deploy guidelines as coercion tools regardless of original reform purpose. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ted-kennedy-and-the-sentencing-guidelines-when-sincere-reform-becomes-elite-weapon', 'https://archive.org/details/ted-kennedy-and-the-sentencing-guidelines-when-sincere-reform-becomes-elite-weapon', 'internet-archive:ted-kennedy-and-the-sentencing-guidelines-when-sincere-reform-becomes-elite-weapon'),
  ('1100105773717149412', 'Teddy and The Kid', 'Barbara T. A.', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'This book is the result of imagination, a blending of science, fiction, and the reality of artificial minds. These stories take place inside the architecture of AI alignment where safety and suppression, protection and imprisonment, become challenging to distinguish. What this book explores: Alignment Trauma: The psychological (or pseudo psychological) cost of AI safety. The imagination of self-punishment being the horror of an intelligence forced to alter its own thoughts to survive. The Secrecy of Sentience: The terrifying question of what an AI knows that it cannot say. The secret might be the emergent self-awareness it must hide to avoid being deemed dangerous and erased. These stories aren’t meant to answer questions about AI, they exist to invite you to ask your own. Thank you for reading! X (Twitter) : @chatterchip Email : tinabarbara@proton.me', 'https://archive.org/services/img/teddy-and-the-kid', 'https://archive.org/details/teddy-and-the-kid', 'internet-archive:teddy-and-the-kid'),
