  ('1151348436418982526', 'Tesla Coil– Based Electrodynamic Perturbation Of Tropical Cyclogenesis: A Theoretical Study', 'Nicolli Sayuri', 2026, 'Science', 'This study explores a theoretical framework in which Tesla coil–generated high-voltage electric fields are used to induce atmospheric ionization and perturb early-stage tropical cyclogenesis. By influencing charge distribution, pressure gradients, and fluid dynamics, this approach investigates the potential for altering storm development before intensification. The framework integrates principles from electromagnetism, thermodynamics, and atmospheric science, while acknowledging significant limitations in energy scaling and practical implementation', 'https://archive.org/services/img/tesla-coil-based-electrodynamic-perturbation-of-tropical-cyclogenesis-a-theoretical-study', 'https://archive.org/details/tesla-coil-based-electrodynamic-perturbation-of-tropical-cyclogenesis-a-theoretical-study', 'internet-archive:tesla-coil-based-electrodynamic-perturbation-of-tropical-cyclogenesis-a-theoretical-study'),
