  ('665537176101357502', 'THAT The Book Of Remembrance, Return, And Alignment 1', 'Adrianus Andrew Muganga(Ramadan)', 2026, 'Science', 'THAT: A Book of Remembrance and Return presents a philosophical and contemplative examination of reality, perception, and identity in response to modern fragmentation and existential uncertainty. The work argues that much of human confusion arises not from lack of information, but from a misinterpretation of reality rooted in the elevation of form over foundational continuity. Through a structured progression, the book diagnoses how visibility, naming, and symbolic attachment contributed to the assumption of separation, leading to fear, instability, and perpetual seeking. Drawing from convergent insights across spiritual traditions and scientific observation, the text proposes that what has been called emptiness, silence, or the Supreme is not absence, but the unformed ground within which all forms arise and dissolve. It contends that reality is whole, continuous, and without outside; nothing enters or leaves it, and no essential substance is lost through change. The work reframes creation, preservation, and dissolution as movements within a single unbroken field of existence rather than as separate acts or entities. The latter sections translate this metaphysical clarification into practical orientation, emphasizing responsibility, discipline, relational integrity, and generational accountability. Remembrance is defined not as emotional intensity or belief adoption, but as recognition of what has never been absent. Return is described not as movement through space, but as the correction of misunderstanding. The book ultimately aims not to introduce a new doctrine, but to restore clarity of perception, offering alignment with reality as it is rather than as it has been fragmented by interpretation.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/that-the-book-of-remembrance-return-and-alignment-1', 'https://archive.org/details/that-the-book-of-remembrance-return-and-alignment-1', 'internet-archive:that-the-book-of-remembrance-return-and-alignment-1'),
