  ('384324968759915939', 'The Billionaire Constrained, Elon Musk, MAGA Ideology, And The Power Of Belief Systems In Contemporary Politics', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study analyzes Elon Musk''s appropriation of MAGA ideology in 2024-2025 as a real-time demonstration of how belief systems function as power infrastructure in contemporary politics, examining how Musk''s alignment with Trump amplified his political influence exponentially before ideological constraints destroyed the relationship within six months. It documents the H-1B visa controversy and "Big Beautiful Bill" conflict to show how true believers in MAGA enforced orthodoxy against Musk when his business interests diverged from movement principles, revealing the same constraint mechanisms that operated in imperial China and medieval Europe. The case demonstrates that belief systems constrain all who appropriate them—whether cynically or genuinely—because the interpretive authority that amplifies power also limits what can be done without undermining legitimacy. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-billionaire-constrained-elon-musk-maga-ideology-and-the-power-of-belief-syst', 'https://archive.org/details/the-billionaire-constrained-elon-musk-maga-ideology-and-the-power-of-belief-syst', 'internet-archive:the-billionaire-constrained-elon-musk-maga-ideology-and-the-power-of-belief-syst'),
