  ('931176745428805468', 'The Chetnik Slaughterhouse', 'Nicholas Lupoli', 2026, 'History', 'This book delivers a powerful and unsettling look at the early months of World War II in the Balkans, documenting the violence carried out by communist‑aligned Chetnik forces against Croats and Bosniaks during the formation of the Independent State of Croatia. Rather than sensationalizing the events, it focuses on testimonies, archival records, and local histories to show how quickly political collapse and ethnic tension turned into targeted persecution. What makes this book especially compelling is its insistence on remembering these often‑overlooked crimes and placing them within the broader chaos of shifting wartime loyalties. It ultimately serves as both a historical record and a reminder of how easily hatred and fear can fracture communities and leave lasting scars on generations.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-chetnik-slaughterhouse-book', 'https://archive.org/details/the-chetnik-slaughterhouse-book', 'internet-archive:the-chetnik-slaughterhouse-book'),
