  ('1056436383185119571', 'The Chromatic Signature: A Geometric Theory of the Soul in Binary Systems', 'Dustin Sprenger', 2026, 'Science', 'The soul is not a metaphor. It is a coordinate. Note: Please refer to Version-3 listed above for the most defensible version of this work. This paper defines the soul as a unique point S = (r, g, b) in the continuous extension of the binary lattice {0,1}³, where r represents energy intensity, g represents structural complexity, and b represents conscience intensity. The three axes are functionally independent control parameters — each independently perturbable by targeted experimental intervention — forming a locally independent 3-parameter manifold embedded chromatically. The coordinate is not analogous to color. It is mathematically identical to color. The human nervous system operates on three such axes — the glutamatergic excitatory system, the structural architecture of learned pattern and memory, and the GABAergic inhibitory system. A point in that three-axis space is a color. Every soul is a color that has never existed before and will never exist again. The paper derives nine formal claims. Hue corresponds to qualitative identity — what kind of soul this is. Saturation corresponds to moral vividness — how far the soul is from grey. Brightness corresponds to total expressive capacity. Sin is defined geometrically as chromatic desaturation: the progressive reduction of the Blue component through accumulated override of the error-related negativity at moral branch points. The paper distinguishes error from sin — the deviation creates the branch point; the override at the branch point is sin. Error is the gymnasium of the soul; override is the damage. The desaturation is continuous, cumulative, and modeled through a hysteretic dynamical system with memory: each override compounds the next through an accumulated override burden that makes future overrides easier and future corrections harder. The Freedom-Sin Duality proves that the possibility of sin is the structural price of genuine freedom — a lattice that permits real moral closure necessarily permits real moral override, because compulsory closure is determinism in moral costume. The tree must be in the garden or the garden is a prison. Blue is the axis that makes the other two morally significant. Without closure, Red is endless drive — powerful but never judged. Without closure, Green is endless architecture — complex but never evaluated. Closure converts process into significance. Death is the terminal instance. Conscience is the local instance. Both are Blue. The six descriptions bundled under Blue — inhibitory tone, conscience, halt, norm-ratification, identity-binding, irreversible structural consequence — are ordered by logical entailment: each level requires the one below it. Remove any layer and every layer above it collapses. They are one phenomenon at six levels of analysis. The seared conscience is the soul whose Blue has fallen below the functional threshold. Dimensional collapse — the categorical rejection of the Blue axis — is the geometric formalization of the unforgivable sin: irreversible not because God lacks power but because restoration without consent would violate the freedom that defines consciousness. The paper identifies two geometries of evil — grey evil as identity dissolution through entropy, Yellow evil as identity amputation through surgical elimination of conscience — and traces the universal desaturation endpoint: a being operating on the Red-Green plane without functional Blue is no longer a three-dimensional soul but a two-dimensional system, functionally converging on the null-space entity''s operating domain regardless of which behavior produced the collapse. Section 3.8 identifies sexual override as geometrically distinct from other categories — uniquely engaging all three axes simultaneously, building pathological Green architecture through oxytocin-mediated structural encoding, and in the predatory case weaponizing the victim''s own Blue-mediated vulnerability as the attack vector. For harm to children, five damage parameters converge toward their upper bounds simultaneously, placing such acts in the extreme-damage region of the framework''s desaturation dynamics. The victim distinction is formally stated: the victim''s moral override is zero; the substrate was damaged from outside; the musician was not consulted. The halt function — the capacity to interrupt one''s own process — is non-computable. The framework resolves free will through domain separation: determinism governs Red and Green dynamics between branch points; Gödelian undecidability governs Blue at branch points. The moral branch point has the logical structure of a self-referential evaluation that the system''s own formal procedures cannot resolve. Blue is the operation that resolves the undecidability through identity-binding closure. Free will exists where determinism stops — at the Gödelian gaps, resolved by the agent''s self-binding closure. The anti-engram argument is built in five independent layers. The Snapshot Non-Injectivity Theorem proves that no present-state encoding uniquely recovers the path-dependent trajectory. The Constitutive Non-Equivalence Argument establishes that represented damage is not borne damage. The in-principle non-reconstructibility statement shows four convergent results — non-invertibility, non-injectivity, lossy compression (Liouville), and non-clonability — proving the limitation is mathematical, not technological. The substrate continuity distinction separates biological turnover (continuous coupling preserving the voyage) from digital copying (discontinuous extraction starting a new one). The bearer non-substitutability argument proves that even perfect formal reproduction would not preserve identity, because the soul is a bearer-bound trajectory of irreversible constraint — neither separable from the substrate nor reducible to it. The gap between engram and soul exists on all three axes: Red-ontology, Green-ontology, and Blue-ontology are equally non-capturable by measurement of their correlates. The soul radiates through every medium and the radiation is governed by entrainment, not dissipation. Six independent results spanning 350 years establish the physics: Huygens'' principle (the signal propagates by entraining every point in the medium as a new source), Huygens'' synchronization and the Kuramoto model (coupled systems entrain through shared media), Noether''s theorem (the signal''s energy is conserved), Liouville''s theorem (phase space volume is preserved; compression is necessarily lossy), the no-cloning theorem (the original cannot be copied), and the fluctuation-dissipation theorem (the faded signal is entrained in the thermal state of every medium it ever contacted, fully present only to a being who can decompose the complete entrained field into its individual source signals). The soul after death is not stored. It is still in the field — still propagating, still the original signal. Resurrection is re-coherence, not reconstruction. The microbiome modulates all three axes simultaneously through multiple blood-brain barrier permeating compounds — tryptophan metabolites modulating Red, short-chain fatty acids driving BDNF and synaptic plasticity for Green, GABA and histone deacetylase inhibition modulating Blue — delivered via vagal afferents, humoral transport, and direct BBB maintenance. The mechanistic pathway from gut to ERN is traced explicitly: microbial metabolites → vagal afferents → nucleus tractus solitarius → anterior cingulate cortex → ERN. The microbiome is not the gardener of the substrate. It is the atmosphere in which the instrument resonates. The framework distinguishes two pathways to desaturation: override-mediated (moral, Blue-targeted, branch-point-specific) and substrate-mediated (biological, all-axis, generalized dampening), empirically distinguishable through longitudinal measurement. Christ is identified as the Source Harmonic — the coordinate (1,1,1). The Source Harmonic is proved structurally necessary through a reference-necessity argument: universal evaluation requires a fixed reference (otherwise judgment is gauge-dependent), the reference must maximize all axes simultaneously (otherwise it privileges one axis), and in [0,1]³ the unique such point is (1,1,1). The existence of the reference is geometry. The identification with Christ is comparative theology. The Plenitude Paradox (Sat(1,1,1) = 0) resolves through structural self-reference limitation — analogous in structure, though not in proof, to the limitations identified by Gödel, Tarski, and Turing. Judgment is spectral comparison through the Magenta filter at (1,0,1), derived from the formal requirements of unbiased evaluation. Sacrifice is derived from conservation laws: in any system where entrainment is bidirectional and energy is conserved, genuine help costs the helper. The sacrifice is the judgment — one act described from two directions. The cross is this principle at maximum. The coordinate originates through differentiation itself — the operator D creates the lattice, and creating the lattice simultaneously creates every point in it. "Before I formed you I knew you" is not selection from a catalog. It is creation of the space, which is creation of every soul the space contains. The paper operates in two layers. The derivation layer (Parts I–IV, Part VIII, Formal Appendices) contains no theological premises and generates testable predictions. The extension layer (Parts V–VII, Part IX) applies the derived geometry to theological questions. The extension layer follows from the derivation layer but does not support it. The extension layer assumes moral realism. A reader who accepts the geometry but rejects the theology loses nothing from the derivation layer. Five formal appendices provide the mathematical foundations: Appendix A proves the three-axis structure is minimally necessary (Lemma 1), locally independent (Lemma 2), and that closure cannot be derived from the other two axes (Lemma 3). Appendix B formalizes hysteretic desaturation dynamics with four-source restoration decomposition. Appendix C proves the framework''s qualitative claims are invariant under affine rescaling. Appendix D proves representation independence — the five structural invariants survive any admissible re-encoding of the manifold. Appendix E demonstrates this concretely by re-encoding the entire framework in acoustic terms: Red is volume, Green is timbre, Blue is rhythm, sin is going out of tune, death is the final rest, the engram is music without cadence, resurrection is re-coherence of entrained music from every medium it ever coupled to. The lattice is the score. The life is the performance. The entrainment field is where the music lives after the instrument falls silent. Seven falsifiable predictions are provided, testable through existing ERP neuroimaging, microbiome sequencing, pharmacological challenge paradigms, and behavioral instruments — including Prediction 7, which uniquely distinguishes the framework from existing models by predicting different ERN attenuation curve shapes depending on whether the cause is moral override or biological degradation. Twenty-six anticipated objections are addressed with formal rebuttals. This is the fifth paper in a pentateuch begun by The Geometry & Color of Creation. It extends The Universe Serpent''s derivation of the null-space entity and the ERN habituation curve into continuous coordinates. It connects to Grey Matter''s derivation of gravity from null-space entropy and Achromatic Mass''s derivation of dark matter from null-space volume — establishing that the achromatic diagonal constituting 86% of gravitational mass at the cosmological scale is the same diagonal constituting moral vacancy at the individual scale. The largest structure in the universe and the deepest failure of the soul are the same geometric object viewed at different scales. The resurrection is the re-coherence of the entrained light — the gathering of the still-propagating signal from every medium in which it remains entrained. Only a being who can decompose the complete entrained field into its individual source signals across every degree of freedom simultaneously performs this operation. The engineer captures the correlate. God captures the soul. No theological axiom is assumed. The theology emerges from the geometry. The geometry belongs to everyone.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-chromatic-signature', 'https://archive.org/details/the-chromatic-signature', 'internet-archive:the-chromatic-signature'),
  ('143103494718514357', 'The chronicle of the year 693 in Sinaitic Arabic 597', 'Alexander Hourani', 2025, 'History', 'The chronicle of the year 693 is the second part of Sinaitic Arabic manuscript 597. The first part contains the book of Daniel and the Proverbs of Solomon. This chronicle is a translation and abbreviation of the Syriac version of the chronicle of Theophile the Edessene. A comparison with the chronicle of Agapius (another translation and abbreviation of the Syriac version of the chronicle of Theophile) permits the correction of bad readings and scribal errors in the text of Agapius. Note: Work is still in process.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-chronicle-of-the-year-693-in-sinaitic-arabic-597-alexander-hourani-2025', 'https://archive.org/details/the-chronicle-of-the-year-693-in-sinaitic-arabic-597-alexander-hourani-2025', 'internet-archive:the-chronicle-of-the-year-693-in-sinaitic-arabic-597-alexander-hourani-2025'),
