  ('92461145298190073', 'THE CODE STONE: A Functional–Computational Hypothesis for an Undeciphered Basalt Tablet', 'Sum Bunny', 2026, 'History', 'This paper presents a functional–computational analysis of the undeciphered basalt tablet discovered in 2021 near Bashplemi Lake (Dmanisi Municipality, Georgia). The artifact contains approximately sixty signs arranged in seven horizontal registers and belongs to no known script family. Rather than attempting phonetic decipherment, the study applies a structural “black box” methodology, analyzing symbol distribution, register layout, repetition patterns, and termination markers to infer functional roles. The tablet is modeled as a formal administrative device or closely related accounting instrument, encoding a procedural system for recording, converting, verifying, and sealing quantified transactions. The paper proposes that the register structure corresponds to a transactional grammar (header, roster, entries, subtotal boundary, reference table, audit, and closure), that certain repeated stroke-based signs function as candidate quantity marks within a mixed-radix system, and that distinct operator symbols delimit clauses, enforce subtotal boundaries, and mark final closure and authorization. A worked heuristic reconstruction is provided to demonstrate internal mathematical consistency, while explicitly distinguishing observation from inference and emphasizing falsifiability. Situating the artifact within the broader archaeological context of Late Bronze Age to Early Iron Age social and metallurgical expansion in the South Caucasus, the study argues that the choice of basalt implies permanent, tamper-resistant record keeping comparable in function to Mesopotamian boundary stones and monumental legal inscriptions. The tablet is interpreted as terminal storage for finalized calculations performed elsewhere, rather than a working computational surface. This work is presented as a rigorous, testable hypothesis intended to contribute to debates on the origins of writing, early accounting systems, administrative technologies, and the evolution of formal symbolic notation prior to narrative literacy.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/code-stone-sum-bunny-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/code-stone-sum-bunny-2026', 'internet-archive:code-stone-sum-bunny-2026'),
  ('796146485547283081', 'The coffin dancer', 'Jeffery Deaver', 1988, 'American Literature', 'The coffin dancer by Jeffery Deaver. A american literature book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL21754W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL21754W-'),
