  ('14156891733750297', 'The Complete Re Membering: From Kemet To Wall Street', 'NILE GREEN', 2026, 'History', 'The Complete Re-Membering: From Kemet to Wall Street is a historical, philosophical, and systems-based work that traces the fragmentation, theft, and transformation of African civilization, knowledge, and identity from ancient Kemet (Egypt) through the Middle Passage and into the foundations of modern Western power structures. Using Kemetic mythology as an encoded systems language rather than literal religion, the book interprets figures such as Osiris, ISIS, Horus, Ra, Thoth, Ma’at, and Set as functional components of an advanced computational and consciousness architecture: recursion, memory, balance, transformation, validation, and corruption. Myth is treated as portable source code—designed to preserve knowledge across generations without technology. Central themes include: Re-membering vs. dismemberment as both historical process and consciousness operation The Middle East, Middle Ages, and Middle Passage as “middle” transition zones where knowledge and people were transported, altered, and rebranded Water as memory and portal , central to both Kemetic cosmology and the transatlantic slave trade The reinterpretation of the Exodus narrative , contrasting exile with racialized, hereditary slavery The symbolic and material analysis of American power , including the dollar bill, the number 13, the eagle, Wall Street, and the African Burial Ground Capitalism as compressed human energy , extracted through slavery and built literally on buried bodies The argument that modern systems represent fire without water : destruction and rebirth without memory or restoration The book culminates in a computational reframing of Kemetic cosmology as an operating system for reality , where: Osiris represents the core system fragmented and upgraded through transformation ISIS functions as the compiler and restorer Ra is the recursive awareness loop Thoth is memory and measurement Ma’at is balance and conservation Anubis is validation and filtering Set is corruption and systemic breakdown This work is not written to persuade institutions or seek validation, but to provide a map for collective re-membering , identity restoration, and systemic balance. It positions re-membering as both a historical correction and a necessary condition for future survival.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-complete-re-membering-from-kemet-to-wall-street', 'https://archive.org/details/the-complete-re-membering-from-kemet-to-wall-street', 'internet-archive:the-complete-re-membering-from-kemet-to-wall-street'),
