  ('713813771075840879', 'The Completion of the Constitution and Federalist Papers', 'Clement, Christina Rev. Dr', 2026, 'History', 'This volume preserves Volume III of the SOLN Federalist Papers as a work of constitutional commentary and public record preservation. The text documents the formation and explanation of an independent constitutional framework grounded in record, notice, fiduciary governance, and historical continuity. It is presented in a restrained explanatory tradition, distinguishing between commentary and command, record and enforcement, and authority and recognition. Part I contains seven SOLN Federalist Papers written to clarify constitutional formation, majority protection, institutional restraint, and the role of documented record in legitimacy. These papers are offered for public understanding and scholarly examination. Part II preserves an Appendix of Record compiling primary documents, filings, notices, codes, directives, fiduciary instruments, and cultural context. All materials are reproduced without editorial alteration to ensure transparency and archival integrity. This volume is issued as a fixed record. No further commentary, revision, or interpretive expansion is intended within this edition. Any use, citation, or interpretation is left to readers, scholars, institutions, and archives according to their own standards and authorities. The work is preserved for historical reference, institutional review, and long-term access.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers', 'https://archive.org/details/the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers', 'internet-archive:the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers'),
  ('542490180504263065', 'The Completion of the Constitution and Federalist Papers', 'Rev Dr Christina Clement', 2026, 'History', 'This volume preserves Volume III of the SOLN Federalist Papers as a work of constitutional commentary and public record preservation. The text documents the formation and explanation of an independent constitutional framework grounded in record, notice, fiduciary governance, and historical continuity. It is presented in a restrained explanatory tradition, distinguishing between commentary and command, record and enforcement, and authority and recognition. Part I contains seven SOLN Federalist Papers written to clarify constitutional formation, majority protection, institutional restraint, and the role of documented record in legitimacy. These papers are offered for public understanding and scholarly examination. Part II preserves an Appendix of Record compiling primary documents, filings, notices, codes, directives, fiduciary instruments, and cultural context. All materials are reproduced without editorial alteration to ensure transparency and archival integrity. This volume is issued as a fixed record. No further commentary, revision, or interpretive expansion is intended within this edition. Any use, citation, or interpretation is left to readers, scholars, institutions, and archives according to their own standards and authorities. The work is preserved for historical reference, institutional review, and long-term access.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers_202601', 'https://archive.org/details/the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers_202601', 'internet-archive:the-completion-of-the-constitution-and-federalist-papers_202601'),
