  ('380334252600049555', 'The Coronation Machine, Joan Of Arc And The Theology Of Factional Victory', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines the Hundred Years'' War (1428–1456) through the lens of elite factional conflict, analyzing how the Armagnac coalition supporting Charles VII''s claim to the French throne deployed Joan of Arc as the mechanism for activating a pre-existing prophetic belief infrastructure — the Maid-of-Lorraine tradition and the theology of sacral coronation — to solve a specific institutional problem that military force alone could not resolve: establishing the theological legitimacy of Charles VII''s kingship against the rival legal framework of the Treaty of Troyes. It traces the full operational sequence from Joan''s institutional validation at the Poitiers commission through the Reims coronation, her capture and trial as an English counter-belief-infrastructure operation, and the 1456 rehabilitation that constructed the founding myth of the Valois monarchy in its most durable form. The case contributes three distinct analytical findings to the broader series: the single charismatic figure as the mechanism for activating pre-existing belief infrastructure, autonomous charismatic authority as an institutional management problem, and the rehabilitation process as founding myth construction documented in real time. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-coronation-machine-joan-of-arc-and-the-theology-of-factional-victory', 'https://archive.org/details/the-coronation-machine-joan-of-arc-and-the-theology-of-factional-victory', 'internet-archive:the-coronation-machine-joan-of-arc-and-the-theology-of-factional-victory'),
  ('149085240362888139', 'The Corporation', 'Dennis Mueller', 2003, 'Economics', 'The Corporation by Dennis Mueller. A economics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL8097934W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL8097934W-'),
