  ('384726026450028485', 'The Correspondent', 'Virginia Evans', 2025, 'Literary Fiction', 'The Correspondent by Virginia Evans', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/15207456-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL42414694W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL42414694W'),
  ('340405049383878430', 'The Cosmos Made Social, Brahmins, Caste, And The Most Complete Compliance Architecture In History', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This case study examines the Brahmin caste system as the most complete compliance architecture in recorded history, tracing how the karma-dharma theological framework was constructed and institutionalized across three millennia of Indian civilization from the Vedic period (c. 1500 BCE) through the post-independence era. It analyzes the specific mechanism through which the people most harmed by the social arrangement were given the most compelling available reasons to accept it — the karma-samsara framework making faithful performance of birth duties spiritually virtuous and rebellion spiritually self-destructive — alongside the Brahmin class''s absorption of the Buddhist challenge, the temple economy''s institutional construction, and the paradoxical hardening of caste under British colonial codification. The study demonstrates how an enforcement architecture embedded in daily social practice at the village level outlasted Mauryan Buddhism, the Delhi Sultanate, the Mughal empire, British colonialism, and seventy-five years of constitutional prohibition, confirming the series'' central finding that cultural practice embedded below the institutional level is the most durable form of social architecture humans have produced. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-cosmos-made-social-brahmins-caste-and-the-most-complete-compliance-architecture-in-history', 'https://archive.org/details/the-cosmos-made-social-brahmins-caste-and-the-most-complete-compliance-architecture-in-history', 'internet-archive:the-cosmos-made-social-brahmins-caste-and-the-most-complete-compliance-architecture-in-history'),
  ('363058713367361088', 'The Council of Justice', 'Edgar Wallace', 1920, 'Adventure', 'The Council of Justice by Edgar Wallace. A adventure book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1518049W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL1518049W-'),
  ('665742900681057075', 'The Council of Justice', 'Edgar Wallace', 1920, 'Adventure', 'The Council of Justice by Edgar Wallace', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/890195-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1518049W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL1518049W'),
  ('219289507772200710', 'The Counter Revolutionary, Jesus Of Nazareth As Strategic Liberator Battling Within The Narrative', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This analytical essay examines Jesus of Nazareth (c. 4 BCE - 30 CE) not as divine savior but as a counter-elite revolutionary who understood belief systems as infrastructure for power and attempted to liberate common Jews from psychological bondage by strategically battling within—rather than against—the Judean religious narrative. The analysis positions the Torah and Temple system as layered control mechanisms creating mental imprisonment through original sin (justifying perpetual toil), purity laws (requiring constant priestly mediation), and Temple sacrifices (economic extraction), then traces how Jesus systematically dismantled each component while learning from John the Baptist''s failed direct challenge. The ultimate irony: Christianity, initially a liberation theology dismantling elite religious control, was itself appropriated by new elites (Paul''s expansion, Constantine''s state religion) and reconstructed as a control mechanism mirroring the Temple system Jesus fought against, demonstrating that belief infrastructure is so powerful even attempts to dismantle it using belief as a tool ultimately reconstruct the infrastructure. This analytical essay is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , applying frameworks developed through analysis of elite power consolidation to understand Jesus as possessing elite-level consciousness deployed toward liberation rather than domination.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-counter-revolutionary-jesus-of-nazareth-as-strategic-liberator-battling-within-the-narrative', 'https://archive.org/details/the-counter-revolutionary-jesus-of-nazareth-as-strategic-liberator-battling-within-the-narrative', 'internet-archive:the-counter-revolutionary-jesus-of-nazareth-as-strategic-liberator-battling-within-the-narrative'),
  ('275975777797909859', 'The counter-revolution of science', 'Friedrich A. von Hayek', 1952, 'Economics', 'The counter-revolution of science by Friedrich A. von Hayek. A economics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1165000W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL1165000W-'),
