  ('604129031079635883', 'The Courtship of Miles Standish', 'Henry Wadsworth Longfellow', 1858, 'Poetry', 'The Courtship of Miles Standish by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8242864-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL495752W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL495752W'),
  ('1103063365751503094', 'The Craft Of Rule', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study examines elite administrative knowledge as craft expertise transmitted through apprenticeship by comparing Moses (trained in Egyptian royal court, led Exodus circa 13th century BCE) and Quintus Sertorius (educated through Roman cursus honorum, governed breakaway Hispania 80-72 BCE). It demonstrates how both figures followed identical trajectories—decades of elite imperial training, forced exile, encounter with populations lacking organizational infrastructure, transformation through application of portable administrative capacity, and legitimation via supernatural claims (burning bush versus white fawn). The critical variable separating their legacies was duration: Moses survived forty years, allowing institutions to solidify and succession to be established, while Sertorius was assassinated after eight years, causing immediate systemic collapse. The analysis reconceptualizes elite power as embodied craft mastery requiring extensive apprenticeship rather than divine inspiration or mere institutional position, revealing why organizational capacity accumulates across generations, remains portable when practitioners are displaced, and resists democratization. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-craft-of-rule', 'https://archive.org/details/the-craft-of-rule', 'internet-archive:the-craft-of-rule'),
  ('533429821260816459', 'The Crater Or Vulcan''s Peak', 'James Fenimore Cooper', 1800, 'Historical Fiction', 'The Crater Or Vulcan''s Peak by James Fenimore Cooper. A historical fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL78030W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL78030W-'),
