  ('743372970384831025', 'The Crescent Lake Cycle', 'NeoThef', 2026, 'Mystery', 'The Crescent Lake Cycle: Names That Return is a supernatural horror novel set in the small Indian town of Nainpur, where five orphan boys grow up in the shadow of an abandoned house at the edge of a dark, crescent-shaped lake. Given names and a mysterious brass locket by a kind volunteer, the boys form an unbreakable brotherhood — unaware that their names have been chosen not by chance, but by something ancient that has been waiting for them. Years later, the five men return to Crescent House with two women, intending to spend a single night and confront the place that has haunted their dreams since childhood. What follows is a night of escalating terror in which the house separates them, exploits their deepest fears and most private wounds, and forces each of them toward choices that cannot be undone. By dawn, lives have been lost, a supernatural weapon has been found and betrayed, and the sole survivor is left to carry the weight of what happened alone. But the tragedy is not an ending. It is a repetition. The brass locket, the names, and the cycle have turned before — and as the final chapters reveal, they are turning again, with a new group of five nameless boys receiving the same names in the same orphanage beside the same lake. The Crescent Lake Cycle is a slow-burning, character-driven horror novel that prioritises dread over gore and emotional devastation over spectacle. It explores themes of identity, fate, loyalty, grief, and the question of whether a cycle centuries old can finally be broken — or whether the most anyone can do is leave a door open for the next generation to walk through.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-crescent-lake-cycle', 'https://archive.org/details/the-crescent-lake-cycle', 'internet-archive:the-crescent-lake-cycle'),
  ('752940739070748214', 'The crescent moon', 'Rabindranath Tagore', 1913, 'Poetry', 'The crescent moon by Rabindranath Tagore. A poetry book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL308959W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL308959W-'),
