  ('658411315569982989', 'The death of innocence', 'John Ramsey, John Ramsey', 2000, 'True Crime', 'The death of innocence by John Ramsey, John Ramsey. A true crime book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5617327W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL5617327W-'),
  ('740453230840085949', 'The death of innocence', 'John Ramsey, John Ramsey', 2000, 'True Crime', 'The death of innocence by John Ramsey, John Ramsey', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/537398-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5617327W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL5617327W'),
  ('201709949914124406', 'The Debt And The Kingdom, Jesus Of Nazareth And The Landscape Of Oppression', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'Historical Fiction', 'This case study examines Jesus of Nazareth as a product of the specific material landscape of first-century Galilee, analyzing how triple extraction — Roman tribute, Herodian taxation, and Temple tithes — was progressively dispossessing small landowners and fishermen through a debt-to-tenancy spiral that operated through legal mechanisms rather than open violence. It highlights two key mechanisms: Jesus''s deliberate deployment of the Torah''s own radical economic provisions — the Jubilee of Leviticus 25, the debt-cancellation tradition of the prophets — against the interpretive apparatus the priestly aristocracy had used to neutralize them, and his development of dignity-preserving resistance techniques (the "Third Way") and double-coded parable speech that functioned as hidden transcript for audiences living inside the extraction system he named. The study further traces how the economic radicalism of the original teaching was systematically spiritualized and deferred through the institutionalization of Christianity, following the same domestication logic that had previously neutralized the prophetic tradition Jesus had weaponized. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-debt-and-the-kingdom-jesus-of-nazareth-and-the-landscape-of-oppression', 'https://archive.org/details/the-debt-and-the-kingdom-jesus-of-nazareth-and-the-landscape-of-oppression', 'internet-archive:the-debt-and-the-kingdom-jesus-of-nazareth-and-the-landscape-of-oppression'),
