  ('1017916802686073297', 'The Elkton Oregon House with Mary and Flora Wells', 'Jeffrey Hunt', 2026, 'History', 'This photograph shows Mary T. Wells and her sister Flora standing outside their home in Elkton, Oregon—a modest boarding house marked by a faded sign offering “Furnished Rooms.” Neither woman had children, and after their deaths, the contents of the home were passed on to extended family. Mary, the youngest daughter of one of Elkton’s earliest homesteading families, was also the family historian. She preserved letters, gathered records, and documented stories—including the 1839 journey of her mother from Prussia to the United States. The image captures more than a house; it reflects the closing chapter of a life rooted in migration, endurance, and memory. Photo mounted on board Overall dimensions: 11 × 13½ inches Image dimensions: 7½ × 9¼ inches', 'https://archive.org/services/img/elkton-house-mary-and-flora-wells', 'https://archive.org/details/elkton-house-mary-and-flora-wells', 'internet-archive:elkton-house-mary-and-flora-wells'),
