  ('786969775084896391', 'The Engineer: Follow Elon Musk on a journey from South Africa to Mars', 'Erik Nordeus', 2013, 'Biography', 'The Engineer: Follow Elon Musk on a journey from South Africa to Mars was the world''s first biography on Elon Musk. This is a book about the beginning of a journey. Elon Musk is the main person in the journey through a roller-coaster life. His journey includes everything from Winston Churchill’s adventures in British colonies to demolished sports cars. From failed marriages to German scientists escaping from the Red Army. From the oil industry to the Burning Man festival. Elon has been described as the Steve Jobs of heavy industry, as a modern version of the scientist Nikola Tesla, and as the Henry Ford of rockets. There’s a high probability that the British Secret Intelligence Service has a file on him. As the files of other James Bond villains, it describes secret rocket launches in the Pacific Ocean. But Elon doesn’t own a white cat - he’s more of a dog person. Maybe the most comparable persons are the great explorers who voyaged across the globe. They had an entrepreneurial spirit, were a little crazy, tried what no one else had tried, and thought what no one else had thought. If you want to describe the companies Elon has founded with one theme, you can say that they improve the world with the help of innovative technologies. This is exactly what our world needs.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/theengineer_201608', 'https://archive.org/details/theengineer_201608', 'internet-archive:theengineer_201608'),
  ('172919419141885012', 'The engineer''s & mechanic''s encyclopædia ..', 'Luke Hebert', 1836, 'Technology', 'The engineer''s & mechanic''s encyclopædia .. by Luke Hebert. A technology book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL235590W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL235590W-'),
  ('516779301118664165', 'The engineer''s & mechanic''s encyclopædia ..', 'Luke Hebert', 1836, 'Technology', 'The engineer''s & mechanic''s encyclopædia .. by Luke Hebert', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5737928-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL235590W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL235590W'),
  ('807477375978725163', 'The Engineered Cosmos', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This major comparative study argues that the convergent evolution of structurally identical belief infrastructures across eleven civilizations — Mesopotamia, ancient Israel, Vedic India, China, Greece, Norse/Germanic societies, Maya, Aztec, Inca, Muisca, and Hawaii — spanning 4,500 years and separated by oceans and millennia, constitutes proof that agricultural elites independently discovered the same narrow engineering solution to the same universal governance problem: sustaining large-scale surplus extraction without proportional coercion through belief systems that perform four universal mechanisms — acknowledging and demonizing alternatives to hierarchy, naturalizing hierarchy as biological or cosmic necessity, sanctifying extraction as cosmic obligation, and constructing collective threat frameworks that make organized resistance appear cosmically suicidal to the community itself. The Hawaiian kapu system serves as the decisive test case, its complete genealogical, geographic, and genetic isolation from all other civilizations eliminating cultural diffusion as explanation and confirming convergent evolution: the same operational package of divine genealogy, priestly interpretive authority, dietary prohibition encoding social hierarchy, death penalties protecting elite sacred status, and collective punishment discouraging coordinated resistance appears identically in a society that could not possibly have borrowed it. The paper traces the full trajectory from the organic animist and shamanic belief systems of pre-agricultural humanity — whose egalitarian character provided the raw spiritual capital that elite capture transformed — through the shaman-to-priest transition, the arithmetic of coercion''s unsustainable scaling costs versus belief infrastructure''s near-zero marginal replication cost, and the secularization of all four mechanisms into contemporary economic ideology, meritocratic naturalization, and market theology, concluding that the consciousness asymmetry between those who understand belief infrastructure as infrastructure and those who inhabit it as reality remains the operative mechanism of large-scale hierarchical governance in the present as in the ancient world. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-engineered-cosmos', 'https://archive.org/details/the-engineered-cosmos', 'internet-archive:the-engineered-cosmos'),
  ('121584451004448695', 'The English catalogue of books [annual]', 'Stewart, James Douglas, [from old catalog] ed', 2019, 'Literature', 'Book digitized by Google and uploaded to the Internet Archive by user tpb.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/englishcatalogu02lowgoog', 'https://archive.org/details/englishcatalogu02lowgoog', 'internet-archive:englishcatalogu02lowgoog'),
