  ('84172623865880289', 'The Garden of Evening Mists', 'Tan Twan Eng', 2011, 'Literary Fiction', 'The Garden of Evening Mists by Tan Twan Eng. A literary fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16807680W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL16807680W-'),
  ('22347010252310735', 'The Garden of Evening Mists', 'Tan Twan Eng', 2011, 'Literary Fiction', 'The Garden of Evening Mists by Tan Twan Eng', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8334888-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16807680W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL16807680W'),
  ('250621912785129715', 'The Garden Of Slowed Light The Idea In A Strange Place By Appleseed Jan', 'Appleseed Jan', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'When a particle decay experiment reveals an unexplained persistence, physicist Imani and her colleagues follow the data wherever it leads — into unsettling territory. What begins as careful scientific inquiry evolves into a deeper question: What if attention itself has measurable consequence? What if observation is not passive, but participatory? As the discovery spreads beyond the laboratory, society wrestles with its implications. Advocates of speed and defenders of patience debate the future of progress. Culture adapts. Institutions shift. Meanwhile, from a vantage point both distant and intimately near, a chamber of watchers confronts a revelation of their own: witnessing may carry responsibility. The Garden of Slowed Light: The Idea in a Strange Place is a contemplative science-fiction story about participation, accountability, and the maturation of consciousness. It does not argue for belief. It extends an invitation — to consider what might change if attention were treated not as a commodity, but as a form of care.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-garden-of-slowed-light-the-idea-in-a-strange-place-by-appleseed-jan', 'https://archive.org/details/the-garden-of-slowed-light-the-idea-in-a-strange-place-by-appleseed-jan', 'internet-archive:the-garden-of-slowed-light-the-idea-in-a-strange-place-by-appleseed-jan'),
  ('428607970789059055', 'THE GARDEN OF SYSTEMATIC ERRORS', 'Necmi Gürsakal', 2026, 'Science', 'Essays and stories about science', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-garden-of-systematic-errors', 'https://archive.org/details/the-garden-of-systematic-errors', 'internet-archive:the-garden-of-systematic-errors'),
  ('798999734431706616', 'The garden of the prophet', 'Kahlil Gibran', 1923, 'Poetry', 'The garden of the prophet by Kahlil Gibran. A poetry book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL318897W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL318897W-'),
  ('606306230161899356', 'The garden of the prophet', 'Kahlil Gibran', 1923, 'Poetry', 'The garden of the prophet by Kahlil Gibran', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/3889578-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL318897W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL318897W'),
  ('1050424123619924069', 'The Garden Of Words (Light Novel)', 'Makoto Shinkai', 2020, 'Romance', 'On rainy mornings, Takao can never bring him-self to go to school-instead, he spends that time at the beautiful Shinjuku Gyoen gardens and finds a brief reprieve from everything else in his life among the trees and flowers. And on one of those mornings, he discovers a mysterious woman named Yukino in his haven, skipping work, and an unlikely friendship blooms between them. But though these two are the center of this story, they are far from the only ones trying to find their way in life. From director Makoto Shinkai comes a deeper look at his award-winning 2013 film, The Garden of Words, full of additional scenes and perspectives to show a whole new side of the many characters who brought the film to life.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-garden-of-words', 'https://archive.org/details/the-garden-of-words', 'internet-archive:the-garden-of-words'),
