values
  ('722488049048246440', 'The Ghost Dance And Wounded Knee ( 1890), American Depoliticization And The Final Destruction Of Lakota Autonomy', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines the Ghost Dance movement of 1890 and the Wounded Knee massacre, demonstrating how the United States government deployed colonial depoliticization mechanisms identical to those used by European powers in Africa and Asia to transform Indigenous spiritual resistance into justification for violent suppression and forced assimilation. It reveals how U.S. authorities systematically erased material grievances—broken treaties, deliberate starvation through ration cuts, buffalo extermination, land confiscation, and the reservation system as concentration camps—while obsessively emphasizing supernatural elements of the Ghost Dance prophecy and Ghost Shirts to declare Lakota Sioux mentally incapable of civilization and to justify the massacre of approximately 300 men, women, and children at Wounded Knee Creek as necessary response to savage fanaticism. The study demonstrates how Wounded Knee was weaponized to accelerate the Dawes Act allotment policies that confiscated 90 million acres of Native lands, to destroy remaining tribal political autonomy, to intensify cultural genocide through boarding schools and religious suppression, and to construct permanent narratives of Native incapacity that marginalized Indigenous peoples for generations, revealing that American westward expansion was a colonial project using systematic colonial methods despite national myths about manifest destiny and democratic values. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-ghost-dance-and-wounded-knee-1890-american-depoliticization-and-the-final-de', 'https://archive.org/details/the-ghost-dance-and-wounded-knee-1890-american-depoliticization-and-the-final-de', 'internet-archive:the-ghost-dance-and-wounded-knee-1890-american-depoliticization-and-the-final-de'),
