  ('666107025340510153', 'The Glorious Revolution, Building On Infrastructure', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines how elite innovations create space for future radicalization across 250 years (1534-1815), tracing the generational ratchet from Henry VIII''s break from Rome through the Glorious Revolution (1688-1689) to the French Revolution''s attempted pure secularism. It analyzes how John Locke synthesized Greco-Roman natural law philosophy with Judeo-Christian theology to legitimate constitutional monarchy, demonstrating how each generation could push secular boundaries further because previous generations created ideological space, while revealing why the French Revolution''s attempt to eliminate Christian infrastructure failed—proving that neither path of Western dual infrastructure can be fully eliminated. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operat', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-glorious-revolution-building-on-infrastructure', 'https://archive.org/details/the-glorious-revolution-building-on-infrastructure', 'internet-archive:the-glorious-revolution-building-on-infrastructure'),
  ('515727829182823839', 'The glow in the dark book of space', 'Nicholas Harris', 2001, 'Science', 'The glow in the dark book of space by Nicholas Harris. A science book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL24208052W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL24208052W-'),
