  ('942428382153376232', 'THE HEART OF MATTER', 'DEEP JYOTI DUTTA', 2026, 'Science', 'THE HEART OF MATTER is an ambitious journey into the world of the atomic nucleus, written for readers who seek a deep understanding of nuclear physics without relying on complex mathematics . It is intended for undergraduates, curious minds, educators, and anyone fascinated by the forces that shape matter, energy, and the cosmos. This book begins at the dawn of nuclear physics, tracing the evolution of ideas from the earliest speculations about atoms to the groundbreaking discoveries of Thomson, Rutherford, and Chadwick. It explores the protons, neutrons, and the extraordinary density of the nucleus , delves into the mysterious strong force that binds it together, and explains the principles of nuclear stability, binding energy, and radioactive decay . Readers are guided through the structure of the nucleus , the mechanisms of nuclear reactions, fission, and fusion , and the principles underlying nuclear energy, reactors, and medical applications . Beyond Earth, the narrative extends to stars, supernovae, and the cosmic origin of elements , revealing how nuclear physics governs the universe on scales both vast and intimate. The book also examines the human and societal dimensions of nuclear physics: the destructive power of nuclear weapons, the ethical responsibilities of scientists, and the promise of fusion energy and climate-conscious nuclear applications . Each chapter is designed to build conceptual clarity , connecting theory with observation, history, and real-world impact. Throughout, the prose emphasizes intuition, visualization, and philosophical reflection , presenting nuclear physics as a story of discovery, responsibility, and cosmic significance. Glossaries, historical timelines, and suggested further reading provide additional layers of context, making this volume a comprehensive conceptual guide rather than a conventional technical textbook. THE HEART OF MATTER is more than a science book. It is an invitation to understand the hidden core of reality , the forces that power stars, sustain life, and define the material universe. By the final page, the reader will appreciate not only the nucleus itself, but the profound connection between matter, energy, and humanity’s place in the cosmos . This book seeks to answer timeless questions: What is matter made of? How does energy emerge from the nucleus? Why does the universe have the elements it does? And, ultimately, how should we wield the knowledge of the atom with wisdom, foresight, and responsibility? In exploring these questions, THE HEART OF MATTER bridges history, science, philosophy, and society , offering a journey that is as intellectual as it is inspiring.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-heart-of-matter', 'https://archive.org/details/the-heart-of-matter', 'internet-archive:the-heart-of-matter'),
