  ('351570817611366062', 'The influence of the climate of California upon its literature', 'James, George Wharton, 1858-1923', 2026, 'Literature', '23 p', 'https://archive.org/services/img/influenceofclima00jameiala', 'https://archive.org/details/influenceofclima00jameiala', 'internet-archive:influenceofclima00jameiala'),
  ('533270013484215949', 'The Information Asymmetry Theory Of Scaled Domination', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This theoretical paper presents the information asymmetry framework that underlies the entire "Patterns of Power" collection, explaining how small elite groups maintain control over large populations without proportional coercive capacity. The analysis examines why claims to privileged knowledge—especially divine revelation and religious prophecy—emerge as optimal mechanisms for scaled domination, analyzing patterns including the "final prophet" doctrine, systematic elimination of competing claimants, coordination between political and interpretive elites, and the transformation of liberation movements into oppressive systems. The framework applies across religious and secular contexts, from ancient theocracies through modern technocratic states, revealing structural continuities beneath apparent ideological transformations. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-information-asymmetry-theory-of-scaled-domination', 'https://archive.org/details/the-information-asymmetry-theory-of-scaled-domination', 'internet-archive:the-information-asymmetry-theory-of-scaled-domination'),
