  ('750294406198838033', 'The Kingdom Of Nothing', 'Adrianus Andrew Muganga', 2025, 'History', 'The Kingdom of Nothing: Unmasking The Prince of the World By Adrianus Andrew Muganga (Ramadan) This book is the fourth step in a spiritual revelation series that explores humanity’s struggle against deception, pride, and illusion. Written as a mix of testimony, scripture, and mystical reflection, it seeks to unmask the “Prince of the World” (Iblīs, Satan, the Adversary) and expose the traps woven throughout history and modern society. At its heart, the work argues that the adversary’s promise of “everything” — power, wealth, status, control — collapses into nothingness , while only God’s eternal love remains. Key Themes Origins of Pride : The fall of Iblīs/Azāzīl from devotion to rebellion, the refusal to bow before Adam, and the beginning of deception. The First Fractures : The temptation of Adam and Eve in Eden and Cain’s murder of Abel as the first bloodshed — patterns of pride, envy, and forgetfulness. History’s Campaign : How the adversary has moved through empires, religions, rulers, and systems of pride across time. Modern Masks : The adversary in the 21st century — governments, media, fashion, gambling, drugs, entertainment, technology, AI, and broken families. The Final Reminder : All pride-based kingdoms collapse into nothing , but in surrender and humility, humanity returns to love and freedom in God. Structure Part I — The Origins (Creation, Angels, Jinn, Humanity, Eden, Cain & Abel) Part II — The Campaign Through History (Prophets, Kings, Religions, Empires) Part III — The Masks of the Modern Age (Governments, Youth, Technology, Family, Earth, Hidden Societies) Part IV — The Final Reminder: NOTHING (The Law of Love, Humanity’s Two Paths, Eternal Return) Style & Purpose The author calls this not just a book but a mirror and revelation . It is meant to be read slowly, prayerfully, and reflectively — a spiritual journey rather than entertainment. Each chapter ends with reflections and practical lessons for resisting pride and remembering the Flame within . The ultimate purpose is freedom, not fear : to awaken readers from illusions and guide them back to the eternal truth — that nothing can separate us from God’s love.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-kingdom-of-nothing', 'https://archive.org/details/the-kingdom-of-nothing', 'internet-archive:the-kingdom-of-nothing'),
