  ('1122931231100061544', 'The Life of Anna Elizabeth Mandler Wells — Part 3 of 4: Crossing into the Unknown Umpqua', 'Mary T. Wells', 2026, 'History', 'This document is the third installment in a six-part transcription of “A Simple Sketch of the Life of Mrs. Anna Elizabeth Wells,” originally written by her daughter Mary T. Wells. It recounts the harrowing and courageous journey of the Wells family as they crossed into the Umpqua Valley during Oregon’s early settlement period. The accompanying reflection by Jeffrey Hunt identifies a family photograph from circa 1872–1875 and links it to key figures in the memoir—most notably Carolyn Wells, born in 1848 and said to be the first white child born in Lane County. The memoir details encounters with Native tribes, the hardships of homesteading, and the foundations of what would become Elkton, Oregon. The reflection provides genealogical insight and emotional context, tying historical narrative to lived memory.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/crossing-into-the-unknown-umpqua', 'https://archive.org/details/crossing-into-the-unknown-umpqua', 'internet-archive:crossing-into-the-unknown-umpqua'),
