  ('854825017588922416', 'The Mantle', 'Nikolai Gogol', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A poor clerk, Akaky Akakievich, saves obsessively to buy a new overcoat, which briefly transforms his life. When it is stolen, he is ignored by society, leading to his decline and death—followed by a haunting, symbolic revenge. Translated from Russian by Claud Field Originally published in 1842', 'https://archive.org/services/img/nikolai-gogol-the-mantle-1842', 'https://archive.org/details/nikolai-gogol-the-mantle-1842', 'internet-archive:nikolai-gogol-the-mantle-1842'),
