  ('1150728522844774438', 'The Messianic Jews Ron Cash', 'Ron Cash', 2025, 'History', 'The text explains the distinction between old and new Jews, emphasizing that true believers in spirit and truth are the spiritual Jews, not based on bloodline. It clarifies that the term "Jew" comes from the Hebrew "Yehudim," meaning "those of God," and highlights that God''s name is ''Yehu'', reflecting His people called by His name. The narrative details how the original Jews, after leaving Egypt, were called Jews after entering into a marriage covenant with God at Mount Sinai, symbolized by the tablets of stone. The old Jewish system was replaced by a spiritual one through Jesus Christ, who became the High Priest from heaven, making salvation accessible by faith rather than bloodline or temple rituals. It emphasizes that salvation is of the Jews because Jesus was the King of the Jews and the ultimate fulfillment of God''s promises. The Bible warns against false religion, traditions, and deviations from God''s commandments, urging believers to follow His laws and festivals, which foreshadow His plan and future events. The text discusses biblical festivals like Passover, Pentecost, and the Sabbath, tying them to God''s eternal plan, and stresses the importance of understanding and observing them as part of God''s culture. It also explores the end-time events, including the final judgment, the resurrection, and the coming of the new heaven and earth, suggesting that the new Jerusalem will be vast, made of precious materials, and located on Jupiter. Additionally, it delves into ancient mysteries, the significance of the Book of Enoch, and the reality of UFOs and fallen angels, linking these to biblical prophecy and the history of angels and giants. The narrative warns of spiritual deception, the importance of knowing one''s true identity in God''s plan, and the necessity of adhering strictly to God''s commandments to avoid judgment and participate in the coming kingdom. Overall, the message encourages rediscovering God''s original laws and traditions, understanding biblical symbols and festivals, and staying true to the faith as revealed through scripture, in preparation for the ultimate fulfillment of God''s plan for humanity.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-messianic-jews-2-ron-cash', 'https://archive.org/details/the-messianic-jews-2-ron-cash', 'internet-archive:the-messianic-jews-2-ron-cash'),
