  ('322081993057300292', 'The Monster''s Corner', 'Christopher Golden, Jonathan Maberry, Lauren Groff', 2011, 'Horror', 'The Monster''s Corner by Christopher Golden, Jonathan Maberry, Lauren Groff. A horror book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16450870W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL16450870W-'),
  ('738940633771185436', 'The Monstrous Feminine : Tales Of Beauty And Horror', 'Carol Soares', 2025, 'Fantasy', 'An enchanting collection of fifteen short stories of women-centric horror, fantasy and sci-fi to explore themes such as grief, sexuality, violence, family, privacy and childhood. “The Doll and Her Girl” - a forgotten doll finds true love and will do whatever it takes to keep it. “Impure” - a young woman finds herself dealing with unwanted desires. “The Returned Child” - a changeling leaves and goes home. “In The Shadows” - A princess and a ghost attend a deathbed. “Pas de Deux” - A ballerina makes a deal with a demon. “Better than Reality” - A woman goes on a date with a man who knows more about her than she expected. “Blessed” - A priest visits a woman in a cell accused of a terrible crime. “The Mermaid''s Song” - A woman survives a plane crash in the middle of the ocean and starts seeing things that may or may not be real. “Eliza & Bianca + The End of the World” - Two women travel together in an empty world. “Game Over” - The ghosts of two forgotten women watch an execution. “Just a part of me” - A girl has another person living inside her mind. “The Girl at the Piano, The Woman in the Garden” - The black sheep of a prestigious family comes back home. “Familiar Ties” - The servant of a family of vampires accompanies her young mistress to her transformation. “Taken by the light” - A woman meets angels, or at least she thinks she does. “Courage Test” - A girl decides to prove herself to the boys from her village.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-monstrous-feminine-tales-of-beauty-and-horror', 'https://archive.org/details/the-monstrous-feminine-tales-of-beauty-and-horror', 'internet-archive:the-monstrous-feminine-tales-of-beauty-and-horror'),
  ('142070801428126157', 'The Moon', 'shah latif', 2026, 'Science', 'Sachal is a curious boy who loves looking at the Moon and dreaming about the universe. With his best friend Karim, he begins a journey filled with questions, hope, and discovery. The Moon is not just in the sky — it becomes a silent guide, teaching them about courage, friendship, and believing in dreams. This story is about imagination, knowledge, and never giving up. Perfect for young readers and anyone who loves space, adventure, and meaningful stories.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-moon_202602', 'https://archive.org/details/the-moon_202602', 'internet-archive:the-moon_202602'),
