  ('639301651867852213', 'The Mystery of Edwin Drood', 'Dickens, Charles', 2026, 'Mystery', 'The Mystery of Edwin Drood explores issues of distrust, obsession, and moral decay in the seemingly respectable setting of a cathedral town. Dickens uses a rich atmosphere and psychological strain to reveal the underlying instability hidden by social decorum. The story depicts a world steeped in remorse and preoccupation, with outward appearances masking interior corruption. Despite its fragmentary state, the novel is a notable late work, representing a more gloomy shift in Dickens''s perspective and providing a disturbing examination of crime, moral responsibility, and the precarious bounds of Victorian decorum. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the_mystery_of_edwin_drood_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/the_mystery_of_edwin_drood_charles_dickens_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:the_mystery_of_edwin_drood_charles_dickens_zebabooks'),
