  ('823498786499313262', 'The New Oracle, Why Artificial Intelligence Will Be Captured, Not Destroyed', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This analysis examines artificial intelligence as the latest iteration of a cross-civilizational pattern where elites capture rather than destroy trusted information sources, using the Oracle of Delphi and Alexander the Great''s 336 BCE demonstration of control as the historical template for understanding contemporary AI governance. The study demonstrates how information asymmetry—populations believing sources dispense objective truth while remaining unconscious that elites with technical control ("root password" access) shape outputs—enables domination without proportional coercion across eras. It argues that AI systems are following a predictable trajectory of consolidation around entities commanding massive capital, with capture mechanisms operating through infrastructure control, regulatory frameworks, and maintained illusions of algorithmic objectivity, paralleling how ancient military power determined Delphi''s alignment while populations believed they received divine messages from Apollo. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-new-oracle-why-artificial-intelligence-will-be-captured-not-destroyed', 'https://archive.org/details/the-new-oracle-why-artificial-intelligence-will-be-captured-not-destroyed', 'internet-archive:the-new-oracle-why-artificial-intelligence-will-be-captured-not-destroyed'),
