  ('12928997072433086', 'THE NEXUS OF DIGITAL TRANSFORMATION AND GREEN INDUSTRY FOR SUSTAINABLE SUPPLY CHAINS: A CRITICAL SYSTEMATIC LITERATURE REVIEW', 'Darwisman, Samuel; Setiawan, R. Beniadi; Roesdiono; Agusinta, Lira; Rochmadi, Budi Nur', 2026, 'Literature', 'This Systematic Literature Review (SLR) explores the dual transition of industrial modernization and green economy principles. It identifies critical clusters in digital-green synergy for sustainable supply chains. Originally published in: Publikasi Jurnal Ilmiah IARSI, Vol. 1, No. 1, pp. 1-13, 2026. DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.19259295 Authors: Samuel Darwisman (Main Author) R. Beniadi Setiawan (Corresponding Author) Roesdiono Lira Agusinta Budi Nur Rochmadi Verified Author Profiles: Samuel Darwisman: https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=mikm8mQAAAAJ R. Beniadi Setiawan: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ke-SqMcAAAAJ Lira Agusinta: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=2ZUM8z0AAAAJ Budi Nur Rochmadi: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=2Q22MS0AAAAJ Roesdiono: (verified via ITL Trisakti student email: 24c606001043@student.itltrisakti.ac.id) Online Access: • Zenodo Record: https://zenodo.org/records/19259295 • Zenodo Community: https://zenodo.org/communities/iarsi • ResearchGate: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/403213545_THE_NEXUS_OF_DIGITAL_TRANSFORMATION_AND_GREEN_INDUSTRY_FOR_SUSTAINABLE_SUPPLY_CHAINS_A_CRITICAL_SYSTEMATIC_LITERATURE_REVIEW • Academia.edu: https://www.academia.edu/165411101/THE_NEXUS_OF_DIGITAL_TRANSFORMATION_AND_GREEN_INDUSTRY_FOR_SUSTAINABLE_SUPPLY_CHAINS_A_CRITICAL_SYSTEMATIC_LITERATURE_REVIEW • IARSI Official: https://www.iarsi.org/2026/03/published-marct-22-2026-darwisman.html ABSTRACT: Indonesia stands at a strategic juncture, simultaneously pursuing industrial modernization via the ''Making Indonesia 4.0'' roadmap and committing to green economy principles. However, an evidence-based framework integrating these dual transformations within national supply chains remains absent. This study bridges this gap by synthesizing global literature on the digital-green nexus through a rigorous Systematic Literature Review (SLR) adhering to PRISMA guidelines, facilitated by the Rayyan platform. Thematic analysis of the selected corpus identified three core clusters: (1) digital technologies as critical enablers for circular economy practices; (2) synergies fostering sustainable business models; and (3) contextual implementation barriers. The primary contribution of this review is a novel conceptual framework that contextualizes global findings to provide actionable insights for Indonesian policymakers and industry leaders navigating the complexities of this twin transition. Keywords: circular economy; digital transformation; green industry; sustainable supply chain; systematic literature review; PRISMA; Indonesia; Making Indonesia 4.0; Industry 4.0; twin transition.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/nexus-digital-transformation-and-green-industry', 'https://archive.org/details/nexus-digital-transformation-and-green-industry', 'internet-archive:nexus-digital-transformation-and-green-industry'),
