  ('1140407920993574485', 'The Noble Killer, Lothar Von Trotha And The Life Of An Aristocrat', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This biographical case study examines Prussian General Lothar von Trotha (1848-1920), architect of the Herero and Nama genocide in German South West Africa (1904-1908), analyzing how the Junker aristocratic class system produced professional killers whose violence was systematically transformed into national honor through military decorations, official histories, and carefully managed information asymmetry. It demonstrates how von Trotha''s extermination order that killed 75-85% of the Herero and Nama populations earned him Prussia''s highest military honor (the Pour le Mérite) rather than prosecution, how his methods learned in German East Africa and China''s Boxer Rebellion served as prototypes for later Nazi genocide, and how the German public was trained through institutional mechanisms to identify with aristocratic conquerors whose violence they funded but whose reality they were prevented from understanding. The study traces von Trotha''s family origins in the medieval Ostsiedlung (German eastward expansion against Slavic peoples) through his comfortable retirement, revealing how seven centuries of hereditary warrior-class privilege culminated in the first genocide of the twentieth century—celebrated as distinguished service. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-noble-killer-lothar-von-trotha-and-the-life-of-an-aristocrat', 'https://archive.org/details/the-noble-killer-lothar-von-trotha-and-the-life-of-an-aristocrat', 'internet-archive:the-noble-killer-lothar-von-trotha-and-the-life-of-an-aristocrat'),
  ('715288598373356151', 'The Nonesuch', 'Georgette Heyer', 1962, 'Romance', 'The Nonesuch by Georgette Heyer. A romance book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4092578W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL4092578W-'),
  ('919367371480895940', 'The Nonesuch', 'Georgette Heyer', 1962, 'Romance', 'The Nonesuch by Georgette Heyer', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/221924-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4092578W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL4092578W'),
  ('729475197449003297', 'The Nordic world', 'Henrik Meinander, J. A. Mangan', 1998, 'Sports', 'The Nordic world by Henrik Meinander, J. A. Mangan', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1351598-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16709378W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL16709378W'),
  ('70567523903087610', 'The Norman Conquest Of Italy And The Papal Dilemma', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study examines the Norman conquest and consolidation of power in southern Italy and Sicily (1016-1194), analyzing how landless Norman knights transformed military conquest into legitimate sovereignty through appropriation of Catholic belief infrastructure. It demonstrates the mutual dependency and ongoing conflict between Norman rulers requiring ecclesiastical legitimation and the Papacy needing Norman military protection, showing how material factors determined outcomes despite shared religious frameworks. The case reveals how belief infrastructure enables elite power to scale beyond coercive capacity and persists across regime changes. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-norman-conquest-of-italy-and-the-papal-dilemma', 'https://archive.org/details/the-norman-conquest-of-italy-and-the-papal-dilemma', 'internet-archive:the-norman-conquest-of-italy-and-the-papal-dilemma'),
