  ('768259925891434668', 'The North Wind and the Sun', 'Jean de La Fontaine', 1964, 'Short Stories', 'The North Wind and the Sun by Jean de La Fontaine', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1122711-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL50391W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL50391W'),
  ('767541079301782279', 'The North Wind''s Teeth Thanos Kalamidas', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'Mystery', 'The north wind doesn’t whisper in Lapland. It doesn’t even talk. It bites down, right through to the bone, and then it keeps chewing. It was chewing on Nils Vartia as he knelt in the snow, his reindeer-skin coat a poor shield against its malice. The aurora borealis rippled overhead, a silent, green-and-violet cathedral ceiling, indifferent to the small, ugly scene unfolding beneath it. Nils’s hands, cracked and thick as birch roots, hovered over the still form of Aurinko, his prize bull. The animal’s white coat, the colour of new snow, was marred by a patch of frozen vomit around its muzzle. Its sides, which should have been heaving with the steam of a healthy giant, were still. The eyes, usually the colour of dark, wild honey, were glazed and staring at the indifferent stars. A Killian Frank Mystery', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-north-winds-teeth-thanos-kalamidas', 'https://archive.org/details/the-north-winds-teeth-thanos-kalamidas', 'internet-archive:the-north-winds-teeth-thanos-kalamidas'),
  ('288131944408986715', 'The North-west passage by land', 'Milton, William Fitzwilliam Viscount', 1865, 'Travel', 'The North-west passage by land by Milton, William Fitzwilliam Viscount. A travel book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7321842W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL7321842W-'),
  ('424179223016062343', 'The North-west passage by land', 'Milton, William Fitzwilliam Viscount', 1865, 'Travel', 'The North-west passage by land by Milton, William Fitzwilliam Viscount', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5640721-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7321842W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL7321842W'),
  ('1096340149305690504', 'The North''s Beast', 'Bahaa', 2026, 'Literature', 'labeled as a traitor and accused of a corruption he never committed, Captain Balint is banished to the North; a desolate, isolated wilderness where specail units vanish without a trace. But the forest isn''t just a prison, it is a chamber of secrets. As Balint fights to survive the psychological traps of it, he uncovers a conspiracy that stretches from the frozen woods back to the heart of the Kingdom’s High Command', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-norths-beast-7', 'https://archive.org/details/the-norths-beast-7', 'internet-archive:the-norths-beast-7'),
  ('543623740041745009', 'The Northfield Allotments Historical & Archaeological Archive (1832–2025)', 'Simon Coleman', 2025, 'History', 'This collection is a comprehensive historical and archaeological record of Northfield Allotments in Ealing, London. Established in 1832 by Bishop Charles James Blomfield, it is recognized as London''s oldest allotment site. The archive includes research on the 1832 Bishop''s Grant, the Victorian ''Show Years,'' the impact of urban population growth, the 1972 Compulsory Purchase Order, and 21st-century heritage restoration projects. Key archaeological findings documented include Victorian grocer W.B. Hieatt bottles, Job''s Dairy artifacts, and 20th-century ''trash archaeology'' such as vintage crisp packets and milk bottles.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/00-start-here-northfield-allotment-history-summary', 'https://archive.org/details/00-start-here-northfield-allotment-history-summary', 'internet-archive:00-start-here-northfield-allotment-history-summary'),
