  ('531535267987708592', 'The Nose', 'Nikolai Gogol', 2026, 'Classic Literature', 'A bureaucrat wakes to find his nose missing, only to discover it living independently as a higher-ranking official. The absurd tale satirises social hierarchy, identity, and the irrationality embedded in everyday life. Translated from Russian by Claud Field Published in 1836', 'https://archive.org/services/img/nikolai-gogol-the-nose-1836', 'https://archive.org/details/nikolai-gogol-the-nose-1836', 'internet-archive:nikolai-gogol-the-nose-1836'),
