  ('822938519099873206', 'The Past Present Killer Thanos Kalamidas', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'Mystery', 'The cleaning woman, Marta, found her. It was six-fifteen on a Tuesday morning in November, the sky beyond the smoked-glass windows of Gallive Investments a bruised, reluctant blue. Marta had a key card for the executive floor, a privilege hard-won over fifteen years of nocturnal servitude. She liked the silence up there, the weight of money and power that settled into the carpets like a held breath. But that morning, the door to office 1407 was ajar. A sliver of absolute darkness. She pushed it, her cart of industrial polishes and vacuums a comforting anchor in the hallway. The smell hit her first, a metallic, coppery scent that cut through the lemon-scented floor cleaner. Then the light from the corridor spilled in, revealing the pale, outstretched hand on the expensive Persian rug. A detective Tiffany Carney of Växjö case.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-past-present-killer-thanos-kalamidas', 'https://archive.org/details/the-past-present-killer-thanos-kalamidas', 'internet-archive:the-past-present-killer-thanos-kalamidas'),
