  ('884541567943628303', 'The Physics of Freedom: Tuning, Choice Bandwidth, and the Width of the Future', 'Sum Bunny', 2026, 'History', 'This essay constitutes the third pillar of the Sum Bunny theoretical triad, following Geometric Non-Coercion and The Memory Escape . It introduces Choice Bandwidth as a formal stability parameter for complex systems, distinct from entropy and energy, defined as the measure of accessible future states a system can reach without collapsing. The paper argues that systems—from materials and biological organisms to economies and civilizations—undergo a process of “tuning,” in which transition costs are gradually adjusted to optimize short-term efficiency at the expense of long-term adaptability. Drawing on control theory (viability kernels), cybernetics (Ashby’s Law), evolutionary biology (canalization), and anthropology (freedom to exit), the essay defines freedom not as a metaphysical abstraction but as a physical quantity: the width of the survivable future.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/physics-of-freedom-sum-bunny-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/physics-of-freedom-sum-bunny-2026', 'internet-archive:physics-of-freedom-sum-bunny-2026'),
