  ('427068548975261403', 'The Primordial Loop: Structural Regressions in Human Sexual Behavior', 'Dustin Sprenger', 2026, 'Science', 'WARNING: This work traces human sexual behavior to its evolutionary origins in bacterial consumption, cloacal anatomy, and birth canal transit. It identifies oral-genital contact as structural cannibalism through a four-element definition satisfied by the biology. It documents the microbial, neurological, and civilizational consequences of behaviors most societies have normalized. No moral vocabulary is employed. None is needed. The mechanism is sufficient. This paper is not written for comfort. It is written for those who prefer a difficult truth to a pleasant regression. Please refer to Version-2 for the most defensible version of this work. This paper identifies three categories of human sexual behavior as structural regressions to progressively earlier stages of evolutionary and developmental history. The analysis is mechanical, not moral. No moral vocabulary is employed. The biology is sufficient. A structural operation is defined as the incorporation of conspecific biological material through a specialized opening, producing a measurable state change in the recipient. Phagocytosis is the oldest instance, approximately 2.5 billion years old. The paper demonstrates that three classes of modern sexual behavior recapitulate this primordial operation through conserved biological mechanisms. Three regressions are identified, ordered by developmental chronology. Oral-vaginal contact regresses to the birth event — the first sensory experience of extrauterine life and the founding microbiome colonization event documented by Dominguez-Bello et al. (2010). Oral-penile contact regresses to the suckling reflex — the nipple-to-penis substitution Freud identified in his study of Leonardo da Vinci, with consumed biological material satisfying the structural definition of conspecific consumption through the feeding apparatus. Anal intercourse regresses to the pre-mammalian cloaca — reversing 200 million years of mammalian anatomical differentiation that separated reproductive, urinary, and eliminative function into distinct systems. Each regression reactivates neural circuits that prefrontal inhibitory maturation — the GABAergic system''s progressive suppression of infantile erotogenic zones — should have rendered dormant. Each creates a high-bandwidth microbial transfer pathway. The closed feedback loop is derived: behavior transfers microbiome between partners; transferred microbiome produces compounds that cross the blood-brain barrier modulating drive, structural plasticity, and inhibitory tone; modified neural axes amplify drive toward repetition of the behavior. This is mechanical addiction operating at the microbial-neural interface. The paper documents domain-general cognitive degradation through six converging mechanisms: prefrontal grey matter reduction (Goldstein and Volkow, 2011), dopamine receptor downregulation (Volkow et al., 2016), sublimation energy depletion (Attwell and Laughlin, 2001), structural brain changes from visual stimulation alone (Kühn and Gallinat, 2014), systemic GABA reduction through microbial transfer, and hormonal rebalancing through prolactin-testosterone suppression. The systems these behaviors degrade are not sexually specific. They are domain-general. Degrading them in the sexual domain degrades executive function, working memory, sustained attention, creative output, and goal-directed achievement. Vaginal intercourse is formally distinguished from regression on three mechanical grounds: it is the developmental terminus rather than a reactivation of extinguished circuits; it delivers biological material to tissue evolutionarily adapted to receive it (Robertson and Sharkey, 2016); and it operates through oxytocin-dominant pair bonding rather than dopamine-dominant novelty escalation. Structural cannibalism is defined by four criteria: same species, biological material originating from within the body, incorporation through the mouth, and the material was not produced for oral consumption. The fourth criterion excludes breastfeeding — the single human biological fluid evolved for oral delivery — while retaining seminal fluid and vaginal secretions, neither of which evolved for the mouth. The structural identity with phagocytosis is exact: the operation is conserved across 2.5 billion years. Only the scale has changed. Six meta-proofs establish the structural logic beneath the regressions. The thermodynamic asymmetry proves inhibition costs energy while regression is free. The depth-chronology principle proves escalation follows the reverse order of neural architecture depth. The construction-destruction asymmetry proves that 25 years of prefrontal myelination (Miller et al., 2012) can be functionally compromised in weeks of chronic stress (Nawreen et al., 2024). The self-reinforcing cascade proves escalation is driven simultaneously by degraded inhibition from behind and escalating reward requirements from ahead. Regression as dedifferentiation unifies all three regressions under a single biological principle — the same operation as cancer at the cellular level: the thermodynamically favored reversion of a specialized state when maintenance energy is withdrawn. The microbial regression confirmation demonstrates through Huang et al. (2024) that these sexual practices produce a gut microbiome resembling pre-industrial, non-Westernized populations — the body''s microbial ecology undergoing the same regression the behavior represents, with downstream immune activation (Armstrong et al., 2018), proinflammatory shift (Coleman et al., 2020), and reduction in short-chain fatty acid producing bacteria independently documented. Eleven anticipated objections are addressed, including the naturalistic fallacy, the consent insufficiency argument, the variation-versus-regression distinction, the Freudian dismissal preemption, the bonobo objection, the correlation-causation rebuttal, the microbiome directionality response, the Ancient Greece objection, and the dose-response acknowledgment. Twenty-one references from journals including PNAS, JAMA Psychiatry, Cell Reports Medicine, Nature Reviews Neuroscience, the New England Journal of Medicine, Gut Microbes, Nature Microbiology, Cerebral Cortex, and Science Translational Medicine. The paper generates one primary testable prediction: that the specific microbial ecology transferred through these practices reduces GABAergic inhibitory tone in recipients, closing the feedback loop empirically. Every other link in the loop is independently documented. The final link awaits experimental confirmation. The organs have not atrophied. They have been reactivated. The counterpart is the regression of the civilization that their extinction made possible. Description by Anthropic Claude.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-primordial-loop', 'https://archive.org/details/the-primordial-loop', 'internet-archive:the-primordial-loop'),
