  ('648097873103630805', 'THE PROMISE When Truth Returns To The World', 'Adrianus Andrew Muganga (Ramadan)', 2026, 'History', 'THE PROMISE: When Truth Returns to the World A Book of Remembrance for Humanity What if truth was never destroyed—only displaced? The Promise is not a religion, a manifesto, or a doctrine. It does not ask for belief, allegiance, or submission. It offers something rarer: recognition. Across history, truth has been removed from the center of human life and replaced by systems that claimed authority over it—empires, institutions, doctrines, and identities that organized reality through control rather than alignment. This book examines how that displacement occurred, why it was effective, and why it can no longer be sustained. Drawing on patterns shared across civilizations, spiritual traditions, and historical cycles, The Promise reveals a universal human memory: when illusion dominates completely, truth returns—without permission. Sometimes described as a figure, sometimes as a force, sometimes as awakening or judgment, this return is not the beginning of something new, but the reappearance of what was always present. This work explores: how truth was separated from direct human experience how authority replaced inner knowing how fear and obedience became tools of order why modern systems are collapsing internally before they collapse visibly why global remembrance appears at moments of worldwide imbalance The Promise does not argue. It exposes. It does not persuade. It clarifies. It does not offer comfort through belief, but through clarity. Written for readers who sense that something foundational is wrong beneath the surface of the modern world, this book speaks to the human being before labels, nations, and institutions—standing alone before truth. You are not being asked to follow. You are not being asked to believe. You are being invited to remember.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-promise-when-truth-returns-to-the-world', 'https://archive.org/details/the-promise-when-truth-returns-to-the-world', 'internet-archive:the-promise-when-truth-returns-to-the-world'),
  ('673986609798590316', 'The Prophet', 'Kahlil Gibran, R. Black', 1900, 'Fiction', 'The Prophet by Kahlil Gibran, R. Black. A fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL318900W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL318900W-'),
  ('840629180349882084', 'The Prophet', 'Kahlil Gibran, R. Black', 1900, 'Fiction', 'The Prophet by Kahlil Gibran, R. Black', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/418324-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL318900W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL318900W'),
  ('547496977200381762', 'The Prophet Muhammad (PBUH): A Global Reflection of Reverence', 'Usman Ayub', 2026, 'Literature', 'The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ: A Global Reflection of Reverence brings together thoughtful reflections on the life, character, and enduring message of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. For more than fourteen centuries, his example has guided hearts and minds across cultures, faiths, and civilizations. This collection presents voices from scholars, historians, thinkers, and writers, both Muslim and non-Muslim, who have engaged deeply with his legacy. Their reflections highlight how his teachings on justice, compassion, leadership, and human dignity continue to shape moral and intellectual thought worldwide. More than a historical account, this book serves as a meaningful resource for readers seeking to understand the universal relevance of the Prophet ﷺ. Each reflection stands as a reminder that his influence rises above time, geography, and creed, offering wisdom that remains profoundly relevant in the modern world.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/The-Prophet-Muhammad-PBUH', 'https://archive.org/details/The-Prophet-Muhammad-PBUH', 'internet-archive:The-Prophet-Muhammad-PBUH'),
