  ('834292849372825005', 'The Pure Theory of Capital', 'Friedrich A. von Hayek', 1941, 'Economics', 'The Pure Theory of Capital by Friedrich A. von Hayek. A economics book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1164996W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL1164996W-'),
  ('173067735040369121', 'The Puritan Dilemma, How Revolutionary Ideology Created Permanent Factional Warfare And Made Orthodoxy Impossible To Enforce', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study examines the structural crisis of authority in Puritan Massachusetts (1630-1693), analyzing how the appropriation of anti-hierarchical Protestant ideology to break English episcopal power created an unsolvable dilemma for colonial elites attempting to establish their own interpretive authority. Focusing on the Antinomian Controversy and the trials of Anne Hutchinson (1636-1638), it demonstrates how revolutionary rhetoric empowering individual scriptural interpretation systematically generated the heresies it sought to suppress, forcing elites into permanent factional warfare conducted in theological language while actually fighting over who controlled the right to interpret scripture and define orthodoxy. The case reveals the impossibility of maintaining elite interpretive monopoly when the legitimating ideology explicitly denies such monopolies exist, resulting in constant trials, banishments, and escalating persecution (culminating in the Salem Witch Trials) as mechanisms to reassert authority that could never be openly claimed. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-puritan-dilemma-how-revolutionary-ideology-created-permanent-factional-warfa', 'https://archive.org/details/the-puritan-dilemma-how-revolutionary-ideology-created-permanent-factional-warfa', 'internet-archive:the-puritan-dilemma-how-revolutionary-ideology-created-permanent-factional-warfa'),
