  ('680297554303864907', 'The Remembering Ones Thanos Kalamidas', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'The sixth story from the series "The colour of the armband", unveiled in a familiar universe and a new era long after wars and peace with new predators and enemies. Kurt stood on the second-floor deck of the charred ruin, watching the orange-grey tendrils curl around the settlement’s perimeter. They moved with a desperate, simulated life, blind fingers seeking a grip on a reality that no longer wanted them. Twenty feet of sterile cement acted as a metaphysical barrier; the haze would not cross. The elders mumbled about the Before Times, invoking the ghosts of molecular chemistry and forgotten synthetic compounds. Kurt, however, harboured the suspicion that the universe was merely tired. Some mysteries existed solely as a buffer to keep the human mind from collapsing into its own gravity.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-remembering-ones-thanos-kalamidas', 'https://archive.org/details/the-remembering-ones-thanos-kalamidas', 'internet-archive:the-remembering-ones-thanos-kalamidas'),
