  ('1104772928770095998', 'The Riftwar Saga', 'Raymond E. Feist', 1988, 'Adventure', 'The Riftwar Saga by Raymond E. Feist', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8738488-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL554715W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL554715W'),
  ('493420269411542011', 'The Right Wine', 'Trade Veteran', 2026, 'History', 'Cool-climate dry wine — low residual sugar, low pH, minimal intervention — has been systematically displaced from both the market and the medical literature by the commercial transformation of the 1990s boom. This essay argues that the epidemiological case against wine was built from the wrong product, consumed in the wrong way, and that the ancestral model — documented from Georgian qvevri tradition through the noble varieties of northern Spain, Piemonte, Burgundy, and the Rhine — has never been adequately evaluated. The argument is grounded in fifty years of biographical evidence and addresses the sick-quitter effect, Blue Zone longevity data, and the methodological failures of the major longitudinal studies.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the_right_wine', 'https://archive.org/details/the_right_wine', 'internet-archive:the_right_wine'),
  ('707016370435173881', 'The righteous men', 'Sam Bourne', 2006, 'Thriller', 'The righteous men by Sam Bourne. A thriller book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL16026757W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL16026757W-'),
  ('584659287971444862', 'The Rigveda: A Historical Analysis', 'Shrikant G. Talageri', 2000, 'History', 'The Rigveda is the oldest and most important source of material for India, Indo-Aryan, and even Indo-European history. It is a text which has been part of a hoary and widespread living tradition thousands of years old. Naturally, a text which has remained alive, as part of a living tradition, for so long cannot and should not be analysed without reference to what that tradition has to say about it. In the present volume, the author has confirmed emphatically that India was also the original homeland not only of the Indo-Aryans but also of the Indo-Iranians and the Indo-Europeans.;The author has gone directly to the primary sources without any preconceived notions, and examined as well analysed the available information with the help of traditional tools of interpretation. In this present study, he has elaborated a historical analysis of the Rigveda on the basis of genealogies of composers of the hymns preserved in the Anukramanis or indices of the Rigveda. Table of Contents:- Section I: The Rigveda The AnukramaNIs The Composers of the Rigveda The Chronology of the Rigveda The Geography of the Rigveda The Historical Identity of the Vedic Aryans Section II: Beyond the Rigveda The Indo-Iranian Homeland The Indo-European Homeland Section III: Appendices Misinterpretations of Rigvedic History Michael Witzel SaramA and the PaNis: A Mythological Theme in the Rigveda Prominent River-names in Rigveda Prominent place-names in Rigveda Anu-Druhyu Migrations', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-rigveda-a-historical-analysis-shrikant-g.-talageri', 'https://archive.org/details/the-rigveda-a-historical-analysis-shrikant-g.-talageri', 'internet-archive:the-rigveda-a-historical-analysis-shrikant-g.-talageri'),
