  ('552532915840894539', 'THE RULE BOOK (Universe Law)', 'Rafick Subear', 2026, 'Science', '​​ "The Rule Book (Universe Law)" is the outcome of an extensive 12-year research by Rafick Subear. This book serves as a profound guide to understanding the unseen laws that govern our existence and the cosmos. It uniquely bridges the gap between science, logic, and spirituality. The author explores the core essence of major world religions—Hinduism, Christianity, and Islam—to find a common thread of universal truth. Furthermore, the book investigates world-renowned mysteries like the Voynich Manuscript, the Bermuda Triangle, and the Egyptian Pyramids through the lens of ''Universe Law.'' A significant highlight is the introduction of "Aero-Electric Starships" and advanced space propulsion, offering a visionary perspective on future human goals and interstellar travel. It is a logical exploration designed to help humanity align their lives and future advancements with the fundamental mechanisms of the universe.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-rule-book-a-4', 'https://archive.org/details/the-rule-book-a-4', 'internet-archive:the-rule-book-a-4'),
