  ('213469957474565718', 'The Salvagers', 'John Michael Godier', 2013, 'Science', 'The Salvagers by John Michael Godier. A science book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL27965874W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL27965874W-'),
  ('162779464024225723', 'The Same Conversation, Written Differently Information Asymmetry In Imperial Vassal Relations', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This comparative historiographical analysis examines two structurally identical imperial-vassal encounters—Herod the Great meeting Octavian (31 BCE) and Cyrus the Great authorizing Jewish return (539 BCE)—demonstrating how the same mechanism (imperial strategic calculation determining vassal fate) is recorded as elite political negotiation in Roman sources (Josephus) versus divine intervention in Hebrew Bible sources. The study reveals information asymmetry as a fundamental mechanism of elite power: elites understand material mechanisms (military force, strategic interests) while common populations receive narratives mystifying these mechanisms through divine will or prophetic fulfillment. It demonstrates how historiographical traditions reveal or conceal power operations depending on whether the intended audience comprises political elites who must understand mechanisms to exercise power, or common populations who must believe legitimating narratives to accept subordination. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-same-conversation-written-differently-information-asymmetry-in-imperial-vassal-relations', 'https://archive.org/details/the-same-conversation-written-differently-information-asymmetry-in-imperial-vassal-relations', 'internet-archive:the-same-conversation-written-differently-information-asymmetry-in-imperial-vassal-relations'),
  ('950469378980589543', 'The Sanders Deception Done', 'J. Weeds', 2025, 'Science', 'The revolution was never going to be televised—because Bernie Sanders made sure it never left the stage. For nearly a decade, Bernie Sanders was worshipped as the outsider inside the machine. But this book tears off the mask. Sanders wasn’t a threat to the system—he was the firewall between uprising and obedience. With AOC, RFK Jr., and a legion of branded “change agents” in tow, Sanders helped build the perfect trap: controlled opposition in a red-white-and-blue wrapper. This is the takedown you weren’t supposed to read. The Sanders Deception is not just a political exposé—it’s a blueprint for liberation. It names names. It calls out the grid. It shows how the ratchet tightens and why the only real exit is through the Green Quadrant—where no elite agenda survives. Forget what they told you about revolution. This is the truth behind the performance.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-sanders-deception-done', 'https://archive.org/details/the-sanders-deception-done', 'internet-archive:the-sanders-deception-done'),
