  ('867984767036360942', 'The Smile', 'Sumit Vishnu Salmuthe', 2026, 'horror story', 'A smile can end a fight. A smile can calm anger. But sometimes… a smile can destroy a life. Sam is an ordinary college student known by everyone as “The Smiling Boy.” Always cheerful, always positive. But one mysterious email promising easy money changes everything. Soon after accepting the offer, Sam receives a strange gift — a smiling toy that seems harmless at first. But as days pass, people around him begin to disappear, strange messages appear on his screen, and the toy’s smile grows wider. Watching. Waiting. Smiling. As Sam searches for answers, he uncovers a terrifying truth hidden deep within the internet — a curse that passes from one person to another. Now Sam faces a horrifying choice: send the curse to someone else… or become its next victim. The Smile is a chilling psychological horror story about technology, temptation, and the terrifying price behind a single click. Because sometimes… the scariest monsters are the ones that smile.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-smile-english-story', 'https://archive.org/details/the-smile-english-story', 'internet-archive:the-smile-english-story'),
