  ('306652718222895078', 'The Sopranos', 'Unknown', 2009, 'History', '“In its original run on HBO, The Sopranos mattered, and it matters still,” Dana Polan asserts early in this analysis of the hit show, in which he sets out to clarify the impact and importance of the series in both its cultural and media-industry contexts. A renowned film and TV scholar, Polan combines a close and extended reading of the show itself—and of select episodes and scenes—with broader attention to the social landscape with which it is in dialogue. For Polan, The Sopranos is a work of playful irony that complicates simplistic attempts to grasp its meanings and values. The show seductively beckons the viewer into an amoral universe, hinting at ways to make sense of its ethically complicated situations, only to challenge the viewer’s complacent grasp of things.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/oapen-20.500.12657-43813', 'https://archive.org/details/oapen-20.500.12657-43813', 'internet-archive:oapen-20.500.12657-43813'),
  ('1075411066845927171', 'THE SOUL BEHIND THE SAYINGS', 'Abdullahi Abdulrazaq', 2026, 'Literature', 'We’ve all heard the sayings: “Money can’t buy happiness.” “Time is money.” “Silence is golden.” We repeat them, agree with them, and pass them on—often without ever stopping to ask what they truly mean. But what if these familiar phrases hold more than just surface-level wisdom? What if they carry quiet, sometimes startling, truths about life, purpose, and human nature? In The Soul Behind the Sayings , Abdullahi Abdulrazaq takes fifty timeless proverbs and holds them up to the light. With a voice that is both thoughtful and accessible, he explores the deeper layers of meaning we often overlook. This is not a book of simple explanations or motivational platitudes. It is a series of gentle, probing reflections that invite you to think more deeply about the ideas that shape your days.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-soul-behind-the-sayings', 'https://archive.org/details/the-soul-behind-the-sayings', 'internet-archive:the-soul-behind-the-sayings'),
  ('829577421967510891', 'The soul continuum', 'Simon West-Bulford', 2015, 'Adventure', 'The soul continuum by Simon West-Bulford. A adventure book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL22320281W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL22320281W-'),
