  ('859269262498868074', 'The Theory Of Evolution What The Text Books Don''t Tell You', 'Talib H. Janabi, Ph.D.', 2026, 'Science', 'All disciplines of science are built on the principle of cause and effect. The theory of evolution is built upon the idea of accidental random changes that resulted in complex and highly regulated living systems. The theory expects us to accept that an infinite number of random accidents kept randomly happening to produce the enormous diversity of living species, and kept improving these species. According to the standards set forth in the scientific process, scientific results are only accepted if they can be reproduced given the same conditions. This principle, upon which all sciences are based, cannot be applied to the theory of evolution. None of the claimed results of evolution can be repeated, and they don’t fulfill the basic requirements of scientific experimentation and testing. This book examines the theories of evolution and shows their scientific absurdity.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-theory-of-evolution-what-the-text-books-dont-tell-you_202602', 'https://archive.org/details/the-theory-of-evolution-what-the-text-books-dont-tell-you_202602', 'internet-archive:the-theory-of-evolution-what-the-text-books-dont-tell-you_202602'),
