  ('461551478596216062', 'The three-body problem', 'Liu, Cixin, author', 2014, 'Science Fiction', '399 pages ; 25 cm', 'https://archive.org/services/img/isbn_9780765377067', 'https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780765377067', 'internet-archive:isbn_9780765377067'),
  ('436724288478698240', 'The Throat Of The Twentieth Century', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This counterfactual history examines how the death of Frederick III of Germany after just 99 days as Kaiser in 1888—caused by a misdiagnosed throat tumor—altered the trajectory of the 20th century. It traces the cascade from this single medical catastrophe to the succession of his psychologically troubled son Wilhelm II, whose dismantling of Bismarck''s alliance system, naval arms race with Britain, and erratic foreign policy created the conditions for World War I, the Bolshevik Revolution, and the totalitarian horrors that followed. The study demonstrates how individual agency and dynastic architecture intersected at a critical historical juncture, arguing that the liberal Anglo-German partnership envisioned by Frederick and his wife Victoria (daughter of Queen Victoria) might have prevented the catastrophic conflicts that killed over 100 million people. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-throat-of-the-twentieth-century', 'https://archive.org/details/the-throat-of-the-twentieth-century', 'internet-archive:the-throat-of-the-twentieth-century'),
