  ('565646737029463875', 'The Thundering Herd', 'Zane Grey', 1924, 'Romance', 'The Thundering Herd by Zane Grey', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1514198-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL485436W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL485436W'),
  ('235959030222908813', 'The Tiger In The Chapel Of Rose Manisha Yadav', 'Ovi eBook Publishing', 2026, 'eBook', 'It was near evening when the cloisters began to empty. The priory’s bell tolled low, heavy in the smoky air of May, and the shadows inside the stone corridors deepened like spilled ink. Soldiers wandered among the walled gardens, laughing too loudly, sword belts clinking against armour ill-fitted to the task of war. One youth, little more than a boy, ran his blade down a hedge, shearing fresh leaves until a steward barked at him. The war was here. And it was coming for all of them. Queen Margaret stood alone by the chapel window, watching. Her fingers, delicate and ringed, clutched at the carved stone like claws on prey. Below her, the banners of the House of Lancaster flapped in nervous rhythm. She did not blink.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-tiger-in-the-chapel-of-rose-manisha-yadav', 'https://archive.org/details/the-tiger-in-the-chapel-of-rose-manisha-yadav', 'internet-archive:the-tiger-in-the-chapel-of-rose-manisha-yadav'),
