  ('130713824248848138', 'THE TWO DARRELLS, HUBERT DARRELL AND DARRELL MORRISEY, Stephen Morrissey', 'Stephen Morrissey', 2026, 'History', 'Hubert Darrell, who explored and mapped parts of Canada''s far north, is the son of Charles Darrell after whom, coincidentally, Darrell Morrisey was named. In 1890 Hubert Darrell moved to Birtle, Manitoba and several years later he began his exploration and mapping of Canada''s far north. Darrell Morrisey was an artist and member of the prestigious Beaver Hall Group of artists. The two Darrells never met and, tragically, they both died young, but they lived true to their inner calling, one that was far removed from the expectations of their families and social class.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-two-darrells-hubert-darrell-and-darrell-morrisey-stephen-morrissey', 'https://archive.org/details/the-two-darrells-hubert-darrell-and-darrell-morrisey-stephen-morrissey', 'internet-archive:the-two-darrells-hubert-darrell-and-darrell-morrisey-stephen-morrissey'),
