  ('139536869686937385', 'The ware tetralogy', 'Rucker, Rudy v. B. (Rudy von Bitter), 1946-', 2010, 'Science Fiction', 'Your Guide to the 21st Century! It starts with Software , where rebel robots bring immortality to their human creator by eating his brain. Software won the first Philip K. Dick Award. In Wetware , the robots decide to start building people—and people get strung out on an insane new drug called merge. This cyberpunk classic garnered a second Philip K. Dick award. By Freeware , the robots have evolved into soft plastic slugs called moldies­—and some human “cheeseballs” want to have sex with them. The action redoubles when aliens begin arriving in the form of cosmic rays. And with Realware , the humans and robots find a wormhole with god inside, learn the art of direct matter control, get wacked out as usual—and find true love. Support the author by buying the paperback via rudyrucker.com Archived by Unglue.it', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ware_tetralogy', 'https://archive.org/details/ware_tetralogy', 'internet-archive:ware_tetralogy'),
  ('464756426274576590', 'The warlord of Mars #3', 'Edgar Rice Burroughs', 1919, 'Science Fiction', 'The warlord of Mars #3 by Edgar Rice Burroughs. A science fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1418137W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL1418137W-'),
