  ('181837825183355454', 'Thirty Godly Short Stories from Chet Swearingen''s Early Childhood in Delta, Ohio', 'Chet Swearingen', 2026, 'Literature', 'Thirty short, engaging stories written especially for eight-year-olds. Each true story is drawn from real-life events that occurred in Delta, Ohio during the first five years of Chet Swearingen’s life and concludes with a clear, godly moral or spiritual lesson. These wholesome tales entertain young readers while gently teaching biblical values, character, and faith through everyday childhood experiences in a small Ohio town. Perfect for bedtime reading, family devotions, Sunday school, or homeschool literature. Additional Information: All thirty stories are true accounts that took place in Delta, Ohio during the author''s first five years of life. Written especially for eight-year-olds (approximately grades 2–4), this collection aims to provide wholesome, faith-building reading material for Christian families, Sunday schools, and homeschoolers.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/the-little-boy-stories', 'https://archive.org/details/the-little-boy-stories', 'internet-archive:the-little-boy-stories'),
