  ('1041775112902737309', 'Thomas Carlyle On Heroes Lecture II Prophet As Hero', 'Thomas Carlyle, (ed) Muhammad Umar Chand', 2014, 'History', 'Thomas Carlyle (1795-1881) on Muhammad (Mohammad, or Mahomet,): Hero as Prophet: 2nd of his 6 lectures on Heroes, Hero-worship, and Heroes in History With notes, prepared for on-line reading and retrieval for research purposes by Muhammad Umar Chand', 'https://archive.org/services/img/ThomasCarlyleOnHeroesLectureIIProphetAsHero', 'https://archive.org/details/ThomasCarlyleOnHeroesLectureIIProphetAsHero', 'internet-archive:ThomasCarlyleOnHeroesLectureIIProphetAsHero'),
  ('658391284671469127', 'Thomas George Hinde And Mary Evelyn Brewer V 4', 'Gene Cook Hall', 2026, 'History', 'This is the story of Thomas George ''Tom'' Hinde and Mary Evelyn Brewer taken from available sources and interviews during their lifetime. They were both from New Mexico and lived during the 20th century. Tom was instrumental in the development of telephone services to the state through his work at Mountain States Telephone and Telegraph. Both, especially Mary Evelyn, were involved in Masonic organizations at the local, state, and national levels. The book includes a complete index of names and sources of the information along with an appendix of historical documents.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/thomas-george-hinde-and-mary-evelyn-brewer-v-4', 'https://archive.org/details/thomas-george-hinde-and-mary-evelyn-brewer-v-4', 'internet-archive:thomas-george-hinde-and-mary-evelyn-brewer-v-4'),
  ('659477769570851378', 'Thomas Jefferson', 'Matt Doeden, Gordon Purcell, Terry Beatty', 2006, 'Graphic Novel', 'Thomas Jefferson by Matt Doeden, Gordon Purcell, Terry Beatty. A graphic novel book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5712411W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL5712411W-'),
  ('781356232415790711', 'Thomas Jefferson', 'Matt Doeden, Gordon Purcell, Terry Beatty', 2006, 'Graphic Novel', 'Thomas Jefferson by Matt Doeden, Gordon Purcell, Terry Beatty', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/463650-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5712411W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL5712411W'),
  ('919496418378202891', 'Thompson’s Summit Grove on Palomar Mountain', 'Peter Brueggeman', 2026, 'History', 'In 1947, Wayne Thompson and his brother Russell Thompson along with Russell''s wife Noreen started Thompson''s Summit Grove on Palomar Mountain, located at the intersection of Highway S6 and State Park Road. The business grew to encompass a gas station, store, snack bar, and then a restaurant. Russell and Noreen Thompson''s share of the business was sold to Carl Henry ''Wog'' Bergman. Wayne Thompson met his future wife Shirley there and she became part of the business. Wayne and Shirley Thompson along with then co-owners Ralph and Lelia Kulk sold the business in 1977.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/thompsons-summit-grove_202401', 'https://archive.org/details/thompsons-summit-grove_202401', 'internet-archive:thompsons-summit-grove_202401'),
