  ('796737841987392125', 'Through the Looking-Glass, and What Alice Found There', 'Carroll, Lewis (Charles Lutwidge Dodgson)', 2026, 'Fantasy', 'Through the Looking-Glass, and What Alice Found There is a charming yet intellectually challenging fiction about logic, selfhood, and the quirks of society standards. When Carroll enters a mirrored realm filled by chatting plants, animating chess pieces, and eccentric personalities, he uses contradiction, linguistic play, and a series of interactions to question established authority, the nature of language, and the foundations of logic. The narrative''s creative breadth and logical complexity foreshadow modern fantasy and speculative fiction by mixing absurdity with philosophical wisdom. Zeba Books Classics presents enduring works that challenge authority and remain relevant today. Carefully prepared, unabridged, and true to the original texts, these books invite readers into a timeless conversation. This edition is published by Zeba Books. Visit us at https://zebabooks.org/genre/classics for more timeless classics.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/through_the_looking_glass_and_what_alice_found_there_lewis_carroll_zebabooks', 'https://archive.org/details/through_the_looking_glass_and_what_alice_found_there_lewis_carroll_zebabooks', 'internet-archive:through_the_looking_glass_and_what_alice_found_there_lewis_carroll_zebabooks'),
