  ('222223351862182329', 'Time Never Stands Still', 'Junaid Farooqui', 2026, 'Literature', 'This book presents a unique literary experiment inspired by the long poem “Waqt Behi Natho” (Time Never Stands Still) by Muhammad Ali Pathan. The work transforms the themes, emotions, and reflections of the original poem into a thoughtful interview format. By framing the poet’s ideas as questions and responses drawn from the poem itself, the book creates an engaging dialogue between the reader and the poet’s imagination. It explores themes of time, love, separation, human struggle, and social realities. This creative approach offers readers a new way to experience poetry—where the poem not only expresses feelings but also answers deeper questions about life and the passage of time.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/time-never-stands-still', 'https://archive.org/details/time-never-stands-still', 'internet-archive:time-never-stands-still'),
  ('403010783401902197', 'Time of Their Lives: Nancy Hanks Lincoln and Dolly Madison (2024)', 'Nancy Hanks Lincoln Public Library', 2026, 'History', 'Dual biographies about Nancy Hanks Lincoln and Dolly Madison from digitally restored page image scans of original 1952 and 1886 editions. Enhanced 2024 edition. This book is copyrighted. Material is not public domain. This is a reading copy only. High resolution version available in trade paperback print format. For print copies please visit online retailers such as Barnes and Noble or Books-a-Million . Both sites offer bulk discount of single titles for schools, colleges, universities and public libraries. Or contact Standish Press at www.standishpress.com', 'https://archive.org/services/img/time-of-their-lives-nancy-hanks-lincoln-and-dolly-madison-2024-6x-9-display-book-version', 'https://archive.org/details/time-of-their-lives-nancy-hanks-lincoln-and-dolly-madison-2024-6x-9-display-book-version', 'internet-archive:time-of-their-lives-nancy-hanks-lincoln-and-dolly-madison-2024-6x-9-display-book-version'),
