  ('876646587401870190', 'Too Hard To Handle', 'Unknown', 2026, 'History', 'Too Hard to Handle: A Memoir of the Pur’p’l Tur’t’lz is Greg Brown’s inside story of a misfit Valley band that grew from living-room jams and backyard generator parties to clubs like the Palomino and Winston’s OB. Part memoir, part band history, it follows Greg, Steve Bryant, Kenny Bellew, Greg Herman, Chris Baustert, Todd Myers, and Ron Russell through flatbed “mobile jams,” Camp Templin chaos, brushes with Rick Rubin and The Turtles, and the making of their album Hatched . This version is without photos. Use links for photos.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/too-hard-to-handle-no-photos', 'https://archive.org/details/too-hard-to-handle-no-photos', 'internet-archive:too-hard-to-handle-no-photos'),
