  ('289307335301296410', 'Too much like Englishmen - Amoy migrants in Australia', 'Michael Williams', 2026, 'History', 'Too much like Englishmen uncovers a forgotten migration that reshaped colonial Australia long before the gold rushes made Chinese migration visible. Between 1848 and 1853, more than 3,000 men from Amoy—modern Xiamen in China''s Fujian province—were recruited under five-year labour contracts and sent to New South Wales.struggling to replace convict labour.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/too-much-like-englishmen-2', 'https://archive.org/details/too-much-like-englishmen-2', 'internet-archive:too-much-like-englishmen-2'),
