  ('778659440101248043', 'Towards a Catalogue of Cleveland Publishings Western Series. 2. Preliminary Title List for the Cleveland Western series', 'Anders N. Nilsson', 2026, 'Literature', 'Author and title of more than two thousand issues of the Australian Cleveland Publishing''s major series of cheap novel magazines, Cleveland Western are listed. This series started in 1953 with #501 and ended in 2016 with #3054. Initiallly, it mixed the two genres crime and western. The last crime novel included was Robert Dudgeon’s Murder So What! in #596. Although mainly including novels written by Australian authors, some American paperbacks, chiefly from Pyramid Books, were reprinted from the start. The last American novel being W.C. Tuttle’s Thunderbird Range in #724. The contents of about 500 issues from this long series remain unknown.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/andersnilsson_2026_clevelandlists_prel_2a', 'https://archive.org/details/andersnilsson_2026_clevelandlists_prel_2a', 'internet-archive:andersnilsson_2026_clevelandlists_prel_2a'),
