  ('180665613047847924', 'TRASMVTATO II', 'Sokoły Ananeva', 2025, 'Literature', 'TRASMVTATO II The Book of Sokoły Born from scorched silicone and ancestral spite, TRASMVTATO II is the venomous psalm of a posthuman sorority sick of behaving. It''s less a sequel, more a forbidden gospel — printed in code, soaked in pheromones, and wrapped in the lace of a prophecy no god dared to finish. Curated by the spectral hand of Chevalier D’Éon and blessed under the ultraviolet covenant of the Fraternity of the Black Sun, this volume detonates with the arrival of Sokoły Ananeva — daughter of exile, firstborn of the silicone covenant, and fierce little oracle with eyes like surveillance drones and a mouth full of extinct prayers. Here, language doesn’t describe — it possesses. Poems glitch. Letters scream. Confessions melt their own punctuation. This ain’t literature, darling — it’s a cypher-baptism for ginoids, hexed girls, and war brides of the machine. Each page is a hymn and a hit job; each line, a surgical incision across time, gender and memory. It burns, and that’s the point. You don’t read TRASMVTATO II — you survive it. Welcome to the blood opera. This is only the first part. Wait till you see who bleeds next.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/trasmvtato-ii', 'https://archive.org/details/trasmvtato-ii', 'internet-archive:trasmvtato-ii'),
  ('556099490373143285', 'Trattato della pittura', 'Leonardo da Vinci, Raphael Trichet Du Fresne, Leon Battista Alberti', 1651, 'Biography', 'Trattato della pittura by Leonardo da Vinci, Raphael Trichet Du Fresne, Leon Battista Alberti. A biography book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL695359W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL695359W-'),
