  ('1083515617778331512', 'UK''s Acute Food System Crisis', 'Sarah Bridle', 2026, 'Science', 'Crossing the Rubicon "The potential for events to trigger acute food crises is frequently underestimated." ▪ U.K. food insecurity , white paper written & published by 37 food system experts in the scientific journal Sustainability on January 29th, 2026. "The stability of the UK’s food system is a critical aspect of national security , yet it remains vulnerable to threats that could precipitate a crisis. Despite living in a high-income country with sophisticated food supply chains, people in the UK are not immune to disruptions that can lead to severe consequences , such as food insecurity , malnutrition and even civil unrest ."', 'https://archive.org/services/img/01-uks-acute-food-system-crisis-01-29-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/01-uks-acute-food-system-crisis-01-29-2026', 'internet-archive:01-uks-acute-food-system-crisis-01-29-2026'),
