  ('288830397220346412', 'UNCAGE THE KIDS: Why Child Detention Is a Security Failure and How to Retire It', 'Sum Bunny', 2026, 'Science', 'A policy essay arguing that child detention is an obsolete security technology and proposing a modern, sovereignty-preserving alternative based on family unity, procedural custody, and rapid legal resolution. UNCAGE THE KIDS is a policy-grade essay arguing that child detention is not only a humanitarian failure, but a strategic and security failure. The paper accepts the premise of state sovereignty and border control, and reframes child detention as an obsolete, low-fidelity technology for managing 21st-century migration flows. Drawing on systems engineering, political science, behavioral economics, and child development research, it demonstrates why deterrence through cruelty repeatedly fails and why family separation undermines long-term stability. The essay proposes a replacement architecture— Refuge Mode —based on family unity as a security doctrine, procedural custody rather than confinement, rapid legal resolution (“Justice of Velocity”), and distributed community placement. Rare high-risk cases are handled through forensic triage rather than universal detention. Written for policymakers, legal scholars, and institutional decision-makers, the document treats child detention as a design failure and offers a modern security alternative that is cheaper, more effective, and more humane without sacrificing sovereignty. Released under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license to encourage reuse, adaptation, and policy experimentation. Part of the Sum Bunny Canon, Ark Hive Press.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/uncage-the-kids-sum-bunny-2026', 'https://archive.org/details/uncage-the-kids-sum-bunny-2026', 'internet-archive:uncage-the-kids-sum-bunny-2026'),
