  ('163337245485174877', 'United Rentals 2024 Annual Report', 'United Rentals', 2025, 'History', 'The 2024 annual report & Form 10-K, Proxy Statement and Chairman''s message for United Rentals (Ticker: URI). The corporation founded in 1997 is an American equipment rental company headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/united-rentals-uri-annual-report-2024', 'https://archive.org/details/united-rentals-uri-annual-report-2024', 'internet-archive:united-rentals-uri-annual-report-2024'),
  ('1097976089103894525', 'United States, From Colonial Creole Oligarchies To Contemporary Financial Capitalism ( 1607 2025)', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines elite control mechanisms in the United States across 418 years (1607-2025), analyzing how American elites adapted from colonial slaveholding oligarchies through industrial capitalism to contemporary financial oligarchy while maintaining concentrated wealth and power. It demonstrates how revolutionary mythology obscures elite continuity, showing that the American Revolution, Civil War, Progressive Era reforms, New Deal, and Civil Rights Movement achieved political transformations without fundamentally redistributing wealth—with contemporary concentration (top 1% controlling 35-40%) approaching Gilded Age levels. The study reveals how regional elite diversity (Southern planters, Northern merchants, Western land speculators), slavery''s centrality to accumulation, and federal structure created distinctive adaptation patterns while preserving the core pattern of elite power persistence across dramatic political upheavals. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/united-states-from-colonial-creole-oligarchies-to-contemporary-financial-capitalism-1607-2025', 'https://archive.org/details/united-states-from-colonial-creole-oligarchies-to-contemporary-financial-capitalism-1607-2025', 'internet-archive:united-states-from-colonial-creole-oligarchies-to-contemporary-financial-capitalism-1607-2025'),
