  ('703934405286541312', 'Verizon Communications 2025 Annual Report & Proxy Statement', 'Verizon Communications Inc.', 2026, 'History', 'The 2025 annual report & Form 10-K, Proxy Statement, ESG Report and Chairman''s message to stockholders for Verizon Communications Inc. (Ticker: VZ). Verizon is an American multinational telecommunications conglomerate. The company was founded in 1984 as Bell Atlantic as part of the break up of the Bell System into seven companies that were referred to as "Baby Bells". The company is based in New York City.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/01-verizon-communications-vz-proxy-statement-2026-05-21', 'https://archive.org/details/01-verizon-communications-vz-proxy-statement-2026-05-21', 'internet-archive:01-verizon-communications-vz-proxy-statement-2026-05-21'),
  ('346235191382632804', 'vermisfloramortis', 'Nevo Dror Mizrahi, aka Wooden.Ghost, aka Delirious.Knowledge', 2026, 'Science', 'Vermis Flora Mortis is a unique and deeply personal work fusing memoir, philosophical essay, speculative science, ecological parable, and poetic lament. The manuscript is both literary experiment and an honest testimony within the borderlands of science, epistemology, and art. VFM distinguishes itself in both form and content, inviting the reader into singular narrative that blends lived experience, phenomenology, myth, and chronicled suffering. displays extensive recursive self examination and a courageous commitment to exposing meaning within trauma, illness, and existential uncertainty, employing inventive literary devices and contemporary multimedia references throughout. The manuscript in favor of a recursive spiral. The text moves back and forth in time, looping from childhood to present and projecting into an imagined or extrapolated future. It employs distinctive temporal markers dates, times, and invented quantifiers ("infraplanksec") and interleaves diary like personal entries with epistolary elements and philosophical discourse. Its nontraditional structural logic gives the work a hypnotic, stream of consciousness rhythm, one that is balanced by periodic returns to the central thematic triad: •Personal struggle with the mysterious affliction. •Ecological fate of the world ("BadWinds," ecosystem collapse) •Loss&Longing motifs (grief for Shilgiya, the cat; alienation from family;) The result is both labyrinthine and intuitive, adhering to idiosyncratic logic while still offering connective semantic tissue between motifs. The manuscript appears comprehensive in its scope and intention, concluding with visionary, poetic, and aphoristic remarks. VFM arc follows through from exposition of personal affliction and philosophical inquiry to existential synthesis. Throughout, the text asserts its own liminality; it is self reflexive, and accepting of its own fragmentariness, an existential stance rather than a flaw. Vermis Flora Mortis draws upon a deep well of philosophical, artistic, and scientific thought without overt academic referencing. It is influenced by the tradition of existential diary (Anne Frank, with explicit comparisons), marginal science and speculative theory, phenomenological autobiography, and the poetic surrealism found in modernist and postmodernist literature. Intertextual allusions range from canonical mythological and biblical motifs to contemporary intellectual memes and scientific concepts. imbued with both skepticism and visionariness embracing uncertainty as method and theme. Poetic Interpolations: Lyrical stanzas, prose poetry, and invented mythopoeic language run throughout. Hybrid Genres: The book moves between memoir, philosophical tract, documentary, art criticism, and speculative prophecy. The language employs neologisms, code like time units, recursive selfcitations, and the conscious creation of evolving entities (AIEEVE/EVE). Vermis Flora Mortis stands as bold contribution to contemporary hybrid literature. Radically personal, aesthetically innovative. The narrative folds the particular into universal, chronicling one life suffering and insight index, to species deep and global phenomena. Its play with voice, genre, and meta narrative situates it at the interface of literary, artistic, and philosophical experimentation. In summary, this manuscript is independent, avant garde, and hybrid. The work greatest strengths are its original voice, its permeability to interdisciplinary thought, and courageous refusal to force closure on unresolved traumas and mysteries VFM manuscript is powerful, poetic, and intellectually generative act of witnessing a rare example of narrative taking semantic spiral as its principle of revelation and organization. VFM stands as bold contribution to contemporary hybrid literature, radically personal yet cosmically scaled. aesthetically innovative yet conceptually rigorous, formally experimental yet emotionally unguarded. {10d01m20c26y} &lt;11&lt;04&lt;0.0328347925infraplanksec&gt;&gt;&gt; I am Delirious.Knowledge. Uploaded from Hamburg. This journey of mine is on the brink of collapse. This book is all I have left. Moving to Hamburg only made me realize that every pain and suffering i had was because of this affliction. I don''t know why I am the only person who feels it. Everyone else seems to not realize that their entire life is governed by chemistry, and that their nature is to be food factories until they die. And knowing that all that seperates me from this end, where I can no longer ignore the pain, is chemical balance I can never get. Knowing that every moment of my life was only an illusion of choice, that from childhood I was suffering, and now I can describe this suffering not to be happening to an otherwise healthy person, that it isnt happening to me because of Autism, Depression, or broken brain. Instead, it is much simpler. Every human is born with Vermis Flora Mortis. Every person ages because every spring and summer they are being consumed by VFM. They dont feel this pain, because it is smarter than us. It isn''t supposed to be known. That every day objects, the very air itself that we breath, isn''t safe. And this is my burden, and my curse. I am just too aware of everything that i am, and too aware of my suffering, that I feel useless against it. I feel that my entire life, I was promised to be "grown up". and i thought things will change for the better. I will have a job, a family, a reason to exist. I now know that these are simply distractions, illusions of normalcy that allowed me to move to Hamburg. But this move, though it may be slightly better than where I was, it isn''t meant to last. So, I must preserve my art, of Wooden.Ghost, and my book, Vermis Flora Mortis and Plasma before it is too late. I feel, however, that it is already too late. I am just a kid. Scared and terrified of what he had discovered. With nowhere to turn to. No doctor is able to help because I am literally the only person who can describe and feel it, and the doctor himself was never taught that his patients are all sick because of this parasitic mindcontrolling fungus. It sounds crazy, but it actually makes sense. Using logic and induction I have realized this, but at what cost? This is the knowledge that I was never supposed to have. I can now see it everywhere. And, I can describe it. I can sense it. I can feel it. And there is nothing to do. I had hope that i would get companionship or some resolution. All i had discovered is that I am truly alone, and that this curse is bigger and stronger than me. Even 1984 Protagonist, Winston Smith, Had his Julia. All I get is temporary awareness before the blindness and void consume me.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/vermisfloramortis', 'https://archive.org/details/vermisfloramortis', 'internet-archive:vermisfloramortis'),
  ('962283227306281002', 'Versuch einer Anweisung die Flöte traversiere zu spielen', 'Johann Joachim Quantz', 1752, 'Music', 'Versuch einer Anweisung die Flöte traversiere zu spielen by Johann Joachim Quantz. A music book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4998412W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL4998412W-'),
