  ('689393223831181048', 'War in heaven', 'Charles Williams', 1930, 'Thriller', 'War in heaven by Charles Williams', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6718269-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL1155806W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL1155806W'),
  ('1063484174067912029', 'War Is A Racket', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study examines General Smedley Butler''s unprecedented confession that U.S. Marine Corps interventions he led across Central America, the Caribbean, and Asia (1898-1931) served corporate profits rather than national security. Butler, the most decorated Marine in American history, documented in his 1935 book War is a Racket how Marines mobilized through genuine patriotic belief actually protected United Fruit Company banana plantations, National City Bank loan collection, and Standard Oil operations while believing they served America. The paper analyzes specific interventions in Haiti, Nicaragua, Honduras, Mexico, and China, demonstrating how patriotism functions identically to religious belief in enabling information asymmetry—grassroots participants cannot be recruited by openly stating corporate objectives, but can be mobilized through appeals to national service and duty they genuinely believe. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/war-is-a-racket_202602', 'https://archive.org/details/war-is-a-racket_202602', 'internet-archive:war-is-a-racket_202602'),
  ('260748825745286196', 'War Storm', 'Victoria Aveyard', 2018, 'Young Adult', 'War Storm by Victoria Aveyard. A young adult book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19740494W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL19740494W-'),
  ('796963287130917442', 'War Storm', 'Victoria Aveyard', 2018, 'Young Adult', 'War Storm by Victoria Aveyard', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/8739000-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL19740494W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL19740494W'),
  ('1044276808764232927', 'Ward six and other stories [6 stories]', 'Антон Павлович Чехов', 1965, 'Literary Fiction', 'Ward six and other stories [6 stories] by Антон Павлович Чехов. A literary fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL10425749W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL10425749W-'),
  ('581274645252050795', 'Ward six and other stories [6 stories]', 'Антон Павлович Чехов', 1965, 'Literary Fiction', 'Ward six and other stories [6 stories] by Антон Павлович Чехов', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/12769790-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL10425749W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL10425749W'),
  ('4423376178298913', 'Warez: The Infrastructure and Aesthetics of Piracy', 'Martin Paul Eve', 2021, 'History', 'When most people think of piracy, they think of Bittorrent and The Pirate Bay. These public manifestations of piracy, though, conceal an elite worldwide, underground, organized network of pirate groups who specialize in obtaining media – music, videos, games, and software – before their official sale date and then racing against one another to release the material for free. Warez: The Infrastructure and Aesthetics of Piracy is the first scholarly research book about this underground subculture, which began life in the pre-internet era Bulletin Board Systems and moved to internet File Transfer Protocol servers (“topsites”) in the mid- to late-1990s. The “Scene,” as it is known, is highly illegal in almost every aspect of its operations. The term “Warez” itself refers to pirated media, a derivative of “software.” Taking a deep dive in the documentary evidence produced by the Scene itself, Warez describes the operations and infrastructures an underground culture with its own norms and rules of participation, its own forms of sociality, and its own artistic forms. Even though forms of digital piracy are often framed within ideological terms of equal access to knowledge and culture, Eve uncovers in the Warez Scene a culture of competitive ranking and one-upmanship that is at odds with the often communalist interpretations of piracy. Broad in scope and novel in its approach, Warez is indispensible reading for anyone interested in recent developments in digital culture, access to knowledge and culture, and the infrastructures that support our digital age.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/b904a8eb-9c98-4bb1-bf25-3cb9d075b157', 'https://archive.org/details/b904a8eb-9c98-4bb1-bf25-3cb9d075b157', 'internet-archive:b904a8eb-9c98-4bb1-bf25-3cb9d075b157'),
  ('486982438209416477', 'Warner Bros. Discovery 2024 Annual Report & Proxy Statement', 'Warner Bros. Discovery Inc.', 2025, 'History', 'The 2024 annual report & Form 10-K, and Chairman''s message to stockholders for Warner Bros. Discovery, Inc. (Ticker: WBD). The corporation founded on April 8, 2022 is an American multinational, mass media and entertainment conglomerate headquartered in New York City. Predecessor companies include WarnerMedia and Discovery, Inc. Business units at the time of founding include Warner Bros. Film & Television, DC Entertainment, Home Box Office (HBO), and U.S. Networks (Discovery, Scripps, Turner Broadcasting, Warner, CNN). The company became publicly traded on April 8th, 2022 following a spin-off from former parent company AT&T and merger with Discovery.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/warner-bros.-discovery-inc.-wbd-proxy-statement-2025-06-03', 'https://archive.org/details/warner-bros.-discovery-inc.-wbd-proxy-statement-2025-06-03', 'internet-archive:warner-bros.-discovery-inc.-wbd-proxy-statement-2025-06-03'),
