  ('647246611103523689', 'WE WILL CONTROL HIM, The 134 Year Pattern Of Elite Miscalculation About Military Strongmen', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This study compares two cases of elite miscalculation about controlling military strongmen: Sieyès''s recruitment of Napoleon Bonaparte during the coup of 18 Brumaire (1799) and Franz von Papen''s appointment of Adolf Hitler as Chancellor (1933). It analyzes how property-owning elites in both cases designed elaborate constraint mechanisms—constitutional frameworks, cabinet control, financial leverage—that proved worthless once strongmen commanded loyal forces and popular support, with both consolidating absolute power far faster than elites anticipated. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/we-will-control-him-the-134-year-pattern-of-elite-miscalculation-about-military-strongmen', 'https://archive.org/details/we-will-control-him-the-134-year-pattern-of-elite-miscalculation-about-military-strongmen', 'internet-archive:we-will-control-him-the-134-year-pattern-of-elite-miscalculation-about-military-strongmen'),
  ('225358951538778436', 'We: a 1972 science-fiction story by Yevgeny Zamyatin', 'Herbert Booker', 2017, 'Science', 'Zamyatin Yevgeny wrote a science-fiction novel with the simple titles of "We," in Russia in 1972. Russian authors have produced really fine stories, especially in science-fiction!', 'https://archive.org/services/img/WeByYevgenyZamyatinv1972', 'https://archive.org/details/WeByYevgenyZamyatinv1972', 'internet-archive:WeByYevgenyZamyatinv1972'),
