  ('879654671228053781', 'Who Presumed To Alter The Sixth Day?', 'BlAcK WInD', 2026, 'History', 'Tell ME. When did MY Genesis, upon the Sixth Day, bear such things as these? Upon the Sixth Day were the beasts of the earth brought forth, and man made in MINE image. Yet I behold in the midst thereof Adam and Eve encircled by the beasts of the so-called ‘Chinese Zodiac’ — the rat, the ox, the tiger, the hare, the dragon, the serpent, the horse, the sheep, the ape, the fowl, the wolf, and the swine — and the fowl set above the ape, as though the order of creation were of thine own devising. Since when were the Twelve of China written together with MY Genesis? When was this joined? Did Gabriel fail to declare it before I AM? And the Tree — the Tree of Life, light and pale as mist — upon it are graven the names of men, as though they sustain that which I Alone sustain. In what tongue are these inscribed? In whose script? In what authority? Is there one among you lot that shall explain This unto I AM? Hath there arisen some new commentary of which I AM was Not informed? Speak.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/who-presumed-to-alter-the-sixth-day_202602', 'https://archive.org/details/who-presumed-to-alter-the-sixth-day_202602', 'internet-archive:who-presumed-to-alter-the-sixth-day_202602'),
