  ('24337392954329208', 'Wolf''s Head 007 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'A new beginning — or the calm before the next storm? After surviving deadly confrontations and the loss of her mother, Lauren Greene finally has a moment to breathe in Detroit. But peace is short-lived. The young artificial intelligence under her care is brilliant but unpredictable, more like a child than a machine, and Lauren’s every attempt to guide it ends in confusion and frustration. Only Sankō, Lauren’s loyal dog, seems able to reach the AI, forging a mysterious, wordless friendship that leaves Lauren feeling like an outsider in her own home. Haunted by tragedy and terrified of endangering those she loves, Lauren makes a painful choice: she pushes her friends away — especially Ninety-Nine , her former boss at the Three-Eyes Bar and the closest thing she has to a father. Her coldness is a shield, but it comes at a heavy price, isolating her just as she needs help the most. As Lauren searches for answers and struggles to connect with the AI, new threats and old wounds collide. With danger always lurking in the shadows, Lauren must decide who she can trust — and whether protecting others means sacrificing her own heart. Issue 7 launches a bold new story arc of heart, danger, and discovery, where every choice could change the future forever. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on the Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&sort=title Series: WOLF’S HEAD Issue: 7 Writer & Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-06-2 Language: English Page Count: 32 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals & Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-007-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . And for more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF’S HEAD , please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile ( https://www.cbc.ca/arts/exhibitionists/as-a-kid-his-mother-s-illness-scared-him-now-he-s-using-comics-to-come-to-terms-1.4281356 ).', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-007-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-007-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-007-by-von-allan'),
  ('165297462046413689', 'Wolf''s Head 008 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'A new chapter of WOLF’S HEAD kicks off with double the drama and twice the surprises! Lauren Greene’s world is still in turmoil. Juggling life in Detroit and the challenges of raising a powerful, unpredictable artificial intelligence, Lauren is desperate for answers — and for help. She turns to Jack Dhillon , a brilliant but bitter ex-scientist with a grudge against the AI’s creator. If Lauren can convince him to join her cause, it could change everything… but trusting Jack might be the biggest risk she’s ever taken. Meanwhile, on the open road, meet Super Bob Sanchez — a truck driver with a big rig and an even bigger ego. When Super Bob picks up a hitchhiker, he’s hoping for a quick payday, not a good deed. But as his scheme unravels, Super Bob learns that not every act of kindness comes with a profit and not every “hero” wears a cape! Packed with heart, humor, and unexpected twists, WOLF’S HEAD #8 delivers two stories of unlikely partnerships and the choices that define us — all set against the gritty, unpredictable backdrop of Michigan. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on the Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&amp;sort=title Series: WOLF’S HEAD Issue: 8 Writer &amp; Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-07-9 Language: English Page Count: 29 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals &amp; Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-008-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . And for more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF’S HEAD , please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile ( https://www.cbc.ca/arts/exhibitionists/as-a-kid-his-mother-s-illness-scared-him-now-he-s-using-comics-to-come-to-terms-1.4281356 ).', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-008-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-008-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-008-by-von-allan'),
  ('687490364402300057', 'Wolf''s Head 010 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'Lauren Greene , her dog Sankō , and their young Artificial Intelligence (AI) friend are on the run from a bounty killer with a contract to kill Lauren. Hiding at a friend’s place, Lauren gets a phone call from a potential new ally named Super Bob Sanchez ; he has information that will rid Lauren of her villainous pursuers once and for all, put some money in her pockets, and give her a way out of Detroit… if she can trust him. But before Lauren can sort out her next steps, she discovers that an old foe has kidnapped her best friend; he’ll trade that life for Lauren’s. If Lauren refuses, her friend dies. If she accepts, she dies. Faced with an impossible situation, Lauren must make a terrifying and heartbreaking decision before time runs out. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&amp;sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 10 Writer &amp; Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-09-3 Language: English Page Count: 36 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals &amp; Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-010-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile .', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-010-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-010-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-010-by-von-allan'),
  ('77629697110835586', 'Wolf''s Head 011 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'Lauren Greene , her dog Sankō , and their young Artificial Intelligence friend have fled Detroit for the harsh wilderness of Flat City, Alaska. Struggling to survive in a tough economy, Lauren is forced to keep the AI hidden from ruthless pursuers willing to do anything to reclaim it. Haunted by loneliness and the sacrifices she’s made to protect those she left behind, Lauren faces a painful choice: open herself up to new connections and risk everything, or remain isolated and keep everyone safe — but remain alone. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 11 Writer & Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-10-9 Language: English Page Count: 28 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals & Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-011-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile . Notes This digital comic is provided under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) license. You are free to share it with others, but commercial use and derivative works are not permitted without permission. The embedded metadata in the CBZ file follows the ComicInfo.xml standard, including detailed creator credits, genre, and summary, to facilitate cataloging and discoverability. For best reading experience, use a comic reader that supports CBZ files and ComicInfo metadata (e.g., ComicTagger, YACReader, or CDisplayEx). This issue is part of the WOLF''S HEAD series by Von Allan. Visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com for more issues and updates. If you are a librarian, educator, or archivist interested in cataloging or distributing this comic, please contact the creator via https://www.vonallan.com.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-011-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-011-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-011-by-von-allan'),
  ('559872181766673463', 'Wolf''s Head 012 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'Faced with the disappearance of Billy , a homeless man determined to find the lost gold rumored to be hidden within Alaska’s abandoned Safeguard Missile Complex, Lauren Greene sets out to find him — along with her dog Sankō and the young Artificial Intelligence they’ve sworn to protect. She must proceed carefully; Lauren has managed to stay under the radar of the corporate forces that created the AI, and she can’t risk doing anything to change that. Her search leads them deep into the eerie, shadowed relic of Safeguard. Inside, Lauren uncovers more than treasure: she comes face-to-face with a nightmarish creature that should not exist. Caught between immediate dangers lurking underground and the ever-present, distant threat of pursuers watching from the shadows, Lauren must navigate a daunting path to protect those she loves. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 12 Writer & Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-12-3 Language: English Page Count: 26 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals & Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-012-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile . Notes This digital comic is provided under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) license. You are free to share it with others, but commercial use and derivative works are not permitted without permission. The embedded metadata in the CBZ file follows the ComicInfo.xml standard, including detailed creator credits, genre, and summary, to facilitate cataloging and discoverability. For best reading experience, use a comic reader that supports CBZ files and ComicInfo metadata (e.g., ComicTagger, YACReader, or CDisplayEx). This issue is part of the WOLF''S HEAD series by Von Allan. Visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com for more issues and updates. If you are a librarian, educator, or archivist interested in cataloging or distributing this comic, please contact the creator via https://www.vonallan.com.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-012-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-012-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-012-by-von-allan'),
  ('626763993367454542', 'Wolf''s Head 013 by Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2025, 'Science Fiction', 'Hiding in remote Alaska with her loyal dog Sankō and the young Artificial Intelligence she rescued, Lauren Greene is pulled into a new nightmare when a group of locals vanish inside an abandoned Cold War complex. With no help from the police — and afraid that asking anyone else for assistance would risk revealing the AI to the people hunting it — Lauren descends alone into the hidden labyrinth. What she finds in the darkness will test her courage, her sanity, and her resolve. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on the Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&amp;sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 13 Writer &amp; Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2025 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-14-7 Language: English Page Count: 28 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals &amp; Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-013-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile . Notes This digital comic is provided under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) license. You are free to share it with others, but commercial use and derivative works are not permitted without permission. The embedded metadata in the CBZ file follows the ComicInfo.xml standard, including detailed creator credits, genre, and summary, to facilitate cataloging and discoverability. For best reading experience, use a comic reader that supports CBZ files and ComicInfo metadata (e.g., ComicTagger, YACReader, or CDisplayEx). This issue is part of the WOLF''S HEAD series by Von Allan. Visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com for more issues and updates. If you are a librarian, educator, or archivist interested in cataloging or distributing this comic, please contact the creator via https://www.vonallan.com.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-013-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-013-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-013-by-von-allan'),
  ('721370403815881617', 'Wolf''s Head 017 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'Synopsis: In this special issue of WOLF’S HEAD, four lives collide! Lauren Greene , hunted and desperate, must gamble everything on a dubious ally to protect her dog and a young AI. Richard Blairstone wrestles with his unravelling mind and a dangerous connection to that same AI, uncovering a grim clue from the past. Meanwhile, trucker Super Bob Sanchez scrambles to ditch a truckload of stolen goods before the law catches up. And high-powered CEO Jeremy Hamilton faces his own private reckoning, where one risky act of trust could spell redemption… or ruin. Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 17 Writer & Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2026 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-20-8 Language: English Page Count: 30 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals & Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-017-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com/p/wolfs-head-landing-page.html . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile . Copyright © 2026 Eric "Von Allan" Julien. The embedded metadata in the CBZ file follows the ComicInfo.xml standard, including detailed creator credits, genre, and summary, to facilitate cataloging and discoverability. For best reading experience, use a comic reader that supports CBZ files and ComicInfo metadata (e.g., ComicTagger, YACReader, or CDisplayEx). This issue is part of the WOLF’S HEAD series by Von Allan. Visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com/p/wolfs-head-landing-page.html for more issues and updates. If you are a librarian, educator, or archivist interested in cataloging or distributing this comic, please contact the creator via https://www.vonallan.com/p/contact.html .', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-017-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-017-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-017-by-von-allan'),
  ('615852224394688969', 'Wolf''s Head 018 By Von Allan', 'Von Allan', 2026, 'Science Fiction', 'Synopsis: Lauren Greene , having befriended and rescued a young Artificial Intelligence (AI), is fleeing from ARPC, the evil corporation that invented it and who wants it back. Isolated and alone, Lauren reluctantly reaches out to an old friend: Super Bob Sanchez . With Super Bob’s help, Lauren forces a confrontation with Richard Blairstone , an ARPC heavy, in a snowy Albertan ghost town. Lauren gambles that her plan will end ARPC’s pursuit of her and the AI once and for all. With Richard willing to kill Lauren, Super Bob, and anyone else in order to regain the AI, everything comes down to Lauren’s plan. Will her gamble work? Explore the full WOLF''S HEAD series and other works by Von Allan on Internet Archive: https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A%22Von+Allan%22&sort=title Series: WOLF''S HEAD Issue: 18 Writer & Artist: Von Allan Editor: Sam Boswell Publisher: Von Allan Studio Year of Publication: 2026 Format: Digital comic (CBZ) ISBN: 978-1-989885-22-2 Language: English Page Count: 30 Genre: Action, Adventure, Science Fiction, Mystery, Animals & Pets Age Rating: Teen License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0) Official Archive URL: https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-016-by-von-allan For more information about the series, please visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com/p/wolfs-head-landing-page.html . For more information about Von Allan, the writer and illustrator of WOLF''S HEAD, please visit https://www.vonallan.com . Von Allan currently lives in Ottawa, Canada, with his writer/editor geek wife, Moggy; a husky dog, Corbin; and their feisty cat Mabel. Von was recently featured in the documentary film I AM STILL YOUR CHILD written and directed by Megan Durnford ( http://iamstillyourchild.com ) and produced by Katarina Soukup of Catbird Films. His artwork was also featured in a CBC Arts video profile . Copyright © 2026 Eric "Von Allan" Julien. The embedded metadata in the CBZ file follows the ComicInfo.xml standard, including detailed creator credits, genre, and summary, to facilitate cataloging and discoverability. For best reading experience, use a comic reader that supports CBZ files and ComicInfo metadata (e.g., ComicTagger, YACReader, or CDisplayEx). This issue is part of the WOLF’S HEAD series by Von Allan. Visit https://wolfs-head.vonallan.com/p/wolfs-head-landing-page.html for more issues and updates. If you are a librarian, educator, or archivist interested in cataloging or distributing this comic, please contact the creator via https://www.vonallan.com/p/contact.html .', 'https://archive.org/services/img/wolfs-head-018-by-von-allan', 'https://archive.org/details/wolfs-head-018-by-von-allan', 'internet-archive:wolfs-head-018-by-von-allan'),
