  ('702688935176411613', 'X FENO ASSEMBLY PLATFORM MODIFIED 3 D PRINTER', 'Carlos Omeñaca Prado', 2026, 'Science', 'This document discloses the complete design, assembly procedure, and operating protocol of the X-FENO Assembly Platform , a low-cost, open, and reproducible system for deterministic stacking of two-dimensional (2D) materials such as graphene and hBN. The platform is built by modifying a standard Cartesian desktop 3D printer, replacing the extrusion toolhead with a rigid scientific tool stack integrating: (i) piezoelectric XYZ micro-positioning, (ii) a motorized rotation stage for twist-angle control, (iii) PDMS/PPC-based pick-up and transfer tooling, and (iv) a heated, vacuum-assisted substrate stage. All mechanical parts, electronics, materials, dimensions, and step-by-step procedures are explicitly specified to enable independent replication without proprietary components. A troubleshooting table of common failure modes and alignment errors is included, along with optional extensions for automation and software control. Target total cost for a complete build is approximately €350–900 , corresponding to an ~90–95% reduction relative to commercial graphene transfer/stacking systems, while preserving full functional capability for research and educational use.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/x-feno-assembly-platform-modified-3-d-printer', 'https://archive.org/details/x-feno-assembly-platform-modified-3-d-printer', 'internet-archive:x-feno-assembly-platform-modified-3-d-printer'),
  ('365045073841313614', 'X-Men', 'Warren Ellis, Tom DeFalco, Howard Mackie', 2005, 'Graphic Novel', 'X-Men by Warren Ellis, Tom DeFalco, Howard Mackie. A graphic novel book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL2888297W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL2888297W-'),
