  ('661940469430530466', 'Xenocide', 'Orson Scott Card', 1991, 'Science Fiction', 'Xenocide by Orson Scott Card. A science fiction book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL49604W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL49604W-'),
  ('335639764900699763', 'Xenocide', 'Orson Scott Card', 1991, 'Science Fiction', 'Xenocide by Orson Scott Card', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10564838-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL49604W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL49604W'),
  ('1086353576179236461', 'XENOSYSTEMS FRAGMENTS', 'Nick Land', 2023, 'History', 'Xenosystems Fragments is a blog by Nick Land that explores various topics related to technology, philosophy, and politics. Land is known for his controversial views on these subjects, which often challenge traditional norms and values. In his blog, he presents a nihilistic worldview that rejects traditional morality and embraces the power of technology and capitalism. Land argues that the rise of technology and capitalism has led to a new era of human history, in which traditional values and institutions are being eroded. He believes that this process is unstoppable and that we must embrace it if we want to survive and thrive in the future. Land''s ideas are often criticized for being too extreme and nihilistic, but they have also attracted a loyal following of fans who appreciate his bold and unapologetic style. In conclusion, Nick Land''s Xenosystems Fragments is a thought-provoking blog that challenges conventional wisdom and presents a unique and controversial perspective on technology, philosophy, and politics. While his ideas may not be for everyone, they have certainly contributed to the ongoing debate about the role of technology and capitalism in shaping our future.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/xenosystems-fragments', 'https://archive.org/details/xenosystems-fragments', 'internet-archive:xenosystems-fragments'),
  ('385911019273679795', 'Xerxes', 'Jacob Abbott', 1850, 'Biography', 'Xerxes by Jacob Abbott. A biography book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4242218W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL4242218W-'),
  ('305181093883449027', 'Xerxes', 'Jacob Abbott', 1850, 'Biography', 'Xerxes by Jacob Abbott', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/5595425-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL4242218W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL4242218W'),
  ('918268731987264060', 'Xi Jinping The Governance Of China Volume 1', 'Xi Jinping', 2014, 'Science', 'The first published work by a sitting Chinese President, Xi Jinping: The Governance of China offers a unique look inside the Communist Party of China and its vision for the future. The book presents excerpts and summaries of 79 speeches, talks, interviews, instructions and correspondences in 18 chapters. Each item is accompanied by relevant notes about China''s social system, history and culture. The book includes 45 photos taken at various stages of Xi''s life, which provide readers with more information about his career and personal life. Topics include: The Chinese Dream Economic Development The Rule of Law Ecological Progress National Defense "One Country, Two Systems" New Model of Major-Country Relations Combating Corruption The CPC Leadership Under the leadership of Xi Jinping, the Communist Party of China has set off in a new direction of reform and modernization. The Governance of China will contribute greatly to the concepts and principles of governance within the CPC leadership, China''s future path of development, and the nations domestic and foreign policies as well as responses to international concerns about China. It is essential reading for anyone interested in knowing how China, and more specifically, how its President views the world and China''s place within it.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/xijinpingthegovernanceofchinavolume1', 'https://archive.org/details/xijinpingthegovernanceofchinavolume1', 'internet-archive:xijinpingthegovernanceofchinavolume1'),
