  ('553173393743633793', 'YUM! Brands 2024 Annual Report', 'YUM! Brands', 2025, 'History', 'The 2024 annual report & Form 10-K, Proxy Statement and Chairman''s message to stockholders for Yum! Brands (Ticker: YUM). The corporation, founded in 1997 as a spin-off from PepsciCo, is an American fast food company headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky. The company operates brands worldwide including: KFC, Pizza Hut, Taco Bell and WingStreet. YUM! previously owned/operated the A&W Restaurants and Long John Silvers.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/yum-brands-yum-annual-report-2024', 'https://archive.org/details/yum-brands-yum-annual-report-2024', 'internet-archive:yum-brands-yum-annual-report-2024'),
  ('453678558790632269', 'YUM! China 2024 Annual Report', 'YUM! China', 2025, 'History', 'The 2024 annual report & Form 10-K, Proxy Statement and Chairman''s message to stockholders for Yum! China (Ticker: YUMC). The corporation founded in 2016 is a Chinese fast food company incorporated in the United States but with operational headquartered in Shanghai, China. The company is a trademark licensee of YUM! Brands and operates brands including: KFC, Pizza Hut, Taco Bell and WingStreet. YUM! China was spun off from YUM! Brands on November 1, 2016.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/yum-china-yumc-annual-report-2024', 'https://archive.org/details/yum-china-yumc-annual-report-2024', 'internet-archive:yum-china-yumc-annual-report-2024'),
