  ('529060508653155611', 'ZAKIR NAIK VS MODERN SCIENCE', 'Gourav YADAV', 2025, 'Science', 'ZAKIR NAIK is an Islamic preacher who is known for scientific explanations of Quran and comparative religion studies, works mainly to convert people into fold of islam and spread of Islam. Why Zakir Naik is controversial ? Individuals and incidents linked to inspiration from Naik''s content include: · 2016 Dhaka cafe attackers: Investigations into the Holey Artisan cafe attack in Dhaka, Bangladesh, revealed that one of the five terrorists followed Naik''s Facebook page and was influenced by his speeches. The Bangladeshi government subsequently banned Peace TV, Naik''s channel. · IS-inspired group in Maharashtra: India''s Anti-Terrorism Squad (ATS) filed a charge sheet stating that members of an "IS-inspired" terror group arrested in January 2019 were inspired by Naik''s speeches. This group allegedly planned a mass poisoning attack at the Shree Mumbreshwar Temple in Mumbra. · 2022 Mangalore auto rickshaw bomber: The Karnataka police reportedly recovered Zakir Naik''s videos from the mobile device of Mohammad Sadiq, the individual involved in a low-intensity bomb explosion in a moving auto-rickshaw in Mangalore. · Najibullah Zazi: The Afghan-American involved in a 2009 Al-Qaeda plot targeting the New York City subway was an "admirer" of Naik''s sermons. · Kerala youth joining ISIS: Indian authorities have accused Naik of influencing young people in Kerala to join the Islamic State (ISIS). · Mumbai terror attacks perpetrators: A British High Court found that Naik''s speeches were among the material shared by the perpetrators of the 2008 Mumbai terror attacks. Key "dangerous" or controversial statements attributed to him include: · On Terrorism and Osama Bin Laden: He has been widely criticized for comments where he stated that "every Muslim should be a terrorist" in the sense of "terrorizing the terrorist" or anti-social elements. He also stated that if Osama bin Laden was "fighting the enemies of Islam," he was "for him," and if he was "terrorizing America, the biggest terrorist," he was "with him". He has also promoted the conspiracy theory that the 9/11 attacks were an "inside job" orchestrated by the U.S. government. · On Women''s Rights: Naik has made several comments widely condemned as misogynistic. o He suggested that "revealing Western dress" makes women more susceptible to rape, effectively blaming the victim for sexual assault. o He claimed that an unmarried woman has no respectability in society and her only choice is to marry, even if it means becoming a "bazaari aurat" (public woman). o He has also suggested girls shouldn''t be sent to schools where they might lose their virginity and has defended the practice of wife-beating. · On Other Religions: He promotes the supremacy of Islam and has argued that non-Muslims should not be allowed to have places of worship or propagate their faith in an Islamic state because their religions are "wrong". · On Apostasy and Homosexuality: He has called for the death penalty for Muslims who convert from Islam and then propagate their new faith against Islam. He has also recommended the death penalty for individuals engaging in homosexual acts. · Inspiration for Terrorists: He has faced intense scrutiny after reports emerged that some of the perpetrators of the 2016 Dhaka cafe attack and a convicted al-Qaeda member, Najibullah Zazi, were admirers of his sermons. My reasons to contradict his literary work “Quran and modern science” Science is the hope of 21 st century. It is the success of human civilisation. One should not associate it with delusions and false knowledge, as it can be misleading. WHAT INSPIRED ME ? Mob burning of Dipu Chandra Das in Bangladesh in the name of religious blasphemy. Desire to de-radicalize and make youth more conscious of reality, who is inspired by Zakir Naik radically. Indian Constitution, through Article 25 and related principles, allows for critical analysis of religion INTENTIONS – Not to hurt people of muslim community but, to give radical people a reality check of religion. WE ARE HUMANS. RELIGION IS AND WAS FOR HUMAN , NOT HUMAN FOR RELIGION.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/zakir-naik-vs-science', 'https://archive.org/details/zakir-naik-vs-science', 'internet-archive:zakir-naik-vs-science'),
