  ('455595666342956667', 'Zikar E Khair Saheefa E Mahboob ,, ذکر خیر صحیفۂ محبوب', 'khawaja mahboob alam,', 2026, 'Biography', 'Zikar E Khair Saheefa E Mahboob ,, ذکر خیر صحیفۂ محبوب', 'https://archive.org/services/img/zikar-e-khair-saheefa-e-mahboob', 'https://archive.org/details/zikar-e-khair-saheefa-e-mahboob', 'internet-archive:zikar-e-khair-saheefa-e-mahboob'),
  ('1065761902702800938', 'Zikr E Pakaan , تجلیات ناصریہ المعروف ذکر پاکان،', 'محمد طفیل ناصری قریشی نقشبندی مجددی چشتی صابری,Muhammad Tufail chishti', 2026, 'Biography', 'اَلَاۤ اِنَّ اَوْلِیَآءَ اللّٰهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَیْهِمْ وَ لَا هُمْ یَحْزَنُوْنَﭕ(62) الَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ كَانُوْا یَتَّقُوْنَﭤ(63)', 'https://archive.org/services/img/zikr-e-pakaan', 'https://archive.org/details/zikr-e-pakaan', 'internet-archive:zikr-e-pakaan'),
  ('161172804237809281', 'Zimbabwe, From Great Zimbabwe To The Hundred Trillion Dollar Note', 'Thomas J. Bryan, Claude/Anthropic', 2026, 'History', 'This case study examines elite control mechanisms in Zimbabwe from pre-colonial Great Zimbabwe civilization through the present crisis (pre-900 CE–2024), analyzing how Cecil Rhodes''s British South Africa Company used the fraudulent Rudd Concession (1888) to initiate corporate colonialism that systematically seized 51% of the country''s best agricultural land for a white settler minority comprising under 5% of the population. It demonstrates how the Land Apportionment Act (1930) crystallized this theft into legal architecture, how the liberation war (Second Chimurenga, 1964–1979) fought explicitly for land was compromised at Lancaster House, and how Robert Mugabe''s government reproduced colonial extraction logic through the Gukurahundi genocide (20,000 Ndebele civilians killed, 1983–1987) and catastrophic Fast Track Land Reform that precipitated world-record hyperinflation of 89.7 sextillion percent (2008). The study traces an unbroken causal chain from the Pioneer Column''s initial 600,000-acre land grant (1890) to contemporary platinum miners at Ngezi earning $400 monthly while producing metal valued at $900 per ounce, using a sustained comparison with Botswana to demonstrate how divergent colonial relationships produced radically different outcomes from similar starting conditions. This case study is part of the larger collection Patterns of Power: Systematic Analysis of Elite Control Mechanisms Across Civilizations , which applies an 8-part analytical framework across maximum historical variation to examine how elite power operates.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/zimbabwe-from-great-zimbabwe-to-the-hundred-trillion-dollar-note', 'https://archive.org/details/zimbabwe-from-great-zimbabwe-to-the-hundred-trillion-dollar-note', 'internet-archive:zimbabwe-from-great-zimbabwe-to-the-hundred-trillion-dollar-note'),
  ('976933527998549858', 'Zin! Zin! Zin! a Violin', 'Lloyd Moss', 1995, 'Music', 'Zin! Zin! Zin! a Violin by Lloyd Moss. A music book.', null, 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL47349W', 'internet-archive:ol-_works_OL47349W-'),
  ('1029978792137436777', 'Zin! Zin! Zin! a Violin', 'Lloyd Moss', 1995, 'Music', 'Zin! Zin! Zin! a Violin by Lloyd Moss', 'https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1320425-L.jpg', 'https://openlibrary.org/works/OL47349W', 'internet-archive:ol-works-OL47349W'),
  ('1079068945924886376', 'Zine 1.1 Colonial Carrion Editions Cafardnaüm', 'Editions Cafardnaüm', 2026, 'History', 'Editions Cafardnaüm are back to share this month''s monomania... This time, it''s bone black. Made up of boiled, carbonated then crushed bones, bone black is used for its filtering, discoloring, whitening properties, its fertilizing qualities, and as a pigment.', 'https://archive.org/services/img/zine-1.1-colonial-carrion-editions-cafardnaum', 'https://archive.org/details/zine-1.1-colonial-carrion-editions-cafardnaum', 'internet-archive:zine-1.1-colonial-carrion-editions-cafardnaum'),
